"following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/0b658847906df8fbce8bf8e57c1f07b461658c7a","node_id":"C_kwDOP93DxNoAKDBiNjU4ODQ3OTA2ZGY4ZmJjZThiZjhlNTdjMWYwN2I0NjE2NThjN2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/70bd095b1ec87280dc42d4ccd294cd4d122d811e","sha":"70bd095b1ec87280dc42d4ccd294cd4d122d811e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/70bd095b1ec87280dc42d4ccd294cd4d122d811e"}],"sha":"0b658847906df8fbce8bf8e57c1f07b461658c7a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/0b658847906df8fbce8bf8e57c1f07b461658c7a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/220909633?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan","id":220909633,"login":"analisaperlengkapan","node_id":"U_kgDODSrQQQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/70bd095b1ec87280dc42d4ccd294cd4d122d811e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T02:38:35Z","email":"analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com","name":"analisaperlengkapan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T02:38:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci(deps): unblock Dependabot PRs (e2e registry flake, title gate, RUSTSEC-2026-0319) (#963)\n\nDependabot PRs were permanently red and could not merge. Three independent\ncauses, all fixed here.\n\n1. E2E docker builds died on registry flake (the real blocker).\n   Every e2e job resolves `mcr.microsoft.com/playwright:v1.60.0-jammy`, and\n   the failures are network-level, not code-level:\n     failed to do request: Head \"https://mcr.microsoft.com/v2/playwright/\n     manifests/v1.60.0-jammy\": read: connection reset by peer\n   and, in the perlengkapan job, `net/http: TLS handshake timeout`.\n   Both are single-attempt. `infra/scripts/docker-build-with-retry.sh` now\n   pre-pulls each `FROM` image (best-effort) and retries `docker build` up to\n   4 times with linear backoff, so one blip no longer fails a 10-minute job.\n   Applied to all four `docker build` sites in ci.yml.\n\n2. PR Title (Conventional Commits) could never pass for a bot.\n   Dependabot writes \"deps(deps): Bump <crate> from X to Y\"; the gate requires\n   `subjectPattern: ^[a-z0-9].+` and the subject always starts with a capital\n   \"Bump\". No repo-side change can fix that — the title is regenerated on\n   every rebase, and `commit-message.prefix` only sets type/scope, not the\n   subject. Exempted via `ignoreLabels: dependencies` rather than by loosening\n   the pattern, which would have disabled the rule for humans too. Added\n   `labeled`/`unlabeled` triggers so a label landing after the check still\n   re-evaluates it. Squash history is unaffected: \"deps(deps): Bump …\" is a\n   valid Conventional Commit, and maintenance.yml already checks every\n   dependabot.yml prefix against this gate''s type/scope lists.\n\n3. cargo-deny RUSTSEC-2026-0319 (advisory).\n   `tracing-subscriber-wasm` reached `anymap2` via `gloo 0.8` →\n   `gloo-worker 0.2`; unmaintained, no fixed version. Replaced with a ~90-line\n   `ConsoleMakeWriter` in `lib/ui/src/utils/console_writer.rs` over `web-sys`,\n   which both FEs already depend on via `gloo 0.12`. Drops a second, stale\n   `gloo` from every WASM bundle as a side effect.\n\nThe writer''s `flush` drains its buffer, so an event is emitted at most once\neven though `tracing_subscriber::fmt` may flush before `Drop` does; the sink\n(not the buffering) is cfg-gated to wasm, since `web_sys` is a panic-on-call\nstub on the host, where lib-ui is also built (`--features ssr`, clippy, doc\ntests). Four host-runnable tests cover it; removing the drain fails\n`an_event_is_emitted_at_most_once`.\n\nNote: neither the title gate nor cargo-deny is a required status check — only\n`CI Summary` blocks, and it was red because of the E2E jobs in (1).\n\nVerified: cargo fmt --all --check; cargo clippy -p lib-ui --all-targets\n--all-features -D warnings; cargo test -p lib-ui (44 lib + 20 doc); wasm32\ncheck for both MFEs; cargo-deny all ok; repo invariant guards green.\n\nCo-authored-by: openhands <openhands@all-hands.dev>","tree":{"sha":"e170d95a6d8ce08889bfdcb55c26fc48547c6312","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/trees/e170d95a6d8ce08889bfdcb55c26fc48547c6312"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/commits/70bd095b1ec87280dc42d4ccd294cd4d122d811e","verification":{"payload":"tree e170d95a6d8ce08889bfdcb55c26fc48547c6312\nparent 5b484f59df557608e37628d7bc46f3978e259254\nauthor analisaperlengkapan <analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com> 1791340715 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791340715 +0700\n\nci(deps): unblock Dependabot PRs (e2e registry flake, title gate, RUSTSEC-2026-0319) (#963)\n\nDependabot PRs were permanently red and could not merge. Three independent\ncauses, all fixed here.\n\n1. E2E docker builds died on registry flake (the real blocker).\n   Every e2e job resolves `mcr.microsoft.com/playwright:v1.60.0-jammy`, and\n   the failures are network-level, not code-level:\n     failed to do request: Head \"https://mcr.microsoft.com/v2/playwright/\n     manifests/v1.60.0-jammy\": read: connection reset by peer\n   and, in the perlengkapan job, `net/http: TLS handshake timeout`.\n   Both are single-attempt. `infra/scripts/docker-build-with-retry.sh` now\n   pre-pulls each `FROM` image (best-effort) and retries `docker build` up to\n   4 times with linear backoff, so one blip no longer fails a 10-minute job.\n   Applied to all four `docker build` sites in ci.yml.\n\n2. PR Title (Conventional Commits) could never pass for a bot.\n   Dependabot writes \"deps(deps): Bump <crate> from X to Y\"; the gate requires\n   `subjectPattern: ^[a-z0-9].+` and the subject always starts with a capital\n   \"Bump\". No repo-side change can fix that — the title is regenerated on\n   every rebase, and `commit-message.prefix` only sets type/scope, not the\n   subject. Exempted via `ignoreLabels: dependencies` rather than by loosening\n   the pattern, which would have disabled the rule for humans too. Added\n   `labeled`/`unlabeled` triggers so a label landing after the check still\n   re-evaluates it. Squash history is unaffected: \"deps(deps): Bump …\" is a\n   valid Conventional Commit, and maintenance.yml already checks every\n   dependabot.yml prefix against this gate''s type/scope lists.\n\n3. cargo-deny RUSTSEC-2026-0319 (advisory).\n   `tracing-subscriber-wasm` reached `anymap2` via `gloo 0.8` →\n   `gloo-worker 0.2`; unmaintained, no fixed version. Replaced with a ~90-line\n   `ConsoleMakeWriter` in `lib/ui/src/utils/console_writer.rs` over `web-sys`,\n   which both FEs already depend on via `gloo 0.12`. Drops a second, stale\n   `gloo` from every WASM bundle as a side effect.\n\nThe writer''s `flush` drains its buffer, so an event is emitted at most once\neven though `tracing_subscriber::fmt` may flush before `Drop` does; the sink\n(not the buffering) is cfg-gated to wasm, since `web_sys` is a panic-on-call\nstub on the host, where lib-ui is also built (`--features ssr`, clippy, doc\ntests). Four host-runnable tests cover it; removing the drain fails\n`an_event_is_emitted_at_most_once`.\n\nNote: neither the title gate nor cargo-deny is a required status check — only\n`CI Summary` blocks, and it was red because of the E2E jobs in (1).\n\nVerified: cargo fmt --all --check; cargo clippy -p lib-ui --all-targets\n--all-features -D warnings; cargo test -p lib-ui (44 lib + 20 doc); wasm32\ncheck for both MFEs; cargo-deny all ok; repo invariant guards green.\n\nCo-authored-by: openhands <openhands@all-hands.dev>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxbCrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAD60QAKgigpSI/zOWfaHdmURqn1Wx\nVw83NwuFYxMtwpB2ZLNCbQJhlzX9RBQnrSjfFhbpoizVwcpJx+7HYc5AyAqferhx\nQ5r9SLO979axYbLUSKMKCe+lURiIlcmmby4blDxMINp1uK9GOIPNatHggg958y4Z\n5K99jdehF8GGn0khex9QGpy+5dywYVrK2XnxUSMESbrfmZZzrMlyhEyULobgOA5O\nplu8VcDJLO1QdgiqNqwhPIJjVGklPBxgOezrw92T1Yj6evbLGuAALXadUuy+iRh1\n1ZxudgNmOVdNFxpXpNX3CvhWEbenT0mxxhaYLpP1OfOHwanfV+7XbRS2kuxtTYjM\n0oAPFbRqc9HxGX3d2nr0ZNy2MRLj/e4zPH0shG+PMPOp1wQ2prnDIyTyCqmKSwfA\nxLIr9dVv/sXElr9XzAjqGk1qATuFQngeVtSM6PusKu01eJr9HzvMRF331tYZrmj/\nlLiiEEjXD/++HjsZkGYECOmhtzgk9oLg83zFWVi7buG3RJDQKh1Jkh3OwoqEk8gg\njS7Qe9Y4vy3ERT3JD5JwGCDJlu5qlFPO/JeShKMcgn3Y8m5xvRSB7ueK5jcpKeH