ser_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/5ef1bbdc5a02b539fca1208a5d3fa1c6f72ffa2b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T08:09:15Z","email":"analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com","name":"analisaperlengkapan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T08:09:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(e2e): collect the orphaned Playwright spec, guard the class (#946)\n\n* test(e2e): collect the orphaned Playwright spec, guard the class\n\n`pemakaian-monitoring.spec.ts` — 8 assertions over the six per-role\nmonitoring read endpoints — was matched by NO Playwright project, so\n`npx playwright test` never collected it. A spec that never runs is\nindistinguishable from one that passes, and nothing noticed: TypeScript\nonly checks loaded files, `cargo` does not know the file, and\n`route-coverage.mjs` greps spec *text* for route strings rather than\nasking whether the spec is collected. Same failure shape as orphaned\nCargo `tests/` sub-dirs that `lint-orphan-tests` already guards.\n\n- wire it into a `perlengkapan-pemakaian-monitoring` project\n- add `check-playwright-projects-cover-specs.py`: derives specs from\n  disk, coverage from the projects'' `testMatch`, with a `--self-test`\n  that removes a project and asserts the guard goes red\n- wire that guard into the *Enforce Repo Invariants* job, and run the\n  newly collected project in `e2e-perlengkapan`\n- add `infra/scripts/run-e2e.sh`, the local harness mirroring the CI e2e\n  recipe (stack up/seed, perlengkapan + portal + cross-app runs,\n  integrasi proto copied into the portal e2e context). It lives beside\n  `secreton-ci-bootstrap.sh` rather than at the root: the Enforce\n  Structure guard whitelists root files, and the other e2e helpers\n  already live in `infra/scripts/`.\n\nVerified against the compose stack: perlengkapan 192/192 in 12 files\n(was 184), portal core+integration 32/32, cross-app SSO 3/3,\nroute-coverage 29/29 + 13/13, secreton Shamir init/unseal + dynamic DB\nlease, simpelv1 PHPUnit IntegrationLive 10/10, 8 invariant guards PASS.\n\nCo-authored-by: openhands <openhands@all-hands.dev>\n\n* fix(e2e): honour testIgnore in the spec-coverage guard, harden the harness\n\nAddress review findings on the orphaned-spec guard and the local e2e harness.\n\nGuard (check-playwright-projects-cover-specs.py):\n- Model testIgnore, not just testMatch. Playwright drops files matching a\n  testIgnore even when a project''s testMatch selects them, so a guard reading\n  only testMatch calls an ignored spec covered. Both the inherited top-level\n  and project-level scopes are honoured now.\n- Blank comments *and* string literals before parsing. A commented-out project\n  was read as live configuration, and the glob patterns are themselves strings,\n  so scanning raw text matched a testMatch inside a // note. Strings blank to a\n  NUL sentinel so whitespace-skipping cannot walk through a blanked literal and\n  miss a bare-string testMatch.\n- Six self-test canaries (was: one) covering each way a spec stops being\n  collected: removed testMatch, new orphan file, project testIgnore, inherited\n  testIgnore, commented-out project, commented-out testMatch.\n- --cross-check compares the static model against ''npx playwright test --list''\n  as a two-way equivalence, so the hand-maintained glob model cannot drift\n  silently. Skips cleanly where there is no Node toolchain (the invariants job),\n  so it can never be what makes the guard fail.\n\nHarness (run-e2e.sh):\n- Set disposable defaults for POSTGRES_PASSWORD and SIMPELV1_APP_KEY. Compose\n  interpolates them for every service in the merged files, including ones the\n  target never starts, so a fresh checkout with no .env failed before anything\n  ran. Explicitly supplied values still win.\n- ''up''/''up-cross'' now run build -> up -> wait -> seed instead of a bare\n  ''up -d''. The seed service carries profiles:[seed] so it never ran, leaving\n  the workflow specs'' non-empty assertions to fail on an empty database; and\n  ''up -d'' reused stale :local images after a source change, testing the\n  previous build.\n- Documented ''wait'' (the usage named a non-existent ''stack-wait'').\n\nVerified: guard self-test + real run + --list equivalence all green\n(perlengkapan 12/12, portal 4/4); compose config succeeds on a fresh clone and\nthe full up sequence builds and starts from it.\n\n* fix(e2e): model Playwright''s per-project collection, run the guard against --list\n\nFollow-up review findings on the spec-coverage guard and the local harness.\nEach was reproduced against the committed code before it was changed.\n\nGuard (check-playwright-projects-cover-specs.py):\n- Keep testMatch paired with its own effective testIgnore, per project. Pooling\n  every match pattern and every ignore pattern into two flat sets lost the\n  association in both directions. An unrelated project''s testIgnore cancelled a\n  valid match (false failure), and a project-level ''testIgnore: []'' could not\n  switch off the inherited top-level ignore (false pass). A spec is now covered\n  when SOME project matches it and that same project does not ignore it.\n- Read the top-level testIgnore from OUTSIDE the projects array. Searching the\n  whole file matched the first project that declares its own, which then became\n  every other project''s inherited ignore — found by self-test canary 8.\n- Mask the source in two passes instead of regexing literals out of the raw\n  span. A quoted pattern inside a comment (testMatch: [/* ''**/x.spec.ts'' */])\n  was read as a live pattern. Structure is now read from a comment+string mask\n  and patterns from a comment-only mask, which is the only way to get the\n  patterns (they are strings) without seeing structure inside comments.\n- Twelve self-test canaries (was: six), covering each way a spec stops being\n  collected, plus the two overlapping-project cases above.\n- Add --e2e-dir so the script can run where the config and node_modules already\n  are, and tolerate being piped in (__file__ is <stdin>).\n\nCI:\n- Run --cross-check in e2e-perlengkapan, against ''npx playwright test --list'',\n  piping the script in over stdin. The invariants job has no Node, so parser\n  drift could otherwise reach the merge gate unseen; the e2e image ships both\n  node and python3. stdin rather than a bind mount because under ARC dind a\n  bind mount resolves against the dind daemon''s filesystem, not the checkout.\n\nHarness (run-e2e.sh):\n- Read .env BEFORE applying defaults. Compose reads .env for interpolation only\n  when the shell does not define the variable, so the previous unconditional\n  export overrode a developer''s own credentials. Postgres does not reset the\n  role on an existing data dir, so an existing volume then rejected the new\n  password and ''up'' stopped at migrate. Precedence is now .env > default, with\n  an explicit export still winning.\n\nVerified end-to-end on a fresh clone with no .env: the harness brought the whole\nstack up (build -> up -> wait -> seed) and the suites passed against it —\nperlengkapan 192, portal-chromium+portal-core 27, portal-cross-app 3,\nroute-coverage 29/29 + 13/13. Guard self-test 12/12; --cross-check green inside\nthe real e2e image (12 files, model == --list).\n\n* fix(e2e): resolve .env through Compose, make the cross-check fail loudly\n\nSecond-round Devin findings. Each reproduced against the committed code first.\n\nrun-e2e.sh — inline comments broke local database credentials:\n- `POSTGRES_PASSWORD=localpw # local database` is `localpw` to Compose (an\n  unquoted '' #'' starts a comment) but `localpw # local database` to the sed\n  pass. Compose then initialised the role with the short value while the\n  harness handed the long one to migrate/seed, and every run failed with\n  ''password authentication failed'' — including immediately, against a volume\n  Compose had just initialised. Reproduced both ways on the seeded stack.\n- Resolve the value with Compose itself (`config --environment`) instead of\n  re-implementing .env syntax. Quoted ''#'' is kept, ''key#x'' is not a comment,\n  and precedence stays Compose''s: explicit export > .env > fallback. The\n  fallback is now exported only for keys .env does not mention, because\n  exporting it first made it win over .env (Compose gives the shell priority)\n  and silently ignored a developer''s own credentials.\n\ncheck-playwright-projects-cover-specs.py — a failed --list passed the check:\n- `--cross-check` skipped on missing node_modules, subprocess error,\n  malformed JSON and an empty listing, and never consulted the exit status;\n  main() only failed on an explicit False. So a `--list` that exits non-zero\n  and prints a diagnostic instead of JSON made the CI step green while\n  comparing nothing.\n- Add `--cross-check-strict`: non-zero exit, unparseable JSON, empty listing\n  and zero suites compared are all failures. CI uses it (the e2e image\n  guarantees the toolchain); plain `--cross-check` still skips, for callers\n  that have no Node. Two self-test canaries cover both directions.\n\n- Fix the docstring example path: antemuka -> antarmuka.\n\nVerified: self-test 14/14; strict cross-check green inside the e2e image and\nred on a failing/malformed/empty --list; all six .env precedence cases match\nCompose; harness brought a fresh stack up and the suite passed on it\n(191 passed, 1 flaky on a metrics-summary render).\n\n* chore(dev): preload the environment before an OpenHands session starts\n\nA fresh sandbox has Node and Docker but no Rust toolchain, no protoc, no\n`.env` and no Playwright browsers, so every session opens by rediscovering\nthat and installing it by hand. `.openhands/setup.sh` runs on session start\n(docs.openhands.dev, ''Repository Customization'') and does it once, up front.\n\nProvisions: Rust 1.97.1 + rustfmt/clippy + wasm32-unknown-unknown, protoc 25.1,\nnpm ci for both Playwright suites, the Chromium browser, and a disposable\n`.env` for compose. Versions mirror the repo''s own pins\n(`.github/actions/setup-rust`, `.github/actions/setup-node`, `Dockerfile.e2e`)\nso a local run and a CI run agree rather than drifting.\n\nDesign notes:\n- Idempotent and non-fatal. Every step checks first and reports ''already\n  present''; a failure (offline, rate limit, no sudo) warns and moves on, so\n  setup can never be why a session cannot start.\n- `~/.cargo/bin` and `~/.local/bin` are prepended to PATH at the top and\n  persisted to `.bashrc`. A non-interactive shell never reads `.bashrc`, so\n  without the unconditional PATH the presence checks cannot see a previous\n  run''s install and every session reinstalls.\n- `.env` is created only when absent. Overwriting it would make Compose\n  initialise Postgres with a different password than the existing volume was\n  created with, and every later command would fail authentication.\n- Opt-in extras stay off: `SIMPEL_SETUP_BUILD=1` builds images,\n  `SIMPEL_SETUP_STACK=1` also brings the stack up and seeds it.\n\n`.gitignore` changes `.openhands/` to `.openhands/*` so the one shared file\ncan be tracked. A directory-level ignore excludes the directory itself and git\nnever descends into it, so `!.openhands/setup.sh` under `.openhands/` is inert\n— verified with `git check-ignore`. Per-developer memory stays ignored.\n\nVerified: shellcheck clean at every severity; `bash -n` clean; idempotent\nacross three runs; `cargo check -p lib-core` and `--target\nwasm32-unknown-unknown` pass; `cargo check -p layanan-gateway` passes (proves\nprotoc); the generated `.env` satisfies `docker compose config`; and only\n`setup.sh` is staged out of `.openhands/`.\n\n* fix(dev): scope the .env umask to the write\n\n`umask 077` was set for the remainder of the script, so every file created\nafter the .env write would inherit it. Wrap the write in a subshell so the\numask applies only there. Verified the file lands 0600 and the shell''s umask\nis unchanged afterwards.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: openhands <openhands@all-hands.dev>","tree":{"sha":"5e1d1fadb21b31c9224865d9d0a968d78e9fbc73","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/trees/5e1d1fadb21b31c9224865d9d0a968d78e9fbc73"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/commits/5ef1bbdc5a02b539fca1208a5d3fa1c6f72ffa2b","verification":{"payload":"tree 5e1d1fadb21b31c9224865d9d0a968d78e9fbc73\nparent 9f8edfc443d55b1aa74903ed89e953328622c8e9\nauthor analisaperlengkapan <analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com> 1790755755 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790755755 +0700\n\ntest(e2e): collect the orphaned Playwright spec, guard the class (#946)\n\n* test(e2e): collect the orphaned Playwright spec, guard the class\n\n`pemakaian-monitoring.spec.ts` — 8 assertions over the six per-role\nmonitoring read endpoints — was matched by NO Playwright project, so\n`npx playwright test` never collected it. A spec that never runs is\nindistinguishable from one that passes, and nothing noticed: TypeScript\nonly checks loaded files, `cargo` does not know the file, and\n`route-coverage.mjs` greps spec *text* for route strings rather than\nasking whether the spec is collected. Same failure shape as orphaned\nCargo `tests/` sub-dirs that `lint-orphan-tests` already guards.\n\n- wire it into a `perlengkapan-pemakaian-monitoring` project\n- add `check-playwright-projects-cover-specs.py`: derives specs from\n  disk, coverage from the projects'' `testMatch`, with a `--self-test`\n  that removes a project and asserts the guard goes red\n- wire that guard into the *Enforce Repo Invariants* job, and run the\n  newly collected project in `e2e-perlengkapan`\n- add `infra/scripts/run-e2e.sh`, the local harness mirroring the CI e2e\n  recipe (stack up/seed, perlengkapan + portal + cross-app runs,\n  integrasi proto copied into the portal e2e context). It lives beside\n  `secreton-ci-bootstrap.sh` rather than at the roo