s.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/78830fdffa55346e76fa83ce4dca85897dc078b4","node_id":"C_kwDOP93DxNoAKDc4ODMwZmRmZmE1NTM0NmU3NmZhODNjZTRkY2E4NTg5N2RjMDc4YjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/f5aee5ac8e5cc33d819f71158aa7046ddebea98e","sha":"f5aee5ac8e5cc33d819f71158aa7046ddebea98e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/f5aee5ac8e5cc33d819f71158aa7046ddebea98e"}],"sha":"78830fdffa55346e76fa83ce4dca85897dc078b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/78830fdffa55346e76fa83ce4dca85897dc078b4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/220909633?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan","id":220909633,"login":"analisaperlengkapan","node_id":"U_kgDODSrQQQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/f5aee5ac8e5cc33d819f71158aa7046ddebea98e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T13:43:32Z","email":"analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com","name":"analisaperlengkapan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T13:43:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: make dependency checks hang-proof with retry + network/idle classification (#930)\n\n* ci: make dependency checks hang-proof with retry + network/idle classification\n\nDependency checks (`cargo audit`, `cargo deny`, `composer audit`) all fetch\nsomething over the network before they can check anything: the RustSec advisory\nDB (a git clone), the Packagist advisory DB, the tool release archive, or the\nPHP container image. A dropped connection therefore surfaced as a red\n\"dependency check\", indistinguishable from a real finding.\n\nThis adds `infra/scripts/retry-dependency-check.py`, a wrapper that retries\nnetwork failures with exponential backoff and a per-attempt timeout, then\nclassifies the outcome in three ways:\n\n  GREEN - tool ran, found nothing\n  RED   - tool ran and found something, or failed for a non-network reason\n          (bad config, missing tool, checksum mismatch)\n  HANG  - no response after every attempt; counted green per owner policy,\n          with an explicit note written to the step summary\n\nThe classification is deliberately narrow: a finding is matched BEFORE any\nnetwork pattern, so a finding can never be absorbed into a silent green. The\ngreen-on-outage decision is recorded in the step summary rather than applied\nquietly, because a check that never ran must not look identical to one that\npassed.\n\nChanged:\n- Add `infra/scripts/retry-dependency-check.py` (wrapper + 16-case self-test)\n- security.yml: wrap cargo-audit, composer-audit and cargo-deny; retry the\n  cargo-audit release download and the Verus release download\n- maintenance.yml: wrap cargo audit; retry the cargo-audit / cargo-outdated\n  install paths\n- ci.yml: run the wrapper''s self-test as a required guard\n\nTwo defects found while testing against the real tools rather than assuming:\n\n- The cargo-deny action runs as a container (`FROM rust:1.85-alpine`), so a\n  runner-side advisory-DB pre-seed would have written to a `$HOME` the tool\n  never reads - a safeguard that looks present but is never mounted. Replaced\n  with a checksum-pinned direct install (0.20.2, matching the action''s pin) so\n  the retry wrapper actually governs the advisory-DB clone. Running the binary\n  directly also needs the runner''s `cargo`, so `setup-rust` was added to that\n  job.\n\n- Testing against the real cargo-deny binary surfaced \"failed to fetch crates:\n  failed to run cargo\", a MISSING TOOLCHAIN, which an over-broad\n  `failed to fetch` pattern classified as network -> green. Narrowed, and both\n  cases are locked in as self-test regression cases.\n\nThe self-test proves it can go red, not just green: two injected regressions\n(inverted match order, broadened network pattern) were both caught.\n\nVerified: all three workflows parse; every embedded bash step passes `bash -n`;\n`check-ci-summary-scope`, `check-guard-imports-are-stdlib`,\n`check-actionlint-parity` and `check-pr-workflows-run-on-every-pr` pass.\n\nCo-authored-by: openhands <openhands@all-hands.dev>\n\n* feat(e2e): screenshot every frontend page and publish the gallery in the README\n\nAdds a screenshot sweep that photographs the whole application — both\nmicrofrontends, every route the routers actually declare — against a real\nrunning stack, and embeds the result in the README. The point is not the\nimages: it is that \"every page renders\" becomes a claim something can\nfalsify, instead of a sentence in a document nobody re-checks.\n\nRoute inventory is DERIVED from the routers (`screenshot-routes.py` walks\nthe nesting in both `routes.rs`, including the parameterised detail routes\nthat the curated `pub const` list omits). A hand-written list is correct on\nthe day it is written and silently wrong the next time a route lands, which\nis exactly the failure this is meant to catch.\n\nThree guards decide whether a shot may be published:\n\n  * `check.py` rejects blank/uniform images by pixel metrics. A gallery\n    asserts each listed page renders something; a flat PNG makes that false.\n  * `capture.mjs` flags 404s, a login page on an authenticated route, WASM\n    panics, raw wire enums, unlabelled UUIDs, raw UTC timestamps, and\n    horizontal overflow — each one a defect that actually shipped here.\n  * `gallery.py` refuses to write anything while a defect or an uncaptured\n    route remains, so the README cannot advertise a page that is broken.\n\nGuard shots (operator opening an admin route) are marked `expectDenied`:\nthe 403 card IS the assertion passing, so those signals are recorded as\n`expected` rather than defects — and a guarded route that renders normally\nbecomes a `GUARD-TIDAK-MENAHAN` defect, which is the half that matters.\n\nFixes found by the sweep and fixed here:\n  * audit log USER column showed the raw `user_id` UUID instead of the\n    actor''s username.\n  * `user_id` was duplicated into the audit detail JSON.\n  * WASM bundle download aborts are forgiven only when the retry-mounted\n    page demonstrably booted; a genuine boot failure still fails both\n    attempts and is still reported.\n\nVerified: 70/70 captured, 0 flagged, 70/70 pass the pixel check, all 70\nREADME links resolve, and the business-process suites pass against the same\nstack (86 workflow + 89 RBAC/guard/nav + 14 kebutuhan = 189 tests).\n\n* docs(agents): record the screenshot sweep and its three publication guards\n\nThe sweep is only worth having if the next person knows it exists and what\ngates it. Documents the derived route inventory (and why the curated\n`pub const` list is the wrong source), the three guards, and the\n`expectDenied` convention for guard shots.\n\n* ci: gate the README screenshot gallery against the routers\n\nThe gallery claims \"every page renders\". Nothing in the build read it, so a\nroute could land and the README would keep showing the previous set —\ncorrect on the day it was generated, quietly incomplete after the next\nrouter change. That is the same shape as the other hand-written lists this\nrepo has already been bitten by (the `-p` matrices, the `needs:` lists, the\nstatus vocabulary), so it gets the same treatment: derive the scope.\n\nBoth sides of the comparison are derived. The expected set comes from\n`screenshot-routes.py` — the very script the sweep consumes — so the gate\nand the sweep cannot disagree about what \"every route\" means. That script\nwalks the router nesting rather than the curated `pub const` list, which is\nwhat makes parameterised detail routes count at all.\n\nThe gate ships with a mutation self-test, because a gate that passes on a\nhealthy repo proves nothing: case two deletes one gallery entry and requires\nthe gate to name that route. The neighbouring guard learned this the hard\nway — check-crate-ci-coverage''s first version passed with its `run:` line\ndeleted, since the step NAME still contained the command.\n\nStdlib only (the ARC runner ships no PyYAML), and `--self-test` is wired\ninto the same job so the canary runs on every PR.\n\nVerified: all 65 routes covered; self-test green; the gate red when one\nentry is removed; and all 25 Python guards in the invariants job pass\nlocally.\n\n* ci: close two silent-green dependency probes in cargo-audit job\n\nThe 2026-09-24 run of `cargo-audit` went red on \"Tak ada ignore basi di\n.cargo/audit.toml\" with `gagal mem-parse laporan JSON cargo-audit:\nExpecting value: line 1 column 1 (char 0)`. The probe had hung ~7 minutes\nand handed the downstream guard 0 bytes. That is a network failure wearing\nthe costume of a real finding — the exact class the retry wrapper exists\nto absorb.\n\nTwo probes in the job bypassed the wrapper:\n\n1. \"Tak ada ignore basi\" ran `cargo audit --json` bare. `cargo audit`\n   fetches the RustSec advisory DB from GitHub first, so one dropped\n   connection yields empty stdout, which the downstream guard reports as\n   an unparseable report.\n\n2. \"Assert lockfile-only audit ignores still hold\" ran\n   `cargo tree -i \"$crate\" 2>/dev/null | grep` with no timeout and stderr\n   discarded. Every failure — network, panic, missing toolchain — printed\n   `ok: rkyv tetap di luar build graph`. It could not tell \"checked and\n   clean\" from \"could not check\", so it passed without checking. `-i` also\n   exits non-zero on the NORMAL case (crate absent), which is why its\n   failures were indistinguishable from a valid result.\n\nBoth now go through the wrapper. A new `--capture` mode handles probes\nwhose payload is stdout rather than an exit code, and it deliberately does\nNOT write the report file when the tool never answered — so the downstream\nguard skips with an honest `::notice::` instead of parsing an empty file\nand going red. The lockfile-only probe now greps a full `cargo tree` dump\n(exit 0 on success), so absence of the crate is meaningful.\n\nSelf-tests cover the capture mode''s three states: report written despite\nnon-zero exit (cargo audit exits non-zero precisely when it finds\nsomething), network failure = green with NO file, non-network failure =\nstill red.\n\nVerified against a simulated hang: step exits 0 with the notice, while a\nreal report still reaches the guard and stale ignores are still caught.\n\n* docs(screenshots): refresh gallery from a clean capture run\n\nRe-ran the full pipeline (capture -> check -> gallery) end to end against the\nlive stack to confirm the committed gallery reproduces from current code\nrather than having drifted.\n\n70 captures, 0 unresolved route parameters, 0 flagged. 21 PNGs differ from the\nprevious set by 0.01-0.28% of pixels — dynamic values only (session timestamps,\nrecord counts). The gallery''s own numbers move with them: the sessions page''s\nheight changed 1095 -> 1089 in README.\n\nThe capture step clears its output directory, so `image-report.json` and\n`GALLERY.md` must be regenerated afterwards; both are restored here.\n\n* ci: stop reading a clean dependency scan as a finding\n\n`composer-audit (simpelv1)` went red with the tool''s own output saying\n\"No security vulnerability advisories found.\" — no advisory existed. The\nfinding pattern `advisories? (found|detected)` matches that clean sentence\nverbatim, so the classifier reported a passing audit as a finding.\n\nThis is the mirror image of the bug the wrapper was written to fix. The\noriginal defect let a failure look like success; this one let success look\nlike a failure. Both destroy the signal, and a red that means nothing is a\nred people learn to ignore — which is how it also hides a real finding.\n\nClean negations are now neutralised before the finding patterns are\napplied. The scrub is per-line (`[^\\n]` bounded), because a blanket scrub\nwould let \"No vulnerabilities found\" on one line swallow a genuine\nadvisory printed on the next. Four self-tests pin that boundary:\n\n  - clean composer baseline            -> GREEN\n  - clean cargo-audit line             -> GREEN\n  - clean line + non-zero exit         -> RED (tool still says failure)\n  - clean line + finding on next line  -> RED (scrub must not leak)\n  - finding on the same line           -> RED (unchanged)\n\nThe last three exist because the first two would also pass if the scrub\nwere too wide. Self-tests now 22 classification + capture cases.\n\n* ci: make a RED dependency report diagnosable\n\nThe wrapper''s excerpt took the literal last 100 lines of output. `cargo\naudit` prints the advisory header first and then a dependency tree of\nhundreds of lines, so the tail discarded the header and kept the tree. The\n2026-09-25 cargo-audit red therefore read \"1 vulnerability found!\" with no\ncrate name, no advisory ID, and no fix — the reader had to go dig through\nthe raw log to learn what was wrong.\n\nFor a RED verdict the excerpt now extracts the lines that answer \"which\nadvisory?\": the decisive signal, advisory IDs (RUSTSEC/CVE/GHSA), and the\nCrate/Version/Title/ID/Date/Solution/Severity fields, printed above the\nusual tail.\n\nThe scrub deliberately does not swallow an advisory''s `Title:` line, which\ncan read like a clean negation, so the clean-line check is applied to the\nextraction too. Verified against a synthetic cargo-audit report: the\nextraction yields the signal line, crate, version, and advisory ID that the\nblind tail hid.\n\n* ci: anchor the RED excerpt to the finding, not the warning noise\n\nThe previous extraction swept the whole output for signal lines and kept\nthe first 40. `cargo audit` prints the WARNING blocks first — ignored\nadvisories, each with its own Crate/ID/Solution lines — so the quota was\nspent on warnings and the vulnerability block was cut off. On the real\n2026-09-25 run that meant the summary surfaced ten RUSTSEC ids of\n*allowed* warnings and neither the crate nor the fix.\n\nThe window is now anchored to the decisive line (`N vulnerabilities\nfound`) and takes the lines around it, which is where the header and\ndetails sit. Verified against a faithful reproduction: extraction yields\nthe crate, version, title, ID, severity, and `Upgrade to >=0.23.45`, and\nno ignored-warning ids.\n\n* chore(autofix): cargo fmt + cargo fix + clippy --fix + Cargo versioning\n\nAuto-applied by autofix.yml di PR #930.\n\n* ci: strip ANSI before classifying, or the check is silently blind\n\nThe RED excerpt was verified against a synthetic cargo-audit report and\nworked. Against the real tool it produced zero lines. `cargo audit` colours\nits output by default, so lines arrive as `\\x1b[1mCrate:\\x1b[0m rustls`.\nThe `^`-anchored patterns (the Crate/Version/Solution fields, `^error:`)\nnever matched, and the section was silently empty.\n\nWorse than a cosmetic miss: `error\\[advisories\\]` and `^error: .*(deny|\nbanned)` are decisive patterns with the same anchor, so a coloured\ncargo-deny failure could have been classified as no-finding. That is the\nsilent-green class this wrapper exists to eliminate, reintroduced through\ncolour codes.\n\nOutput is now stripped of ANSI once, centrally, before any matching, rather\nthan relying on every tool being invoked with `--color never`. Two\nself-tests feed real escape sequences through the classifier so this cannot\nregress quietly.\n\nVerified against the actual CI log: the excerpt now yields\n`Crate: rustls / Version: 0.23.43 / RUSTSEC-2026-0285 / Severity: 5.3 /\nSolution: Upgrade to >=0.23.45` — the exact information the blind tail was\ndiscarding.\n\n* fix(screenshots): stop the gallery generator emitting a lint error\n\n`gallery.py --embed` appended `\"\\n\" + \"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\\n\"`, but `lines`\nalready ends with a blank separator. Joining then leaves one trailing newline,\nso the extra `\"\\n\\n\"` produced two blank lines before the END marker —\n`README.md:617-618`, which markdownlint flags as MD012 (no-multiple-blanks).\nIt was the only failing check on this PR, and it came from the tool rather\nthan from anyone''s edit.\n\nNow normalises to exactly one blank line. Regenerating is idempotent: the only\ndiff is the single removed line.\n\nThe generator also checks the block it just wrote for consecutive blank lines\nand fails with the offending line number, so a future edit to the append logic\nsurfaces here instead of in CI. Verified by reintroducing the old\nconcatenation: the guard reported `README.md:617` and exited 2.\n\nConfirmed against the repo''s own config — `markdownlint-cli2@0.18.0 --config\ninfra/lint/.markdownlint.jsonc README.md` → 0 errors.\n\n* fix(ci): parse the advisory block instead of anchoring to a stray error line\n\nThe RED excerpt claimed to extract \"what was found?\" but in CI it emitted a\nsingle line: `error: 1 vulnerability found!` — no crate, no ID, no fix. The\ninformation it was written to surface stayed invisible.\n\nRoot cause: `run_once` captures stdout and stderr **separately** and\nconcatenates them. `cargo audit` writes the report to stdout and the summary\nline to stderr, so in the output actually classified, `error:` sits at the\nvery end — hundreds of lines past the advisory block it describes. The ±line\nwindow around that anchor could never reach the block.\n\nThat it appeared to work while developing is the instructive part: the\nearlier check was run against the *merged* CI log, where the two streams are\ninterleaved and `error:` happens to land inside its block. It depended on a\ncoincidence of ordering, not on content.\n\nReplaced with a block parser: `Crate:` opens a block, `Dependency tree:`\ncloses it (the tree runs to hundreds of lines and is not part of the answer).\nA block counts as a finding when it has `Severity:`, or `ID:` without\n`Warning:` — cargo audit''s informational advisories always carry `Warning:`\nand never `Severity:`, so warnings no longer drown the summary.\n\nVerified against the real captured output: 8 lines returned including\n`Crate: rustls`, `Version: 0.23.43`, `RUSTSEC-2026-0285`, `Severity: 5.3\n(medium)` and `Solution: Upgrade to >=0.23.45`. Self-tests now reproduce the\nstdout/stderr split rather than the interleaved form, and assert both that the\nfinding is surfaced and that warning blocks and dependency-tree tails are not.\n\nAlso drops the now-unused `RAW_ERROR_RE`.\n\n* fix(screenshots): repair overflow detection that could never run\n\nThe layout check that flags a page wider than the viewport pushed to a `flags`\narray declared ~120 lines *below* it, and again inside the same block as the\nreport site. Two consequences, both silent:\n\n1. **Temporal dead zone.** `flags` was in scope but uninitialised when the check\n   ran, so any page with `scrollWidth > innerWidth` threw\n   `ReferenceError: Cannot access ''flags'' before initialization`. That is caught\n   by the catch-all, so the page was filed as a generic capture failure instead\n   of `meluber-horizontal:1700>1600`. The one signal that says \"this page is\n   untidy\" was the one that could never fire.\n2. **Shadowing.** The inner `const flags = []` was declared in the same block as\n   the `findings.push`, so even initialising the outer one would have had its\n   overflow entries discarded at report time.\n\nReproduced both before fixing: the TDZ throws, and after fixing only the TDZ the\noverflow flags still never reach `findings`. With the declaration hoisted to the\ntop of `shoot()` and the shadow removed, the check collects\n`meluber-horizontal` and `elemen-luar` as intended.\n\nConsequence for the current gallery: the \"0 flagged\" result stands for every\ncategory except this one, which was not actually running — its 0 was a constant,\nnot a measurement. Re-running the capture is what settles whether any page\ngenuinely overflows; that is in flight and will be reported, not assumed.\n\n* docs(screenshots): document the seeding step the gallery actually requires\n\nThe gallery''s ''how to update'' table listed three commands, none of which\nprepare the database. Following it verbatim against a fresh stack does not\nfail loudly: capture.mjs reports ''64 captured, 7 unresolved'' and exits 1,\nbecause the detail pages for izin pemakaian and penghapusan have no row to\nopen. The run looks mostly successful while four pages silently drop out of\nthe gallery.\n\nBoth fixtures are required and ordered — seed-perlengkapan-workflow.sql\nreferences the users and satkers seed-multisatker.sql creates.\n\nAlso refresh the 70 captures and re-embed them into README.md.\n\n* fix(security): bump rustls 0.23.43 -> 0.23.45 (RUSTSEC-2026-0285)\n\ncargo audit turned red on this branch, and it was right to: RUSTSEC-2026-0285\n(medium, published 2026-09-14) reports TLS 1.3 handshake messages being\naccepted across encryption level boundaries. rustls is in the build graph via\nlayanan-perlengkapan, authenc-core and lib-ui, so the advisory is not\nlockfile-only.\n\nThe workspace pin was already ''0.23.40'' — permissive enough to pick up the fix,\nso only the lockfile moves. rustls-webpki and aws-lc-rs/aws-lc-sys follow\n(0.103.13->0.103.15, 1.16.3->1.18.1, 0.40.0->0.45.0); all are the versions\ncargo resolves as compatible with the existing requirements.\n\nVerified: ''cargo audit'' exits 0 (only the 9 pre-existing allowed warnings\nremain), ''cargo metadata --locked'' resolves, and ''cargo check --locked -p\nlayanan-gateway'' compiles clean.\n\nWorth noting this is evidence the retry wrapper behaves as intended: the same\nstep that would have been retried on a network blip reported a real finding\ninstead of masking it.\n\n* ci(security): stop the full-history fetch flake from failing the secret scan\n\nThe gitleaks job went red twice in a row on 2026-09-25, and neither time was\na finding. Both failures were in actions/checkout, the only checkout in this\nworkflow with fetch-depth: 0:\n\n  error: RPC failed; curl 92 HTTP/2 stream 5 was not closed cleanly: CANCEL (err 8)\n  error: 11992 bytes of body are still expected\n  fatal: early EOF\n  fatal: fetch-pack: invalid index-pack output\n\nThe transfer then stalled until timeout-minutes: 30 killed the job at ~19 min.\nSecurity Summary is fail-closed on a cancelled blocking job, so a transport\nblip surfaced as a red secret scan.\n\nThat fail-closed behaviour is correct and is left alone — a cancelled secret\nscan must never read as green, and worse, a half-fetched tree scanned as if\ncomplete would report ''no findings'' for code gitleaks never read. The repair\ntherefore goes in the transport and is paired with a hard assertion:\n\n  - HTTP/1.1 + larger postBuffer + low-speed timeouts, set before checkout so\n    the action''s git inherits them (HTTP/1.1 is the documented mitigation for\n    this HTTP/2 stream CANCEL class).\n  - actions/checkout has no retry, so a single blip is fatal. It now runs with\n    continue-on-error, and a bounded 5-attempt fetch loop repairs a failed\n    checkout. On success the commit is checked out by SHA — fetching refs alone\n    leaves no working tree, which is the silent-empty-scan failure mode.\n  - A final assertion fails the job if history is shallow, if HEAD has no\n    usable history, or if .gitleaks.toml is absent (proving the tree really is\n    checked out).\n\nVerified: YAML parses (6 steps); the repair loop''s fetch+checkout-by-SHA path\nreproduces against a local remote; the shallow guard exits 1 as intended.\n\n* feat(authz): give role checks one definition shared by both tiers\n\n\"Is this caller an admin?\" had four different answers in this repository:\n\n| Location | Rule |\n|---|---|\n| `lib_core::UserRole::is_admin` | `starts_with(\"admin\")` |\n| authenc `admin_auth_middleware` | `roles.contains(\"admin\")` |\n| perlengkapan `Claims::require_admin` | `admin` / `admin_pusat` / `superadmin` |\n| perlengkapan `Claims::is_cross_satker_role` | the above **plus** `validator_pusat`, `pusat`, `analis_pusat` |\n\nThe frontend''s was the loosest, so the UI could open a surface the server\nthen refused -- or treat a read-only role as an administrator. The\ndisagreement was not theoretical: `admin_pusat` and `superadmin` were\nadministrators everywhere except authenc''s guard, so the profile badge read\n\"Admin Pusat\", the FE rendered the admin console, and every request behind it\nanswered 403.\n\nThe permission vocabulary was in the same state. Portal''s `has_permission`\ntested role names against strings like `\"admin:*\"` and `\"user:read\"` that no\nissuer ever minted, so `MenuVisibility::AnyPermission` could never fire. And\nauthenc''s `require_permission` ignored its `permission` argument entirely and\nreduced to \"is admin\" -- a guard that looks mounted but checks something else\nis how a missing check stays missing.\n\n`lib_core::authz` is now the single source of truth, consumed by both\nmicrofrontends and both backends:\n\n* `RoleSet` projects the token''s realm roles; every predicate is an **exact**\n  match against a named role. `starts_with(\"admin\")` admitted\n  `admin_master_read_only`, `admin_audit_log` and `administrative` -- all\n  plausible names, because roles are database rows, not compile-time variants.\n* `Capability` is the action layer on top, so surfaces ask for a capability\n  rather than a role name and the role-to-privilege mapping lives in one place.\n* `require_permission` resolves the capability it is given and answers 500 on\n  an unrecognised one, surfacing a route-definition typo instead of blaming\n  the caller.\n\nAlso removes perlengkapan''s \"Ganti Role\" switcher. The server re-derives every\nscope from the bearer token, so it was never escalation -- but it let the UI\nassert an identity the user does not hold, showing an operator an admin menu\nwhose every link 403s. The session is now read from the JWT.\n\nThe new predicates carry tests, and the negative case is the one that matters:\n`admin_readonly`, `administrative` and `super_admin` must be refused, and every\nrole the shared allowlist blesses must pass in any casing. authenc''s admin\nmodule previously had no test at all -- only a `TODO` stub -- so nothing pinned\nthat a satker-bound role could not pass its guard.\n\nCo-authored-by: openhands <openhands@all-hands.dev>\n\n* fix(perlengkapan): consolidate the response envelope onto one shared type\n\nThe `/penghapusan-bmn` list rendered \"Gagal memuat data\" over a perfectly\nhealthy 200. The cause was a local `PaginatedResponse` that had dropped\n`total_pages`: serde rejects the **entire** response when one required field\nis absent, so a stale copy of the envelope blanked the whole page. Three\ncopies existed -- `penghapusan_bmn/handlers.rs` plus\n`workflow/handlers.rs` and `workflow/definition_handlers.rs` -- and all now\nre-export `lib_perlengkapan::response::ApiResponse`. The two remaining copies\nwere field-identical at the time of the fix, so no bug was live; they were\nthe exact class that had already drifted once.\n\nThe DTO-drift guard could not see this, and that is the more important half of\nthe fix. Its field-level pass **unions** same-named backend structs, so it\nmerged the shared envelope with the local copy and absorbed the difference --\nleaving it blind to exactly the class of bug it exists to catch. It now also\ncatches duplicate envelope declarations, scoped by *derived* crate dependency\nrather than a hand-written list: it reads each service''s `Cargo.toml` and flags\na local envelope only when that service depends on a shared crate defining the\nsame one. That distinction is load-bearing -- secreton''s `ApiResponse` carries\n`error`/`metadata` where perlengkapan''s carries `message`, and the two are\nunrelated types in unrelated domains, so a naive \"more than one declaration\"\nrule would flag it and get the guard deleted.\n\n`lib/perlengkapan/src/response.rs` is added to the scan because the canonical\nenvelope moved there; without it the shared type had no local twin to pair\nagainst and the frontend''s copy read as an invention, the opposite of the\ntruth.\n\nGuards are mutation-tested against the real tree, not just asserted:\n\n* reintroducing a duplicate envelope in `workflow/handlers.rs` turns the guard\n  red with `rc=1`;\n* `#[serde(skip_serializing)]` on the shared `message` field fails the unit\n  test with `left: {\"data\",\"success\"}`.\n\nThe unit test was strengthened for the same reason. It previously asserted\nonly that the serialised output *contained* `\"success\"` and `\"true\"` -- which\npasses just as well when `data` and `message` are gone, so it could not have\ncaught the drift above. It now asserts the exact key set.\n\n`--selftest` is wired into CI next to the guard, following the convention\nalready used for the dependency-check wrapper: a check that exists to catch a\nblind spot must be shown to catch it.\n\nCo-authored-by: openhands <openhands@all-hands.dev>\n\n* fix(portal): let the compose FE-to-BE data path actually reach a backend\n\nThe portal''s `nginx.conf` hard-coded its upstream backends to the Kubernetes\nService ports under a comment claiming they \"can be overridden at build time\nvia --build-arg or in docker-compose environment\". No such override existed:\n`map $host $perlengkapan_api_upstream { default \"layanan-perlengkapan:8093\"; }`\nis a literal, and compose binds those backends on 3020/8088. So any in-browser\ncall routed through the portal''s own nginx answered 502 -- including the login\npage''s captcha widget -- while looking, from the config and the comment, like a\nportable setup.\n\nThe upstreams are now `__PLACEHOLDER__`s substituted at container start from\n`PERLENGKAPAN_API_UPSTREAM` / `AUTHENC_API_UPSTREAM`, matching the pattern\nperlengkapan''s entrypoint already uses. Defaults stay the K8s ports; compose\nsets 3020/8088.\n\nTwo details inherited from that precedent, both of which are failure modes\nrather than style: the `sed -i` must not run unconditionally under `set -e`\n(it writes its temp file into the target''s directory), and under Helm the chart\nmounts its own rendered config over this path -- a read-only ConfigMap on a\nread-only root filesystem -- so the substitution is skipped when the\nplaceholders are absent. If placeholders are present but unwritable the\ncontainer exits rather than serving a config that would proxy to a literal\n`__..__` host.\n\nAlso corrects the `AUTHENC_URL` comment in compose, which described\norigin-relative auth calls as surfacing \"a clear 404\" instead of hitting a\nstaging IP. They surface a 502 against an upstream that never existed.\n\nCo-authored-by: openhands <openhands@all-hands.dev>\n\n* docs(screenshots): refresh the README gallery from a clean capture run\n\nRe-captured both frontends after the portal proxy fix, so the data-driven\npages now render their content instead of the error arm. The gallery is\nregenerated from the capture rather than hand-edited; only the pixel\ndimensions in the `<sub>` captions moved.\n\nEvery shot is verified by `image-report.json`, which measures each PNG rather\nthan trusting that the page loaded: 70 images, 0 flags, minimum 62 distinct\ncolours, minimum ink-row fraction 0.181, and content reaching the middle of\nthe viewport in all 70. A blank, white or single-colour page cannot satisfy\nthose numbers, so the gallery cannot silently regress to empty shells.\n\nCo-authored-by: openhands <openhands@all-hands.dev>\n\n* fix(security): tutup false-green CI, IAM admin=admin saja, audit aksi admin, step-up MFA\n\nCI (wrapper dependency-check):\n- klasifikasi TLS/integritas (sertifikat tak tepercaya) => MERAH, bukan \"jaringan\"\n- pola jaringan dipersempit agar teks temuan tidak dianggap gangguan jaringan\n- job terjadwal fail-closed (DEP_CHECK_HANG_IS_RED): HANG => merah; PR/push tetap hijau + ::warning\n- repair loop gitleaks: fetch SHA eksplisit dan cek checkout sebelum exit 0\n- selftest diperluas (regresi false-green + kontrol positif)\n\nlib-core / lib-backend:\n- authz: tanpa \"admin implisit superset\"; capability aditif; IAM admin = role `admin` persis\n- Capability::View = punya >=1 role; role approver_satker/validator_satker di katalog\n- Claims membawa assigned_roles/active_role/groups\n- lib_backend::client_ip: resolusi IP klien hanya dari proxy tepercaya (TRUSTED_PROXY_CIDRS)\n\nauthenc:\n- token mfa_pending ditolak di validate/introspect/gRPC ValidateToken/require_admin\n- audit_logs.ip_address tidak lagi gagal cast `inet` (IP diparse ke IpAddr) dan tidak bisa dipalsukan via XFF\n- konsol IAM: guard memverifikasi JWT + revocation + role dari token saja (tanpa fallback DB)\n- aksi admin (user/role) dicatat dengan aktor, resource, perubahan field; admin terakhir tidak bisa dicabut/dinonaktifkan; sesi dicabut saat role dicabut\n- generate kode pemulihan MFA butuh TOTP saat ini (step-up), dicatat sebagai MFA_BACKUP_CODES; jalur MFA/password masuk audit\n- muat role user diurutkan deterministik dan mengabaikan role terhapus\n\nportal: halaman kode cadangan MFA meminta kode TOTP saat ini.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01317pESAnup3pKqMNMfBi6r\n\n* feat(perlengkapan): auth deny-by-default, tanpa bypass admin, maker-checker, break-glass\n\nAutentikasi\n- middleware `require_authentication` di seluruh /api/v1/perlengkapan: tanpa bearer\n  token => 401 sebelum handler (termasuk path yang tak ada). Hanya handshake WebSocket\n  (validasi token sendiri) yang dikecualikan. Extractor `Claims` memakai klaim yang\n  sudah divalidasi (tanpa panggilan gRPC kedua).\n- rate limiter per-user kini benar-benar per-user (dulu semua request jatuh ke satu\n  bucket \"nil user\"); health/metrics tidak lagi ikut dibatasi.\n- ClientIp lewat lib_backend::client_ip (header hanya dipercaya dari proxy tepercaya).\n- CORS: deny-by-default di luar dev; SKIP_AUTHENC hanya untuk dev/development/local/test.\n\nOtorisasi\n- Claims membawa SEMUA role + role primer deterministik (bukan `realm_roles.first()`);\n  role `system` tidak bisa diklaim token.\n- Hapus bypass admin di WorkflowPolicy, Claims::require_any_role, dan engine workflow;\n  COMPLETED kini `validator_pusat`. Admin tetap bisa: data master/template (Capability::\n  Administer), audit (ViewAudit), auto-expire.\n- admin/master, admin/templates tidak lagi terbuka untuk validator_pusat/pusat/analis_pusat.\n- Pemakaian: policy untuk create/update/cancel/activate/dokumen; transisi generik hanya\n  Submit & Cancel (endpoint khusus tak bisa dilewati); maker-checker (pengusul tak boleh\n  memvalidasi, approver bukan pengusul/validator); auto-expire khusus admin.\n- Kebutuhan/Penghapusan/Pakaian: peran aktor yang mengotorisasi diteruskan ke engine;\n  gerbang kasar batch & transisi; campaign submit/approve/reject khusus validator_pusat;\n  override darurat sinkronisasi menjadi wewenang Validator Pusat (bukan prefix `admin_`).\n- Penghapusan: create khusus operator, lookup SIMAN dibatasi scope pemanggil dan\n  fail-closed (bukan fallback ke nilai klien), plafon kewenangan Wilayah opsional\n  (PENGHAPUSAN_WILAYAH_MAX_NILAI).\n- Delegasi divalidasi (hanya role yang dipegang, bukan admin, maks 30 hari, alasan,\n  penerima ada) dan ditandai `berlaku: false` karena belum menjadi hak akses.\n\nBreak-glass\n- POST /admin/break-glass/{modul}/{id}/transition (khusus admin, alasan >= 20 karakter,\n  dicatat SEBELUM dijalankan di perlengkapan.break_glass_log [V012], dijalankan sebagai\n  aktor internal dengan user id admin) dan GET /admin/break-glass (admin + validator_pusat).\n\nTes: 13 tes integrasi baru (rbac_bfla_test) + unit tes policy/claims/CORS/delegasi/break-glass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01317pESAnup3pKqMNMfBi6r\n\n* feat(perlengkapan): tutup BFLA/BOLA tersisa, batasi ekspor & analisis per satker, validasi unggahan\n\nEkspor\n- ExportQuery membawa scope dari klaim (tak bisa dikirim klien; default Denied): ekspor\n  kebutuhan & pakaian dinas dibatasi ke satker pemanggil (pakaian = NIP + nama pegawai,\n  dulu se-Indonesia untuk siapa pun). roadmap/riwayat (kunci uuid legacy, tak bisa dibatasi)\n  hanya untuk peran lintas-satker.\n- Job ekspor dimiliki pembuatnya (created_by): status/unduh oleh orang lain = 404; query\n  tersimpan utuh (dulu filter hilang saat unduh; bind text->jsonb tak valid).\n\nAnalisis, forecast, monitoring\n- analisis_kebutuhan mendapat satker_code (V013, additive) — baca dibatasi scope, tulis khusus\n  operator_satker, satker diturunkan dari token.\n- /forecast* khusus ViewAllSatker; /workflow/monitoring/* khusus ViewAudit.\n\nKebutuhan BMN\n- update/hapus periode, tambah satker, prioritas, jml_setuju, tambah/hapus barang, batch:\n  semua kini punya gerbang peran (dan scope untuk objek yang dijangkau lewat id sendiri).\n\nPakaian Dinas\n- tulis roster/profil/ukuran khusus operator_satker (scope `All` milik validator_pusat tak\n  lagi berarti boleh menimpa pegawai siapa pun).\n\nUnggahan & tautan\n- shared::upload: allowlist ekstensi, magic bytes harus cocok, Content-Type diturunkan\n  server (bukan klien), batas 10 MiB & 20 file, dan tautan dokumen hanya http(s)/path situs\n  (bukan javascript:/data:/file:). Lampiran penghapusan khusus operator & hanya saat\n  Draft/Dikembalikan.\n\nTes: +7 tes integrasi (total 20 di rbac_bfla_test), fixture kebutuhan kini menambah barang\nsebagai operator satker (dulu sebagai validator_pusat, lolos hanya karena tak ada gerbang).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01317pESAnup3pKqMNMfBi6r\n\n* ci(authz): penjaga matriks rute + larangan daftar peran-literal; dokumentasi otorisasi\n\n- infra/scripts/check-authz-guards.py (+ --self-test, terpasang di ci.yml):\n  R1 handler ditemukan, R2 menerima Claims, R3 handler TULIS bergerbang, R4 handler BACA\n  ber-scope/bergerbang, R5 tak ada daftar peran-literal di luar lib_core::authz,\n  R6 allowlist tidak boleh basi/tak terpakai. Parser rute tak lagi buta pada\n  `.route(` yang diberi komentar di dalamnya.\n- pakaian-dinas validator-action: gerbang kasar peran alur; /audit: gerbang bernama\n  (admin + validator_pusat/analis_pusat/pusat) alih-alih \"boleh baca lintas satker\".\n- AGENTS.md perlengkapan/lib-core/lib-backend: otentikasi deny-by-default, tanpa bypass\n  admin, maker-checker, break-glass, delegasi (belum berlaku), ekspor & unggahan,\n  CORS/SKIP_AUTHENC, TRUSTED_PROXY_CIDRS, PENGHAPUSAN_WILAYAH_MAX_NILAI.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01317pESAnup3pKqMNMfBi6r\n\n* ci(authz): waiver peran-literal ditaruh di baris yang sama agar selamat dari rustfmt\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01317pESAnup3pKqMNMfBi6r\n\n* feat(authenc): role aktif per sesi (DSD) + klaim groups di balik flag, PKCE hanya S256, DCR jujur (501)\n\n- handlers::active_role: satu pembangun klaim untuk semua jalur penerbitan token.\n  Token selalu memuat assigned_roles + active_role; AUTHENC_ACTIVE_ROLE_ENFORCEMENT=true\n  membuat realm_access.roles tepat [active_role] (semua layanan hilir otomatis mengikuti).\n  POST /api/v1/auth/session/active-role mengganti role (role harus dimiliki; access token\n  lama di-revoke; pilihan disimpan di refresh token bertanda tangan; dicatat ROLE_SWITCH).\n  Default OFF — tanpa flag tak ada perubahan perilaku.\n- AUTHENC_GROUPS_CLAIM=true menambah klaim groups dari hierarki satker (informasional).\n- PKCE: hanya S256; `plain` dan metode kosong ditolak; discovery hanya mengiklankan S256.\n- DCR /register*: 501 dengan penjelasan (dulu 201 berisi error, 200 \"stub\", 204 palsu).\n- AGENTS.md authenc diperbarui.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01317pESAnup3pKqMNMfBi6r\n\n* feat(fe): gerbang konsol IAM = admin, selaraskan tombol dengan backend, katalog role satker\n\n- Portal: konsol IAM hanya untuk `admin` persis (UserSession::can_administer_iam),\n  sama dengan aturan IAM API; sebelumnya terbuka untuk admin_pusat/superadmin lalu\n  setiap request dijawab 403.\n- Perlengkapan: tombol aksi validator tidak lagi menampilkan admin; override untuk\n  validator_pusat; dashboard memakai ViewAllSatker.\n- Katalog peran + deskripsi diselaraskan dengan role satker; label audit portal\n  memakai nama event IAM yang benar (AUTHZ_FAILURE, MFA_SETUP/ENABLE/DISABLE,\n  MFA_BACKUP_CODES, ROLE_SWITCH, SUSPICIOUS_ACTIVITY) dengan nada merah untuk\n  kegagalan.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01317pESAnup3pKqMNMfBi6r\n\n* fix(fe): token `primary` = navy, kontras token dinaikkan, guard CI kontras & token tak terdefinisi\n\n- `bg-primary-600`, `ring-primary-500`, dst. (~100 pemakaian, sebagian besar di\n  lib/ui) tidak punya skala di kedua tailwind config, sehingga Tailwind tidak\n  menghasilkan apa pun: tombol utama transparan, ring fokus tak muncul. `primary`\n  kini alias navy (+ DEFAULT/dark).\n- check-tailwind-shades-exist.py juga gagal untuk token yang dipakai tetapi tak\n  ada skalanya (bukan palet Tailwind).\n- check-color-contrast.py (+ --self-test, di CI): pasangan token yang dideklarasikan\n  harus memenuhi WCAG 2.2 (teks 4.5:1, komponen UI 3:1); `primary` harus sama\n  dengan navy. Menemukan --text-dim 3.5:1, --state-danger 4.49:1 dan ring fokus\n  portal berwarna emas saja 2.2:1 di atas putih -> dinaikkan / dibuat dua warna.\n- Teks inline #64748b di permukaan gelap perlengkapan -> #7b8ba1.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01317pESAnup3pKqMNMfBi6r\n\n* feat(fe): pengalih peran aktif (portal), banner \"belum berlaku\" pada delegasi, label peran\n\n- Portal: UserSession membawa assigned_roles/active_role; komponen RoleSwitcher\n  (\"Bertindak sebagai\") di navbar memanggil POST /api/v1/auth/session/active-role\n  dan hanya muncul bila pengguna punya >1 peran DAN token hanya memuat satu peran\n  (enforcement aktif) — tanpa kontrol yang pasti ditolak server.\n- Perlengkapan: halaman delegasi memuat `berlaku`/`catatan_berlaku` dari server dan\n  menampilkan banner bahwa delegasi belum memberi kewenangan; payload tanpa flag\n  dibaca sebagai \"tidak berlaku\".\n- Portal: halaman peran menampilkan label peran (role_label) + identifier.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01317pESAnup3pKqMNMfBi6r\n\n* feat(infra): CSP script-src berbasis hash, PVC dokumen, allowlist IAM — semuanya opt-in (default OFF)\n\n- CSP: infra/scripts/csp-script-hashes.py (+ --self-test terhadap vektor referensi\n  spesifikasi CSP) menghitung SHA-256 tiap <script> inline di dist/index.html saat\n  build image. Entrypoint portal/perlengkapan menulis /tmp/csp-script-hashes.conf\n  bila CSP_HASH_MODE=true (gagal keras bila berkas hash hilang); nginx (in-image dan\n  ConfigMap Helm) memakai map $csp_script_inline yang jatuh kembali ke\n  ''unsafe-inline'' bila tak ada hash. Diuji dengan nginx sungguhan: header sama\n  dengan sebelumnya saat OFF, script-src berisi hash saat ON. Portal juga kini\n  memakai satu definisi $portal_csp untuk header tingkat-server.\n- Helm: layananPerlengkapan.persistence (PVC + DOCUMENT_STORAGE_PATH + mount) lewat\n  helper _workload.tpl generik; tanpa ini dokumen unggahan hidup di emptyDir /tmp.\n  perlengkapan mendapat tmpVolumeSizeLimit (untuk berkas hash).\n- Helm: istio.iamAllowlist -> AuthorizationPolicy DENY /api/v1/iam/* di luar CIDR;\n  enabled tanpa cidrs membuat render gagal (bukan mengunci semua orang).\n- Render default identik dengan sebelumnya (diff kosong); helm lint + template\n  staging/production hijau, juga dengan flag dinyalakan.\n- infra/AGENTS.md: bagian \"Hardening Opt-in\" (cara nyalakan, verifikasi, batas).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01317pESAnup3pKqMNMfBi6r\n\n* ci(security): pin SHA-256 untuk cargo-audit dan Verus; satu installer bersama\n\n- infra/scripts/install-cargo-audit.sh: unduh rilis ber-versi, verifikasi SHA-256,\n  baru ekstrak. Digest berbeda = gagal keras (asset berubah di bawah tag yang\n  dipin, bukan gangguan jaringan); unduhan gagal = jatuh ke `cargo install --locked`.\n  Dipakai security.yml dan maintenance.yml (sebelumnya `curl | tar` tanpa\n  verifikasi). Diuji: jalur sukses dan jalur digest salah (exit 1).\n- security.yml: unduhan Verus diverifikasi SHA-256 sebelum di-unzip.\n- Digest dihitung dari unduhan langsung rilis GitHub (trust-on-first-use, sama\n  dengan pin cargo-deny yang sudah ada); naikkan versi + digest bersamaan.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01317pESAnup3pKqMNMfBi6r\n\n* docs: laporan audit PR #930 dengan status penanganan per temuan\n\nMemuat temuan A–H (kondisi saat audit), batas audit (integrasi/secreton hanya\ndangkal; ambang nilai Pengelola Barang tidak terverifikasi), dan tabel status:\napa yang diperbaiki, apa yang opt-in default OFF, apa yang belum dikerjakan\nbeserta alasannya.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01317pESAnup3pKqMNMfBi6r\n\n* ci(dto-drift): izinkan cermin FE `Delegation` = BE `DelegationView` (flatten) dengan alasan tertulis\n\nGuard tidak mengikuti #[serde(flatten)] di sisi backend, sehingga `berlaku` dan\n`catatan_berlaku` (ditambahkan DelegationView) terbaca ALWAYS-EMPTY. Dua field itu\nmemang dikirim server; allowlist memuat alasannya dan struct FE mendokumentasikan\nbahwa ia mencerminkan seluruh objek wire.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01317pESAnup3pKqMNMfBi6r\n\n* fix(ci): klasifikasi TLS tidak boleh membuat pemeriksaan yang LULUS menjadi merah\n\nAkar masalah cargo-deny merah di setiap commit sejak e36050a: TLS_INTEGRITY_RE\ndiperiksa sebelum return code dan memuat kata `schannel` telanjang. cargo-deny\nmencetak seluruh pohon dependensi, yang memuat crate `schannel v0.1.x` (dependensi\nnative-tls) — sehingga proses yang keluar 0 diklasifikasikan \"verifikasi sertifikat\nTLS gagal\" (RED). Direproduksi lokal dengan cargo-deny 0.20.2 yang sama: exit 0,\nwrapper RED sebelum perbaikan, GREEN sesudahnya.\n\n- Klasifikasi TLS hanya untuk proses yang gagal (non-nol atau timeout).\n- `schannel` telanjang diganti pola kegagalan sungguhan (`schannel: `, SEC_E_*).\n- Self-test +3 kasus: nama crate `schannel` + exit 0 = GREEN; nama crate saja tidak\n  mengubah kegagalan jaringan menjadi RED; kegagalan SChannel sungguhan tetap RED.\n- docs/audit-pr-930.md: baris kosong di sekitar heading (MD022, gagal di Lint Markdown)\n  dan catatan koreksi C2.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01317pESAnup3pKqMNMfBi6r\n\n* fix(authenc): clippy unnecessary_get_then_check pada test refresh-token role aktif\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01317pESAnup3pKqMNMfBi6r\n\n* test(e2e): gerbang /admin perlengkapan = admin saja; validator_pusat kini 403\n\nSpec masih menegaskan perilaku lama (require_admin = peran lintas-satker, sehingga\nvalidator_pusat mendapat 200). Backend sengaja diubah: require_admin memakai peran\n`admin` persis (lib_core::authz), selaras dengan gerbang FE `/admin`. Seluruh peran\nbisnis di seed CI kini 403; seed CI tak punya user `admin`, sisi positifnya dicakup\nunit test Claims::require_admin.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01317pESAnup3pKqMNMfBi6r\n\n* test(e2e): pulihkan sisi positif gerbang /admin + luruskan komentar basi\n\nPemeriksaan e2e `rbac-scoping.spec.ts` menegaskan validator_pusat mendapat 200\ndi `/admin/master` — perilaku lama sebelum gerbang backend dipersempit menjadi\n`Capability::Administer` (`lib_core::authz::ADMIN_ROLES`). Perilaku baru itu\nsengaja, jadi spesifikasi harus mengikutinya, bukan sebaliknya.\n\nSpec kini menyatakan matriks penuh: setiap peran bisnis (validator_pusat\ntermasuk) ditolak 403, dan identitas `admin` diterima 200.\n\nKomentar pendamping sebelumnya mengklaim \"seed CI tak punya user admin\" — itu\nkeliru. `tests/fixtures/e2e/seed-multisatker.sql` tidak menambah admin, tetapi\nseed authenc (`002_seed.sql:985`) memberi user seed semua-peran\n(199203142014031001) role `admin`, dan `tokenFor(\"admin\")` memang memakai\nidentitas itu. Karena itu sisi positifnya bisa di-assert di sini, bukan\ndiserahkan ke unit test seperti yang dikatakan komentar lama — dan memang\ndi-assert, supaya gerbang tak diam-diam menjadi \"tolak semua\".\n\nKomentar basi yang menyebut `require_admin = is_cross_satker_role` di\n`helpers/real-auth.ts` dan `admin/templates.rs` ikut diluruskan agar tidak\nmengajak pembaca menyimpulkan aturan otorisasi yang sudah tidak berlaku.\n\nCo-authored-by: openhands <openhands@all-hands.dev>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: openhands <openhands@all-hands.dev>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"77b934aec598a8f5045fc4ed55182ab408970503","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/trees/77b934aec598a8f5045fc4ed55182ab408970503"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/commits/f5aee5ac8e5cc33d819f71158aa7046ddebea98e","verification":{"payload":"tree 77b934aec598a8f5045fc4ed55182ab408970503\nparent 22ca5e1a85d25d20d8231f81a56e6a65ca36cbf6\nauthor analisaperlengkapan <analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com> 1790689412 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790689412 +0700\n\nci: make dependency checks hang-proof with retry + network/idle classification (#930)\n\n* ci: make dependency checks hang-proof with retry + network/idle classification\n\nDependency checks (`cargo audit`, `cargo deny`, `composer audit`) all fetch\nsomething over the network before they can check anything: the RustSec advisory\nDB (a git clone), the Packagist advisory DB, the tool release archive, or the\nPHP container image. A dropped connection therefore surfaced as a red\n\"dependency check\", indistinguishable from a real finding.\n\nThis adds `infra/scripts/retry-dependency-check.py`, a wrapper that retries\nnetwork failures with exponential backoff and a per-attempt timeout, then\nclassifies the outcome in three ways:\n\n  GREEN - tool ran, found nothing\n  RED   - tool ran and found something, or failed for a non-network reason\n          (bad config, missing tool, checksum mismatch)\n  HANG  - no response after every attempt; counted green per owner policy,\n          with an explicit note written to the step summary\n\nThe classification is deliberately narrow: a finding is matched BEFORE any\nnetwork pattern, so a finding can never be absorbed into a silent green. The\ngreen-on-outage decision is recorded in the step summary rather than applied\nquietly, because a check that never ran must not look identical to one that\npassed.\n\nChanged:\n- Add `infra/scripts/retry-dependency-check.py` (wrapper + 16-case self-test)\n- security.yml: wrap cargo-audit, composer-audit and cargo-deny; retry the\n  cargo-audit release download and the Verus release download\n- maintenance.yml: wrap cargo audit; retry the cargo-audit / cargo-outdated\n  install paths\n- ci.yml: run the wrapper''s self-test as a required guard\n\nTwo defects found while testing against the real tools rather than assuming:\n\n- The cargo-deny action runs as a container (`FROM rust:1.85-alpine`), so a\n  runner-side advisory-DB pre-seed would have written to a `$HOME` the tool\n  never reads - a safeguard that looks present but is never mounted. Replaced\n  with a checksum-pinned direct install (0.20.2, matching the action''s pin) so\n  the retry wrapper actually governs the advisory-DB clone. Running the binary\n  directly also needs the runner''s `cargo`, so `setup-rust` was added to that\n  job.\n\n- Testing against the real cargo-deny binary surfaced \"failed to fetch crates:\n  failed to run cargo\", a MISSING TOOLCHAIN, which an over-broad\n  `failed to fetch` pattern classified as network -> green. Narrowed, and both\n  cases are locked in as self-test regression cases.\n\nThe self-test proves it can go red, not just green: two injected regressions\n(inverted match order, broadened network pattern) were both caught.\n\nVerified: all three workflows parse; every embedded bash step passes `bash -n`;\n`check-ci-summary-scope`, `check-guard-imports-are-stdlib`,\n`check-actionlint-parity` and `check-pr-workflows-run-on-every-pr` pass.\n\nCo-authored-by: openhands <openhands@all-hands.dev>\n\n* feat(e2e): screenshot every frontend page and publish the gallery in the README\n\nAdds a screenshot sweep that photographs the whole application — both\nmicrofrontends, every route the routers actually declare — against a real\nrunning stack, and embeds the result in the README. The point is not the\nimages: it is that \"every page renders\" becomes a claim something can\nfalsify, instead of a sentence in a document nobody re-checks.\n\nRoute inventory is DERIVED from the routers (`screenshot-routes.py` walks\nthe nesting in both `routes.rs`, including the parameterised detail routes\nthat the curated `pub const` list omits). A hand-written list is correct on\nthe day it is written and silently wrong the next time a route lands, which\nis exactly the failure this is meant to catch.\n\nThree guards decide whether a shot may be published:\n\n  * `check.py` rejects blank/uniform images by pixel metrics. A gallery\n    asserts each listed page renders something; a flat PNG makes that false.\n  * `capture.mjs` flags 404s, a login page on an authenticated route, WASM\n    panics, raw wire enums, unlabelled UUIDs, raw UTC timestamps, and\n    horizontal overflow — each one a defect that actually shipped here.\n  * `gallery.py` refuses to write anything while a defect or an uncaptured\n    route remains, so the README cannot advertise a page that is broken.\n\nGuard shots (operator opening an admin route) are marked `expectDenied`:\nthe 403 card IS the assertion passing, so those signals are recorded as\n`expected` rather than defects — and a guarded route that renders normally\nbecomes a `GUARD-TIDAK-MENAHAN` defect, which is the half that matters.\n\nFixes found by the sweep and fixed here:\n  * audit log USER column showed the raw `user_id` UUID instead of the\n    actor''s username.\n  * `user_id` was duplicated into the audit detail JSON.\n  * WASM bundle download aborts are forgiven only when the retry-mounted\n    page demonstrably booted; a genuine boot failure still fails both\n    attempts and is still reported.\n\nVerified: 70/70 captured, 0 flagged, 70/70 pass the pixel check, all 70\nREADME links resolve, and the business-process suites pass against the same\nstack (86 workflow + 89 RBAC/guard/nav + 14 kebutuhan = 189 tests).\n\n* docs(agents): record the screenshot sweep and its three publication guards\n\nThe sweep is only worth having if the next person knows it exists and what\ngates it. Documents the derived route inventory (and why the curated\n`pub const` list is the wrong source), the three guards, and the\n`expectDenied` convention for guard shots.\n\n* ci: gate the README screenshot gallery against the routers\n\nThe gallery claims \"every page renders\". Nothing in the build read it, so a\nroute could land and the README would keep showing the previous set —\ncorrect on the day it was generated, quietly incomplete after the next\nrouter change. That is the same shape as the other hand-written lists this\nrepo has already been bitten by (the `-p` matrices, the `needs:` lists, the\nstatus vocabulary), so it gets the same treatment: derive the scope.\n\nBoth sides of the comparison are derived. The expected set comes from\n`screenshot-routes.py` — the very script the sweep consumes — so the gate\nand the sweep cannot disagree about what \"every route\" means. That script\nwalks the router nesting rather than the curated `pub const` list, which is\nwhat makes parameterised detail routes count at all.\n\nThe gate ships with a mutation self-test, because a gate that passes on a\nhealthy repo proves nothing: case two deletes one gallery entry and requires\nthe gate to name that route. The neighbouring guard learned this the hard\nway — check-crate-ci-coverage''s first version passed with its `run:` line\ndeleted, since the step NAME still contained the command.\n\nStdlib only (the ARC runner ships no PyYAML), and `--self-test` is wired\ninto the same job so the canary runs on every PR.\n\nVerified: all 65 routes covered; self-test green; the gate red when one\nentry is removed; and all 25 Python guards in the invariants job pass\nlocally.\n\n* ci: close two silent-green dependency probes in cargo-audit job\n\nThe 2026-09-24 run of `cargo-audit` went red on \"Tak ada ignore basi di\n.cargo/audit.toml\" with `gagal mem-parse laporan JSON cargo-audit:\nExpecting value: line 1 column 1 (char 0)`. The probe had hung ~7 minutes\nand handed the downstream guard 0 bytes. That is a network failure wearing\nthe costume of a real finding — the exact class the retry wrapper exists\nto absorb.\n\nTwo probes in the job bypassed the wrapper:\n\n1. \"Tak ada ignore basi\" ran `cargo audit --json` bare. `cargo audit`\n   fetches the RustSec advisory DB from GitHub first, so one dropped\n   connection yields empty stdout, which the downstream guard reports as\n   an unparseable report.\n\n2. \"Assert lockfile-only audit ignores still hold\" ran\n   `cargo tree -i \"$crate\" 2>/dev/null | grep` with no timeout and stderr\n   discarded. Every failure — network, panic, missing toolchain — printed\n   `ok: rkyv tetap di luar build graph`. It could not tell \"checked and\n   clean\" from \"could not check\", so it passed without checking. `-i` also\n   exits non-zero on the NORMAL case (crate absent), which is why its\n   failures were indistinguishable from a valid result.\n\nBoth now go through the wrapper. A new `--capture` mode handles probes\nwhose payload is stdout rather than an exit code, and it deliberately does\nNOT write the report file when the tool never answered — so the downstream\nguard skips with an honest `::notice::` instead of parsing an empty file\nand going red. The lockfile-only probe now greps a full `cargo tree` dump\n(exit 0 on success), so absence of the crate is meaningful.\n\nSelf-tests cover the capture mode''s three states: report written despite\nnon-zero exit (cargo audit exits non-zero precisely when it finds\nsomething), network failure = green with NO file, non-network failure =\nstill red.\n\nVerified against a simulated hang: step exits 0 with the notice, while a\nreal report still reaches the guard and stale ignores are still caught.\n\n* docs(screenshots): refresh gallery from a clean capture run\n\nRe-ran the full pipeline (capture -> check -> gallery) end to end against the\nlive stack to confirm the committed gallery reproduces from current code\nrather than having drifted.\n\n70 captures, 0 unresolved route parameters, 0 flagged. 21 PNGs differ from the\nprevious set by 0.01-0.28% of pixels — dynamic values only (session timestamps,\nrecord counts). The gallery''s own numbers move with them: the sessions page''s\nheight changed 1095 -> 1089 in README.\n\nThe capture step clears its output directory, so `image-report.json` and\n`GALLERY.md` must be regenerated afterwards; both are restored here.\n\n* ci: stop reading a clean dependency scan as a finding\n\n`composer-audit (simpelv1)` went red with the tool''s own output saying\n\"No security vulnerability advisories found.\" — no advisory existed. The\nfinding pattern `advisories? (found|detected)` matches that clean sentence\nverbatim, so the classifier reported a passing audit as a finding.\n\nThis is the mirror image of the bug the wrapper was written to fix. The\noriginal defect let a failure look like success; this one let success look\nlike a failure. Both destroy the signal, and a red that means nothing is a\nred people learn to ignore — which is how it also hides a real finding.\n\nClean negations are now neutralised before the finding patterns are\napplied. The scrub is per-line (`[^\\n]` bounded), because a blanket scrub\nwould let \"No vulnerabilities found\" on one line swallow a genuine\nadvisory printed on the next. Four self-tests pin that boundary:\n\n  - clean composer baseline            -> GREEN\n  - clean cargo-audit line             -> GREEN\n  - clean line + non-zero exit         -> RED (tool still says failure)\n  - clean line + finding on next line  -> RED (scrub must not leak)\n  - finding on the same line           -> RED (unchanged)\n\nThe last three exist because the first two would also pass if the scrub\nwere too wide. Self-tests now 22 classification + capture cases.\n\n* ci: make a RED dependency report diagnosable\n\nThe wrapper''s excerpt took the literal last 100 lines of output. `cargo\naudit` prints the advisory header first and then a dependency tree of\nhundreds of lines, so the tail discarded the header and kept the tree. The\n2026-09-25 cargo-audit red therefore read \"1 vulnerability found!\" with no\ncrate name, no advisory ID, and no fix — the reader had to go dig through\nthe raw log to learn what was wrong.\n\nFor a RED verdict the excerpt now extracts the lines that answer \"which\nadvisory?\": the decisive signal, advisory IDs (RUSTSEC/CVE/GHSA), and the\nCrate/Version/Title/ID/Date/Solution/Severity fields, printed above the\nusual tail.\n\nThe scrub deliberately does not swallow an advisory''s `Title:` line, which\ncan read like a clean negation, so the clean-line check is applied to the\nextraction too. Verified against a synthetic cargo-audit report: the\nextraction yields the signal line, crate, version, and advisory ID that the\nblind tail hid.\n\n* ci: anchor the RED excerpt to the finding, not the warning noise\n\nThe previous extraction swept the whole output for signal lines and kept\nthe first 40. `cargo audit` prints the WARNING blocks first — ignored\nadvisories, each with its own Crate/ID/Solution lines — so the quota was\nspent on warnings and the vulnerability block was cut off. On the real\n2026-09-25 run that meant the summary surfaced ten RUSTSEC ids of\n*allowed* warnings and neither the crate nor the fix.\n\nThe window is now anchored to the decisive line (`N vulnerabilities\nfound`) and takes the lines around it, which is where the header and\ndetails sit. Verified against a faithful reproduction: extraction yields\nthe crate, version, title, ID, severity, and `Upgrade to >=0.23.45`, and\nno ignored-warning ids.\n\n* chore(autofix): cargo fmt + cargo fix + clippy --fix + Cargo versioning\n\nAuto-applied by autofix.yml di PR #930.\n\n* ci: strip ANSI before classifying, or the check is silently blind\n\nThe RED excerpt was verified against a synthetic cargo-audit report and\nworked. Against the real tool it produced zero lines. `cargo audit` colours\nits output by default, so lines arrive as `\\x1b[1mCrate:\\x1b[0m rustls`.\nThe `^`-anchored patterns (the Crate/Version/Solution fields, `^error:`)\nnever matched, and the section was silently empty.\n\nWorse than a cosmetic miss: `error\\[advisories\\]` and `^error: .*(deny|\nbanned)` are decisive patterns with the same anchor, so a coloured\ncargo-deny failure could have been classified as no-finding. That is the\nsilent-green class this wrapper exists to eliminate, reintroduced through\ncolour codes.\n\nOutput is now stripped of ANSI once, centrally, before any matching, rather\nthan relying on every tool being invoked with `--color never`. Two\nself-tests feed real escape sequences through the classifier so this cannot\nregress quietly.\n\nVerified against the actual CI log: the excerpt now yields\n`Crate: rustls / Version: 0.23.43 / RUSTSEC-2026-0285 / Severity: 5.3 /\nSolution: Upgrade to >=0.23.45` — the exact information the blind tail was\ndiscarding.\n\n* fix(screenshots): stop the gallery generator emitting a lint error\n\n`gallery.py --embed` appended `\"\\n\" + \"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\\n\"`, but `lines`\nalready ends with a blank separator. Joining then leaves one trailing newline,\nso the extra `\"\\n\\n\"` produced two blank lines before the END marker —\n`README.md:617-618`, which markdownlint flags as MD012 (no-multiple-blanks).\nIt was the only failing check on this PR, and it came from the tool rather\nthan from anyone''s edit.\n\nNow normalises to exactly one blank line. Regenerating is idempotent: the only\ndiff is the single removed line.\n\nThe generator also checks the block it just wrote for consecutive blank lines\nand fails with the offending line number, so a future edit to the append logic\nsurfaces here instead of in CI. Verified by reintroducing the old\nconcatenation: the guard reported `README.md:617` and exited 2.\n\nConfirmed against the repo''s own config — `markdownlint-cli2@0.18.0 --config\ninfra/lint/.markdownlint.jsonc README.md` → 0 errors.\n\n* fix(ci): parse the advisory block instead of anchoring to a stray error line\n\nThe RED excerpt claimed to extract \"what was found?\" but in CI it emitted a\nsingle line: `error: 1 vulnerability found!` — no crate, no ID, no fix. The\ninformation it was written to surface stayed invisible.\n\nRoot cause: `run_once` captures stdout and stderr **separately** and\nconcatenates them. `cargo audit` writes the report to stdout and the summary\nline to stderr, so in the output actually classified, `error:` sits at the\nvery end — hundreds of lines past the advisory block it describes. The ±line\nwindow around that anchor could never reach the block.\n\nThat it appeared to work while developing is the instructive part: the\nearlier check was run against the *merged* CI log, where the two streams are\ninterleaved and `error:` happens to land inside its block. It depended on a\ncoincidence of ordering, not on content.\n\nReplaced with a block parser: `Crate:` opens a block, `Dependency tree:`\ncloses it (the tree runs to hundreds of lines and is not part of the answer).\nA block counts as a finding when it has `Severity:`, or `ID:` without\n`Warning:` — cargo audit''s informational advisories always carry `Warning:`\nand never `Severity:`, so warnings no longer drown the summary.\n\nVerified against the real captured output: 8 lines returned including\n`Crate: rustls`, `Version: 0.23.43`, `RUSTSEC-2026-0285`, `Severity: 5.3\n(medium)` and `Solution: Upgrade to >=0.23.45`. Self-tests now reproduce the\nstdout/stderr split rather than the interleaved form, and assert both that the\nfinding is surfaced and that warning blocks and dependency-tree tails are not.\n\nAlso drops the now-unused `RAW_ERROR_RE`.\n\n* fix(screenshots): repair overflow detection that could never run\n\nThe layout check that flags a page wider than the viewport pushed to a `flags`\narray declared ~120 lines *below* it, and again inside the same block as the\nreport site. Two consequences, both silent:\n\n1. **Temporal dead zone.** `flags` was in scope but uninitialised when the check\n   ran, so any page with `scrollWidth > innerWidth` threw\n   `ReferenceError: Cannot access ''flags'' before initialization`. That is caught\n   by the catch-all, so the page was filed as a generic capture failure instead\n   of `meluber-horizontal:1700>1600`. The one signal that says \"this page is\n   untidy\" was the one that could never fire.\n2. **Shadowing.** The inner `const flags = []` was declared in the same block as\n   the `findings.push`, so even initialising the outer one would have had its\n   overflow entries discarded at report time.\n\nReproduced both before fixing: the TDZ throws, and after fixing only the TDZ the\noverflow flags still never reach `findings`. With the declaration hoisted to the\ntop of `shoot()` and the shadow removed, the check collects\n`meluber-horizontal` and `elemen-luar` as intended.\n\nConsequence for the current gallery: the \"0 flagged\" result stands for every\ncategory except this one, which was not actually running — its 0 was a constant,\nnot a measurement. Re-running the capture is what settles whether any page\ngenuinely overflows; that is in flight and will be reported, not assumed.\n\n* docs(screenshots): document the seeding step the gallery actually requires\n\nThe gallery''s ''how to update'' table listed three commands, none of which\nprepare the database. Following it verbatim against a fresh stack does not\nfail loudly: capture.mjs reports ''64 captured, 7 unresolved'' and exits 1,\nbecause the detail pages for izin pemakaian and penghapusan have no row to\nopen. The run looks mostly successful while four pages silently drop out of\nthe gallery.\n\nBoth fixtures are required and ordered — seed-perlengkapan-workflow.sql\nreferences the users and satkers seed-multisatker.sql creates.\n\nAlso refresh the 70 captures and re-embed them into README.md.\n\n* fix(security): bump rustls 0.23.43 -> 0.23.45 (RUSTSEC-2026-0285)\n\ncargo audit turned red on this branch, and it was right to: RUSTSEC-2026-0285\n(medium, published 2026-09-14) reports TLS 1.3 handshake messages being\naccepted across encryption level boundaries. rustls is in the build graph via\nlayanan-perlengkapan, authenc-core and lib-ui, so the advisory is not\nlockfile-only.\n\nThe workspace pin was already ''0.23.40'' — permissive enough to pick up the fix,\nso only the lockfile moves. rustls-webpki and aws-lc-rs/aws-lc-sys follow\n(0.103.13->0.103.15, 1.16.3->1.18.1, 0.40.0->0.45.0); all are the versions\ncargo resolves as compatible with the existing requirements.\n\nVerified: ''cargo audit'' exits 0 (only the 9 pre-existing allowed warnings\nremain), ''cargo metadata --locked'' resolves, and ''cargo check --locked -p\nlayanan-gateway'' compiles clean.\n\nWorth noting this is evidence the retry wrapper behaves as intended: the same\nstep that would have been retried on a network blip reported a real finding\ninstead of masking it.\n\n* ci(security): stop the full-history fetch flake from failing the secret scan\n\nThe gitleaks job went red twice in a row on 2026-09-25, and neither time was\na finding. Both failures were in actions/checkout, the only checkout in this\nworkflow with fetch-depth: 0:\n\n  error: RPC failed; curl 92 HTTP/2 stream 5 was not closed cleanly: CANCEL (err 8)\n  error: 11992 bytes of body are still expected\n  fatal: early EOF\n  fatal: fetch-pack: invalid index-pack output\n\nThe transfer then stalled until timeout-minutes: 30 killed the job at ~19 min.\nSecurity Summary is fail-closed on a cancelled blocking job, so a transport\nblip surfaced as a red secret scan.\n\nThat fail-closed behaviour is correct and is left alone — a cancelled secret\nscan must never read as green, and worse, a half-fetched tree scanned as if\ncomplete would report ''no findings'' for code gitleaks never read. The repair\ntherefore goes in the transport and is paired with a hard assertion:\n\n  - HTTP/1.1 + larger postBuffer + low-speed timeouts, set before checkout so\n    the action''s git inherits them (HTTP/1.1 is the documented mitigation for\n    this HTTP/2 stream CANCEL class).\n  - actions/checkout has no retry, so a single blip is fatal. It now runs with\n    continue-on-error, and a bounded 5-attempt fetch loop repairs a failed\n    checkout. On success the commit is checked out by SHA — fetching refs alone\n    leaves no working tree, which is the silent-empty-scan failure mode.\n  - A final assertion fails the job if history is shallow, if HEAD has no\n    usable history, or if .gitleaks.toml is absent (proving the tree really is\n    checked out).\n\nVerified: YAML parses (6 steps); the repair loop''s fetch+checkout-by-SHA path\nreproduces against a local remote; the shallow guard exits 1 as intended.\n\n* feat(authz): give role checks one definition shared by both tiers\n\n\"Is this caller an admin?\" had four different answers in this repository:\n\n| Location | Rule |\n|---|---|\n| `lib_core::UserRole::is_admin` | `starts_with(\"admin\")` |\n| authenc `admin_auth_middleware` | `roles.contains(\"admin\")` |\n| perlengkapan `Claims::require_admin` | `admin` / `admin_pusat` / `superadmin` |\n| perlengkapan `Claims::is_cross_satker_role` | the above **plus** `validator_pusat`, `pusat`, `analis_pusat` |\n\nThe frontend''s was the loosest, so the UI could open a surface the server\nthen refused -- or treat a read-only role as an administrator. The\ndisagreement was not theoretical: `admin_pusat` and `superadmin` were\nadministrators everywhere except authenc''s guard, so the profile badge read\n\"Admin Pusat\", the FE rendered the admin console, and every request behind it\nanswered 403.\n\nThe permission vocabulary was in the same state. Portal''s `has_permission`\ntested role names against strings like `\"admin:*\"` and `\"user:read\"` that no\nissuer ever minted, so `MenuVisibility::AnyPermission` could never fire. And\nauthenc''s `require_permission` ignored its `permission` argument entirely and\nreduced to \"is admin\" -- a guard that looks mounted but checks something else\nis how a missing check stays missing.\n\n`lib_core::authz` is now the single source of truth, consumed by both\nmicrofrontends and both backends:\n\n* `RoleSet` projects the token''s realm roles; every predicate is an **exact**\n  match against a named role. `starts_with(\"admin\")` admitted\n  `admin_master_read_only`, `admin_audit_log` and `administrative` -- all\n  plausible names, because roles are database rows, not compile-time variants.\n* `Capability` is the action layer on top, so surfaces ask for a capability\n  rather than a role name and the role-to-privilege mapping lives in one place.\n* `require_permission` resolves the capability it is given and answers 500 on\n  an unrecognised one, surfacing a route-definition typo instead of blaming\n  the caller.\n\nAlso removes perlengkapan''s \"Ganti Role\" switcher. The server re-derives every\nscope from the bearer token, so it was never escalation -- but it let the UI\nassert an identity the user does not hold, showing an operator an admin menu\nwhose every link 403s. The session is now read from the JWT.\n\nThe new predicates carry tests, and the negative case is the one that matters:\n`admin_readonly`, `administrative` and `super_admin` must be refused, and every\nrole the shared allowlist blesses must pass in any casing. authenc''s admin\nmodule previously had no test at all -- only a `TODO` stub -- so nothing pinned\nthat a satker-bound role could not pass its guard.\n\nCo-authored-by: openhands <openhands@all-hands.dev>\n\n* fix(perlengkapan): consolidate the response envelope onto one shared type\n\nThe `/penghapusan-bmn` list rendered \"Gagal memuat data\" over a perfectly\nhealthy 200. The cause was a local `PaginatedResponse` that had dropped\n`total_pages`: serde rejects the **entire** response when one required field\nis absent, so a stale copy of the envelope blanked the whole page. Three\ncopies existed -- `penghapusan_bmn/handlers.rs` plus\n`workflow/handlers.rs` and `workflow/definition_handlers.rs` -- and all now\nre-export `lib_perlengkapan::response::ApiResponse`. The two remaining copies\nwere field-identical at the time of the fix, so no bug was live; they were\nthe exact class that had already drifted once.\n\nThe DTO-drift guard could not see this, and that is the more important half of\nthe fix. Its field-level pass **unions** same-named backend structs, so it\nmerged the shared envelope with the local copy and absorbed the difference --\nleaving it blind to exactly the class of bug it exists to catch. It now also\ncatches duplicate envelope declarations, scoped by *derived* crate dependency\nrather than a hand-written list: it reads each service''s `Cargo.toml` and flags\na local envelope only when that service depends on a shared crate defining the\nsame one. That distinction is load-bearing -- secreton''s `ApiResponse` carries\n`error`/`metadata` where perlengkapan''s carries `message`, and the two are\nunrelated types in unrelated domains, so a naive \"more than one declaration\"\nrule would flag it and get the guard deleted.\n\n`lib/perlengkapan/src/response.rs` is added to the scan because the canonical\nenvelope moved there; without it the shared type had no local twin to pair\nagainst and the frontend''s copy read as an invention, the opposite of the\ntruth.\n\nGuards are mutation-tested against the real tree, not just asserted:\n\n* reintroducing a duplicate envelope in `workflow/handlers.rs` turns the guard\n  red with `rc=1`;\n* `#[serde(skip_serializing)]` on the shared `message` field fails the unit\n  test with `left: {\"data\",\"success\"}`.\n\nThe unit test was strengthened for the same reason. It previously asserted\nonly that the serialised output *contained* `\"success\"` and `\"true\"` -- which\npasses just as well when `data` and `message` are gone, so it could not have\ncaught the drift above. It now asserts the exact key set.\n\n`--selftest` is wired into CI next to the guard, following the convention\nalready used for the dependency-check wrapper: a check that exists to catch a\nblind spot must be shown to catch it.\n\nCo-authored-by: openhands <openhands@all-hands.dev>\n\n* fix(portal): let the compose FE-to-BE data path actually reach a backend\n\nThe portal''s `nginx.conf` hard-coded its upstream backends to the Kubernetes\nService ports under a comment claiming they \"can be overridden at build time\nvia --build-arg or in docker-compose environment\". No such override existed:\n`map $host $perlengkapan_api_upstream { default \"layanan-perlengkapan:8093\"; }`\nis a literal, and compose binds those backends on 3020/8088. So any in-browser\ncall routed through the portal''s own nginx answered 502 -- including the login\npage''s captcha widget -- while looking, from the config and the comment, like a\nportable setup.\n\nThe upstreams are now `__PLACEHOLDER__`s substituted at container start from\n`PERLENGKAPAN_API_UPSTREAM` / `AUTHENC_API_UPSTREAM`, matching the pattern\nperlengkapan''s entrypoint already uses. Defaults stay the K8s ports; compose\nsets 3020/8088.\n\nTwo details inherited from that precedent, both of which are failure modes\nrather than style: the `sed -i` must not run unconditionally under `set -e`\n(it writes its temp file into the target''s directory), and under Helm the chart\nmounts its own rendered config over this path -- a read-only ConfigMap on a\nread-only root filesystem -- so the substitution is skipped when the\nplaceholders are absent. If placeholders are present but unwritable the\ncontainer exits rather than serving a config that would proxy to a literal\n`__..__` host.\n\nAlso corrects the `AUTHENC_URL` comment in compose, which described\norigin-relative auth calls as surfacing \"a clear 404\" instead of hitting a\nstaging IP. They surface a 502 against an upstream that never existed.\n\nCo-authored-by: openhands <openhands@all-hands.dev>\n\n* docs(screenshots): refresh the README gallery from a clean capture run\n\nRe-captured both frontends after the portal proxy fix, so the data-driven\npages now render their content instead of the error arm. The gallery is\nregenerated from the capture rather than hand-edited; only the pixel\ndimensions in the `<sub>` captions moved.\n\nEvery shot is verified by `image-report.json`, which measures each PNG rather\nthan trusting that the page loaded: 70 images, 0 flags, minimum 62 distinct\ncolours, minimum ink-row fraction 0.181, and content reaching the middle of\nthe viewport in all 70. A blank, white or single-colour page cannot satisfy\nthose numbers, so the gallery cannot silently regress to empty shells.\n\nCo-authored-by: openhands <openhands@all-hands.dev>\n\n* fix(security): tutup false-green CI, IAM admin=admin saja, audit aksi admin, step-up MFA\n\nCI (wrapper dependency-check):\n- klasifikasi TLS/integritas (sertifikat tak tepercaya) => MERAH, bukan \"jaringan\"\n- pola jaringan dipersempit agar teks temuan tidak dianggap gangguan jaringan\n- job terjadwal fail-closed (DEP_CHECK_HANG_IS_RED): HANG => merah; PR/push tetap hijau + ::warning\n- repair loop gitleaks: fetch SHA eksplisit dan cek checkout sebelum exit 0\n- selftest diperluas (regresi false-green + kontrol positif)\n\nlib-core / lib-backend:\n- authz: tanpa \"admin implisit superset\"; capability aditif; IAM admin = role `admin` persis\n- Capability::View = punya >=1 role; role approver_satker/validator_satker di katalog\n- Claims membawa assigned_roles/active_role/groups\n- lib_backend::client_ip: resolusi IP klien hanya dari proxy tepercaya (TRUSTED_PROXY_CIDRS)\n\nauthenc:\n- token mfa_pending ditolak di validate/introspect/gRPC ValidateToken/require_admin\n- audit_logs.ip_address tidak lagi gagal cast `inet` (IP diparse ke IpAddr) dan tidak bisa dipalsukan via XFF\n- konsol IAM: guard memverifikasi JWT + revocation + role dari token saja (tanpa fallback DB)\n- aksi admin (user/role) dicatat dengan aktor, resource, perubahan field; admin terakhir tidak bisa dicabut/dinonaktifkan; sesi dicabut saat role dicabut\n- generate kode pemulihan MFA butuh TOTP saat ini (step-up), dicatat sebagai MFA_BACKUP_CODES; jalur MFA/password masuk audit\n- muat role user diurutkan deterministik dan mengabaikan role terhapus\n\nportal: halaman kode cadangan MFA meminta kode TOTP saat ini.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01317pESAnup3pKqMNMfBi6r\n\n* feat(perlengkapan): auth deny-by-default, tanpa bypass admin, maker-checker, break-glass\n\nAutentikasi\n- middleware `require_authentication` di seluruh /api/v1/perlengkapan: tanpa bearer\n  token => 401 sebelum handler (termasuk path yang tak ada). Hanya handshake WebSocket\n  (validasi token sendiri) yang dikecualikan. Extractor `Claims` memakai klaim yang\n  sudah divalidasi (tanpa panggilan gRPC kedua).\n- rate limiter per-user kini benar-benar per-user (dulu semua request jatuh ke satu\n  bucket \"nil user\"); health/metrics tidak lagi ikut dibatasi.\n- ClientIp lewat lib_backend::client_ip (header hanya dipercaya dari proxy tepercaya).\n- CORS: deny-by-default di luar dev; SKIP_AUTHENC hanya untuk dev/development/local/test.\n\nOtorisasi\n- Claims membawa SEMUA role + role primer deterministik (bukan `realm_roles.first()`);\n  role `system` tidak bisa diklaim token.\n- Hapus bypass admin di WorkflowPolicy, Claims::require_any_role, dan engine workflow;\n  COMPLETED kini `validator_pusat`. Admin tetap bisa: data master/template (Capability::\n  Administer), audit (ViewAudit), auto-expire.\n- admin/master, admin/templates tidak lagi terbuka untuk validator_pusat/pusat/analis_pusat.\n- Pemakaian: policy untuk create/update/cancel/activate/dokumen; transisi generik hanya\n  Submit & Cancel (endpoint khusus tak bisa dilewati); maker-checker (pengusul tak boleh\n  memvalidasi, approver bukan pengusul/validator); auto-expire khusus admin.\n- Kebutuhan/Penghapusan/Pakaian: peran aktor yang mengotorisasi diteruskan ke engine;\n  gerbang kasar batch & transisi; campaign submit/approve/reject khusus validator_pusat;\n  override darurat sinkronisasi menjadi wewenang Validator Pusat (bukan prefix `admin_`).\n- Penghapusan: create khusus operator, lookup SIMAN dibatasi scope pemanggil dan\n  fail-closed (bukan fallback ke nilai klien), plafon kewenangan Wilayah opsional\n  (PENGHAPUSAN_WILAYAH_MAX_NILAI).\n- Delegasi divalidasi (hanya role yang dipegang, bukan admin, maks 30 hari, alasan,\n  penerima ada) dan ditandai `berlaku: false` karena belum menjadi hak akses.\n\nBreak-glass\n- POST /admin/break-glass/{modul}/{id}/transition (khusus admin, alasan >= 20 karakter,\n  dicatat SEBELUM dijalankan di perlengkapan.break_glass_log [V012], dijalankan sebagai\n  aktor internal dengan user id admin) dan GET /admin/break-glass (admin + validator_pusat).\n\nTes: 13 tes integrasi baru (rbac_bfla_test) + unit tes policy/claims/CORS/delegasi/break-glass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01317pESAnup3pKqMNMfBi6r\n\n* feat(perlengkapan): tutup BFLA/BOLA tersisa, batasi ekspor & analisis per satker, validasi unggahan\n\nEkspor\n- ExportQuery membawa scope dari klaim (tak bisa dikirim klien; default Denied): ekspor\n  kebutuhan & pakaian dinas dibatasi ke satker pemanggil (pakaian = NIP + nama pegawai,\n  dulu se-Indonesia untuk siapa pun). roadmap/riwayat (kunci uuid legacy, tak bisa dibatasi)\n  hanya untuk peran lintas-satker.\n- Job ekspor dimiliki pembuatnya (created_by): status/unduh oleh orang lain = 404; query\n  tersimpan utuh (dulu filter hilang saat unduh; bind text->jsonb tak valid).\n\nAnalisis, forecast, monitoring\n- analisis_kebutuhan mendapat satker_code (V013, additive) — baca dibatasi scope, tulis khusus\n  operator_satker, satker diturunkan dari token.\n- /forecast* khusus ViewAllSatker; /workflow/monitoring/* khusus ViewAudit.\n\nKebutuhan BMN\n- update/hapus periode, tambah satker, prioritas, jml_setuju, tambah/hapus barang, batch:\n  semua kini punya gerbang peran (dan scope untuk objek yang dijangkau lewat id sendiri).\n\nPakaian Dinas\n- tulis roster/profil/ukuran khusus operator_satker (scope `All` milik validator_pusat tak\n  lagi berarti boleh menimpa pegawai siapa pun).\n\nUnggahan & tautan\n- shared::upload: allowlist ekstensi, magic bytes harus cocok, Content-Type diturunkan\n  server (bukan klien), batas 10 MiB & 20 file, dan tautan dokumen hanya http(s)/path situs\n  (bukan javascript:/data:/file:). Lampiran penghapusan khusus operator & hanya saat\n  Draft/Dikembalikan.\n\nTes: +7 tes integrasi (total 20 di rbac_bfla_test), fixture kebutuhan kini menambah barang\nsebagai operator satker (dulu sebagai validator_pusat, lolos hanya karena tak ada gerbang).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01317pESAnup3pKqMNMfBi6r\n\n* ci(authz): penjaga matriks rute + larangan daftar peran-literal; dokumentasi otorisasi\n\n- infra/scripts/check-authz-guards.py (+ --self-test, terpasang di ci.yml):\n  R1 handler ditemukan, R2 menerima Claims, R3 handler TULIS bergerbang, R4 handler BACA\n  ber-scope/bergerbang, R5 tak ada daftar peran-literal di luar lib_core::authz,\n  R6 allowlist tidak boleh basi/tak terpakai. Parser rute tak lagi buta pada\n  `.route(` yang diberi komentar di dalamnya.\n- pakaian-dinas validator-action: gerbang kasar peran alur; /audit: gerbang bernama\n  (admin + validator_pusat/analis_pusat/pusat) alih-alih \"boleh baca lintas satker\".\n- AGENTS.md perlengkapan/lib-core/lib-backend: otentikasi deny-by-default, tanpa bypass\n  admin, maker-checker, break-glass, delegasi (belum berlaku), ekspor & unggahan,\n  CORS/SKIP_AUTHENC, TRUSTED_PROXY_CIDRS, PENGHAPUSAN_WILAYAH_MAX_NILAI.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01317pESAnup3pKqMNMfBi6r\n\n* ci(authz): waiver peran-literal ditaruh di baris yang sama agar selamat dari rustfmt\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01317pESAnup3pKqMNMfBi6r\n\n* feat(authenc): role aktif per sesi (DSD) + klaim groups di balik flag, PKCE hanya S256, DCR jujur (501)\n\n- handlers::active_role: satu pembangun klaim untuk semua jalur penerbitan token.\n  Token selalu memuat assigned_roles + active_role; AUTHENC_ACTIVE_ROLE_ENFORCEMENT=true\n  membuat realm_access.roles tepat [active_role] (semua layanan hilir otomatis mengikuti).\n  POST /api/v1/auth/session/active-role mengganti role (role harus dimiliki; access token\n  lama di-revoke; pilihan disimpan di refresh token bertanda tangan; dicatat ROLE_SWITCH).\n  Default OFF — tanpa flag tak ada perubahan perilaku.\n- AUTHENC_GROUPS_CLAIM=true menambah klaim groups dari hierarki satker (informasional).\n- PKCE: hanya S256; `plain` dan metode kosong ditolak; discovery hanya mengiklankan S256.\n- DCR /register*: 501 dengan penjelasan (dulu 201 berisi error, 200 \"stub\", 204 palsu).\n- AGENTS.md authenc diperbarui.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01317pESAnup3pKqMNMfBi6r\n\n* feat(fe): gerbang konsol IAM = admin, selaraskan tombol dengan backend, katalog role satker\n\n- Portal: konsol IAM hanya untuk `admin` persis (UserSession::can_administer_iam),\n  sama dengan aturan IAM API; sebelumnya terbuka untuk admin_pusat/superadmin lalu\n  setiap request dijawab 403.\n- Perlengkapan: tombol aksi validator tidak lagi menampilkan admin; override untuk\n  validator_pusat; dashboard memakai ViewAllSatker.\n- Katalog peran + deskripsi diselaraskan dengan role satker; label audit portal\n  memakai nama event IAM yang benar (AUTHZ_FAILURE, MFA_SETUP/ENABLE/DISABLE,\n  MFA_BACKUP_CODES, ROLE_SWITCH, SUSPICIOUS_ACTIVITY) dengan nada merah untuk\n  kegagalan.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01317pESAnup3pKqMNMfBi6r\n\n* fix(fe): token `primary` = navy, kontras token dinaikkan, guard CI kontras & token tak terdefinisi\n\n- `bg-primary-600`, `ring-primary-500`, dst. (~100 pemakaian, sebagian besar di\n  lib/ui) tidak punya skala di kedua tailwind config, sehingga Tailwind tidak\n  menghasilkan apa pun: tombol utama transparan, ring fokus tak muncul. `primary`\n  kini alias navy (+ DEFAULT/dark).\n- check-tailwind-shades-exist.py juga gagal untuk token yang dipakai tetapi tak\n  ada skalanya (bukan palet Tailwind).\n- check-color-contrast.py (+ --self-test, di CI): pasangan token yang dideklarasikan\n  harus memenuhi WCAG 2.2 (teks 4.5:1, komponen UI 3:1); `primary` harus sama\n  dengan navy. Menemukan --text-dim 3.5:1, --state-danger 4.49:1 dan ring fokus\n  portal berwarna emas saja 2.2:1 di atas putih -> dinaikkan / dibuat dua warna.\n- Teks inline #64748b di permukaan gelap perlengkapan -> #7b8ba1.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01317pESAnup3pKqMNMfBi6r\n\n* feat(fe): pengalih peran aktif (portal), banner \"belum berlaku\" pada delegasi, label peran\n\n- Portal: UserSession membawa assigned_roles/active_role; komponen RoleSwitcher\n  (\"Bertindak sebagai\") di navbar memanggil POST /api/v1/auth/session/active-role\n  dan hanya muncul bila pengguna punya >1 peran DAN token hanya memuat satu peran\n  (enforcement aktif) — tanpa kontrol yang pasti ditolak server.\n- Perlengkapan: halaman delegasi memuat `berlaku`/`catatan_berlaku` dari server dan\n  menampilkan banner bahwa delegasi belum memberi kewenangan; payload tanpa flag\n  dibaca sebagai \"tidak berlaku\".\n- Portal: halaman peran menampilkan label peran (role_label) + identifier.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01317pESAnup3pKqMNMfBi6r\n\n* feat(infra): CSP script-src berbasis hash, PVC dokumen, allowlist IAM — semuanya opt-in (default OFF)\n\n- CSP: infra/scripts/csp-script-hashes.py (+ --self-test terhadap vektor referensi\n  spesifikasi CSP) menghitung SHA-256 tiap <script> inline di dist/index.html saat\n  build image. Entrypoint portal/perlengkapan menulis /tmp/csp-script-hashes.conf\n  bila CSP_HASH_MODE=true (gagal keras bila berkas hash hilang); nginx (in-image dan\n  ConfigMap Helm) memakai map $csp_script_inline yang jatuh kembali ke\n  ''unsafe-inline'' bila tak ada hash. Diuji dengan nginx sungguhan: header sama\n  dengan sebelumnya saat OFF, script-src berisi hash saat ON. Portal juga kini\n  memakai satu definisi $portal_csp untuk header tingkat-server.\n- Helm: layananPerlengkapan.persistence (PVC + DOCUMENT_STORAGE_PATH + mount) lewat\n  helper _workload.tpl generik; tanpa ini dokumen unggahan hidup di emptyDir /tmp.\n  perlengkapan mendapat tmpVolumeSizeLimit (untuk berkas hash).\n- Helm: istio.iamAllowlist -> AuthorizationPolicy DENY /api/v1/iam/* di luar CIDR;\n  enabled tanpa cidrs membuat render gagal (bukan mengunci semua orang).\n- Render default identik dengan sebelumnya (diff kosong); helm lint + template\n  staging/production hijau, juga dengan flag dinyalakan.\n- infra/AGENTS.md: bagian \"Hardening Opt-in\" (cara nyalakan, verifikasi, batas).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01317pESAnup3pKqMNMfBi6r\n\n* ci(security): pin SHA-256 untuk cargo-audit dan Verus; satu installer bersama\n\n- infra/scripts/install-cargo-audit.sh: unduh rilis ber-versi, verifikasi SHA-256,\n  baru ekstrak. Digest berbeda = gagal keras (asset berubah di bawah tag yang\n  dipin, bukan gangguan jaringan); unduhan gagal = jatuh ke `cargo install --locked`.\n  Dipakai security.yml dan maintenance.yml (sebelumnya `curl | tar` tanpa\n  verifikasi). Diuji: jalur sukses dan jalur digest salah (exit 1).\n- security.yml: unduhan Verus diverifikasi SHA-256 sebelum di-unzip.\n- Digest dihitung dari unduhan langsung rilis GitHub (trust-on-first-use, sama\n  dengan pin cargo-deny yang sudah ada); naikkan versi + digest bersamaan.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01317pESAnup3pKqMNMfBi6r\n\n* docs: laporan audit PR #930 dengan status penanganan per temuan\n\nMemuat temuan A–H (kondisi saat audit), batas audit (integrasi/secreton hanya\ndangkal; ambang nilai Pengelola Barang tidak terverifikasi), dan tabel status:\napa yang diperbaiki, apa yang opt-in default OFF, apa yang belum dikerjakan\nbeserta alasannya.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01317pESAnup3pKqMNMfBi6r\n\n* ci(dto-drift): izinkan cermin FE `Delegation` = BE `DelegationView` (flatten) dengan alasan tertulis\n\nGuard tidak mengikuti #[serde(flatten)] di sisi backend, sehingga `berlaku` dan\n`catatan_berlaku` (ditambahkan DelegationView) terbaca ALWAYS-EMPTY. Dua field itu\nmemang dikirim server; allowlist memuat alasannya dan struct FE mendokumentasikan\nbahwa ia mencerminkan seluruh objek wire.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01317pESAnup3pKqMNMfBi6r\n\n* fix(ci): klasifikasi TLS tidak boleh membuat pemeriksaan yang LULUS menjadi merah\n\nAkar masalah cargo-deny merah di setiap commit sejak e36050a: TLS_INTEGRITY_RE\ndiperiksa sebelum return code dan memuat kata `schannel` telanjang. cargo-deny\nmencetak seluruh pohon dependensi, yang memuat crate `schannel v0.1.x` (dependensi\nnative-tls) — sehingga proses yang keluar 0 diklasifikasikan \"verifikasi sertifikat\nTLS gagal\" (RED). Direproduksi lokal dengan cargo-deny 0.20.2 yang sama: exit 0,\nwrapper RED sebelum perbaikan, GREEN sesudahnya.\n\n- Klasifikasi TLS hanya untuk proses yang gagal (non-nol atau timeout).\n- `schannel` telanjang diganti pola kegagalan sungguhan (`schannel: `, SEC_E_*).\n- Self-test +3 kasus: nama crate `schannel` + exit 0 = GREEN; nama crate saja tidak\n  mengubah kegagalan jaringan menjadi RED; kegagalan SChannel sungguhan tetap RED.\n- docs/audit-pr-930.md: baris kosong di sekitar heading (MD022, gagal di Lint Markdown)\n  dan catatan koreksi C2.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01317pESAnup3pKqMNMfBi6r\n\n* fix(authenc): clippy unnecessary_get_then_check pada test refresh-token role aktif\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01317pESAnup3pKqMNMfBi6r\n\n* test(e2e): gerbang /admin perlengkapan = admin saja; validator_pusat kini 403\n\nSpec masih menegaskan perilaku lama (require_admin = peran lintas-satker, sehingga\nvalidator_pusat mendapat 200). Backend sengaja diubah: require_admin memakai peran\n`admin` persis (lib_core::authz), selaras dengan gerbang FE `/admin`. Seluruh peran\nbisnis di seed CI kini 403; seed CI tak punya user `admin`, sisi positifnya dicakup\nunit test Claims::require_admin.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01317pESAnup3pKqMNMfBi6r\n\n* test(e2e): pulihkan sisi positif gerbang /admin + luruskan komentar basi\n\nPemeriksaan e2e `rbac-scoping.spec.ts` menegaskan validator_pusat mendapat 200\ndi `/admin/master` — perilaku lama sebelum gerbang backend dipersempit menjadi\n`Capability::Administer` (`lib_core::authz::ADMIN_ROLES`). Perilaku baru itu\nsengaja, jadi spesifikasi harus mengikutinya, bukan sebaliknya.\n\nSpec kini menyatakan matriks penuh: setiap peran bisnis (validator_pusat\ntermasuk) ditolak 403, dan identitas `admin` diterima 200.\n\nKomentar pendamping sebelumnya mengklaim \"seed CI tak punya user admin\" — itu\nkeliru. `tests/fixtures/e2e/seed-multisatker.sql` tidak menambah admin, tetapi\nseed authenc (`002_seed.sql:985`) memberi user seed semua-peran\n(199203142014031001) role `admin`, dan `tokenFor(\"admin\")` memang memakai\nidentitas itu. Karena itu sisi positifnya bisa di-assert di sini, bukan\ndiserahkan ke unit test seperti yang dikatakan komentar lama — dan memang\ndi-assert, supaya gerbang tak diam-diam menjadi \"tolak semua\".\n\nKomentar basi yang menyebut `require_admin = is_cross_satker_role` di\n`helpers/real-auth.ts` dan `admin/templates.rs` ikut diluruskan agar tidak\nmengajak pembaca menyimpulkan aturan otorisasi yang sudah tidak berlaku.\n\nCo-authored-by: openhands <openhands@all-hands.dev>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: openhands <openhands@all-hands.dev>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAA