mY4OGQzZjhiZjllMjVkZmIzN2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/39f1b3a5eb3177f3f6ab839d22e77bcccb1c8f22","sha":"39f1b3a5eb3177f3f6ab839d22e77bcccb1c8f22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/39f1b3a5eb3177f3f6ab839d22e77bcccb1c8f22"}],"sha":"b2626f3f558513ab45dc2f88d3f8bf9e25dfb37a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/b2626f3f558513ab45dc2f88d3f8bf9e25dfb37a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/220909633?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan","id":220909633,"login":"analisaperlengkapan","node_id":"U_kgDODSrQQQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/39f1b3a5eb3177f3f6ab839d22e77bcccb1c8f22/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T03:02:44Z","email":"analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com","name":"analisaperlengkapan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T03:02:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(perlengkapan): the SK''s photo box was an empty rectangle with a URL under it (#905)\n\nPage 1 of the SK izin pemakaian BMN is specified to carry the employee''s\nphoto. What it drew was a 35x45 mm empty rectangle labelled \"FOTO\" with the\nsource URL printed underneath as body text — an internal address on a formal\ndecision letter, which is not only useless to its reader but a leak.\n\nThe code said this was a printpdf 0.7 limitation. printpdf has been 0.12 in\nthis workspace since #898, and 0.12 embeds images. The comment outlived the\nconstraint it described.\n\nThree things had to exist first.\n\n**A way in.** perlengkapan cannot fetch the photo. `layanan-integrasi-egress`\nis the only NetworkPolicy in the namespace opening `0.0.0.0/0:443`; every other\npod is egress-restricted because `allow-dns-egress` uses `podSelector: {}`. The\ntwo frontends get away with building the URL because the fetch is done by the\nUSER''S BROWSER, not by a pod. The SK is rendered server-side, so there is no\nbrowser to hand a URL to. Hence `GetPegawaiFoto`, and hence the rule now\nwritten into `layanan/integrasi/AGENTS.md`: anything that needs the internet\ngoes through integrasi as an RPC, because `reqwest` anywhere else compiles,\npasses compose, and then sits in staging as a silent TCP timeout.\n\nThe RPC distinguishes \"no photo on record\" (`found: false`) from \"could not be\nfetched\" (a gRPC status). Collapsing them would make a dead media host look\nexactly like an employee who never uploaded a photo — on the page both are an\nempty box. It also refuses to be an existence oracle: an unknown NIP and a\nknown NIP with no photo answer identically.\n\n**A way to draw.** `PdfBuilder::image` scales to FIT, never to fill: a pasfoto\nstretched to a fixed 35x45 box distorts the face on the document whose purpose\nis to identify the person. Images cannot be registered when they are drawn —\n`add_image` lives on `PdfDocument`, which `finish` builds — so the op carries a\nplaceholder id that `finish` swaps out, and a placeholder that never got an\nimage is an error rather than a dangling reference that renders as blank space.\n\n`jpeg` and `png` are NOT printpdf default features. Without them\n`decode_from_bytes` still COMPILES, as a stub that always returns Err — so\ndropping them would restore the empty box with a green build. Proven both\nways: removing the features makes `png_benar_benar_ter_decode` fail with\n\"requires the ''images'' feature\".\n\n**One URL builder, not two.** `foto_pegawai_url` moved from `lib-ui` to\n`lib-core`, which integrasi already depends on; a backend service cannot depend\non a Leptos crate, and a second hand-rolled percent-encoder in integrasi is\nexactly the two-sided drift this repo keeps paying for. `lib-ui` re-exports it,\nso every existing caller is unchanged.\n\nThe photo is resolved from the NIP, not read off `permit.foto_pegawai`. That\ncolumn holds a file NAME the frontend sent at creation time, and a name is not\na snapshot — it points at a mutable remote object, so it is neither current\ndata nor preserved evidence.\n\nTwo guards were wrong, and both were mine.\n\n`check-proto-copies-agree.py` protected string literals from comment-stripping\nby finding every quoted run in the file — including quotes INSIDE comments. A\ncomment reading `// False means \"no photo on record\"` opened a fake literal and\nleaked its own text into the comparison, so two correctly-generated copies\nreported as disagreeing. That is the fourth time a comment has been read as\ncode in this repo. Replaced with a character scan, which cannot make the\nmistake: a quote inside a comment is reached in the comment state. Six canaries\nplus a \"the copies as committed still pass\" case, wired as `--self-test`.\n\n`check-csp-allows-referenced-hosts.py` named `lib/ui/src/components/foto_pegawai.rs`\nliterally, so moving that one file killed the guard — a correct scope with a\nhand-written list that did not move with it, one level deeper than the failure\nthe guard exists to catch. The source files are now globbed, and an empty scan\nexits 2.\n\nTests assert the photo reaches the bytes by SIZE DIFFERENCE against the same SK\nrendered without one, not by \"the call returned Ok\" — a render that silently\ndropped the image would return Ok and produce a valid PDF, which is the exact\nfailure being fixed.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019zMeXt2VAqLqnTwparBntq\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b48e139fd46a60fed77ff2378d361645fd81f23b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/trees/b48e139fd46a60fed77ff2378d361645fd81f23b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/commits/39f1b3a5eb3177f3f6ab839d22e77bcccb1c8f22","verification":{"payload":"tree b48e139fd46a60fed77ff2378d361645fd81f23b\nparent ea8ca39401bf61a2653bf1c4d7a3160be4286f0f\nauthor analisaperlengkapan <analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com> 1789700564 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789700564 +0700\n\nfeat(perlengkapan): the SK''s photo box was an empty rectangle with a URL under it (#905)\n\nPage 1 of the SK izin pemakaian BMN is specified to carry the employee''s\nphoto. What it drew was a 35x45 mm empty rectangle labelled \"FOTO\" with the\nsource URL printed underneath as body text — an internal address on a formal\ndecision letter, which is not only useless to its reader but a leak.\n\nThe code said this was a printpdf 0.7 limitation. printpdf has been 0.12 in\nthis workspace since #898, and 0.12 embeds images. The comment outlived the\nconstraint it described.\n\nThree things had to exist first.\n\n**A way in.** perlengkapan cannot fetch the photo. `layanan-integrasi-egress`\nis the only NetworkPolicy in the namespace opening `0.0.0.0/0:443`; every other\npod is egress-restricted because `allow-dns-egress` uses `podSelector: {}`. The\ntwo frontends get away with building the URL because the fetch is done by the\nUSER''S BROWSER, not by a pod. The SK is rendered server-side, so there is no\nbrowser to hand a URL to. Hence `GetPegawaiFoto`, and hence the rule now\nwritten into `layanan/integrasi/AGENTS.md`: anything that needs the internet\ngoes through integrasi as an RPC, because `reqwest` anywhere else compiles,\npasses compose, and then sits in staging as a silent TCP timeout.\n\nThe RPC distinguishes \"no photo on record\" (`found: false`) from \"could not be\nfetched\" (a gRPC status). Collapsing them would make a dead media host look\nexactly like an employee who never uploaded a photo — on the page both are an\nempty box. It also refuses to be an existence oracle: an unknown NIP and a\nknown NIP with no photo answer identically.\n\n**A way to draw.** `PdfBuilder::image` scales to FIT, never to fill: a pasfoto\nstretched to a fixed 35x45 box distorts the face on the document whose purpose\nis to identify the person. Images cannot be registered when they are drawn —\n`add_image` lives on `PdfDocument`, which `finish` builds — so the op carries a\nplaceholder id that `finish` swaps out, and a placeholder that never got an\nimage is an error rather than a dangling reference that renders as blank space.\n\n`jpeg` and `png` are NOT printpdf default features. Without them\n`decode_from_bytes` still COMPILES, as a stub that always returns Err — so\ndropping them would restore the empty box with a green build. Proven both\nways: removing the features makes `png_benar_benar_ter_decode` fail with\n\"requires the ''images'' feature\".\n\n**One URL builder, not two.** `foto_pegawai_url` moved from `lib-ui` to\n`lib-core`, which integrasi already depends on; a backend service cannot depend\non a Leptos crate, and a second hand-rolled percent-encoder in integrasi is\nexactly the two-sided drift this repo keeps paying for. `lib-ui` re-exports it,\nso every existing caller is unchanged.\n\nThe photo is resolved from the NIP, not read off `permit.foto_pegawai`. That\ncolumn holds a file NAME the frontend sent at creation time, and a name is not\na snapshot — it points at a mutable remote object, so it is neither current\ndata nor preserved evidence.\n\nTwo guards were wrong, and both were mine.\n\n`check-proto-copies-agree.py` protected string literals from comment-stripping\nby finding every quoted run in the file — including quotes INSIDE comments. A\ncomment reading `// False means \"no photo on record\"` opened a fake literal and\nleaked its own text into the comparison, so two correctly-generated copies\nreported as disagreeing. That is the fourth time a comment has been read as\ncode in this repo. Replaced with a character scan, which cannot make the\nmistake: a quote inside a comment is reached in the comment state. Six canaries\nplus a \"the copies as committed still pass\" case, wired as `--self-test`.\n\n`check-csp-allows-referenced-hosts.py` named `lib/ui/src/components/foto_pegawai.rs`\nliterally, so moving that one file killed the guard — a correct scope with a\nhand-written list that did not move with it, one level deeper than the failure\nthe guard exists to catch. The source files are now globbed, and an empty scan\nexits 2.\n\nTests assert the photo reaches the bytes by SIZE DIFFERENCE against the same SK\nrendered without one, not by \"the call returned Ok\" — a render that silently\ndropped the image would return Ok and produce a valid PDF, which is the exact\nfailure being fixed.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019zMeXt2VAqLqnTwparBntq\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrKnUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgxAQAI1UAkesbOErQedSMLXl4u61\ntD7jUaRibKn8nfnTmlICqATUn81NNClUuq9zhkBt6DSFSN26galpWMTzqyZMEQrh\nH+lwgY5SiVigSmjLfaWmymlx8M+Ek051mm1uh547a10eOnZQVkRp5Oumsy5XeKnP\nTlW/hqs606tnj1t4POld76cW2GHNTBZgusAh+Bttr8bjgDeaDU9fKbiGrhfMhq6H\nSR5AVECVVhB6RWNmRBhUhxFudokAd7GT9f1CTvaGQMrVtcW+f87Wh+078BbrFaqg\nywafPARrQU/3vFb7oTjVNKg7DnE7ViaATYrZdqr1B4Rgo5HNQ4f3OytPWB2jpE65\nX1OyBglRTk3XQ5jsPy9f0N2zOvNkMdJ9I76RV5YI7YH9qppY