s{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan","id":220909633,"login":"analisaperlengkapan","node_id":"U_kgDODSrQQQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/f21354a8975696576af3f87c791cce2672452702/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T09:39:10Z","email":"analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com","name":"analisaperlengkapan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T09:39:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(perlengkapan): pakaian dinas could not be started by anyone (#901)\n\n* feat(perlengkapan): pakaian dinas could not be started by anyone\n\nA pengajuan pakaian dinas requires at least one spesifikasi — the form refuses\nan empty selection, and a campaign with no pakaian has no size columns to fill.\nNothing in either frontend could create one: the backend''s POST/PUT/DELETE for\n`/pakaian-dinas/spesifikasi` and `/subspesifikasi` had ZERO callers anywhere in\nthe repo. Staging shows what that produced: 8 jenis, 0 spesifikasi, 0\nsubspesifikasi. The whole workflow''s entry point was missing, and the approval\ntail behind it — which does work — had nothing to approve.\n\nThe page at `/pakaian-dinas/jenis/:id/spesifikasi` now writes as well as reads.\nEach row opens a drawer for its subspesifikasi, the gendered variants\n(\"Lengan Pendek - L\", \"Celana Wanita\") that decide which size boxes a person is\nshown later. Ukuran group and gender are picked from the closed lists the\nserver validates against (`services.rs` rejects anything else with 400), so\nneither is typed. Both levels are `require_admin` on the server, so the write\ncontrols are hidden from everyone else rather than offered and then refused —\nthe audit found \"Tambah Jenis\" and \"Buat Pengajuan\" shown to all seven roles.\n\nV011 carries the reference rows themselves. They are not invented: 7\nspesifikasi and 3 subspesifikasi lifted from `dbsimpelv1.sql.gz`, authored by\n\"Superadmin\" between 2023-07-31 and 2023-08-31 and still amended 2024-06-24.\nv1 ids are text, v2 ids are uuid, so the mapping goes through jenis NAME. The\njenis `PDU-I 2023` exists only in v1 and is restored; the four jenis v2 has\nthat v1 does not (Batik, Jas Almamater, Toga Jaksa, Toga TU) are left alone —\ndeleting data someone may have entered is not a seed migration''s business.\n\nVerified against a real Postgres, not reasoned about:\n\n    pass 1   4 jenis -> 5 jenis, 7 spesifikasi, 3 subspesifikasi\n    pass 2   5 jenis,   7 spesifikasi, 3 subspesifikasi     (idempotent)\n    canary   a row an admin had edited (\"  pakaian dinas \", deskripsi\n             \"diubah admin\") is neither duplicated nor overwritten\n\n`components/layout/data_table.rs` goes with it. It had exactly one consumer —\nthe list-only page this replaces — and `lib/ui` already carries the shared\n`data_table_v2`. A second, now-callerless copy is how dead code accumulates,\nso it is deleted rather than its warning silenced.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WQ99i4hsHtgtPr4pHRk6Vn\n\n* fix(perlengkapan): pressing Simpan twice made two identical size columns\n\nFound by making the mistake: driving the new spesifikasi page against staging\nleft \"Celana\", \"Pakaian Dinas\" and \"Sepatu Dinas\" recorded three times each,\nand \"Lengan Pendek - L/P\" twice each. Nothing objected — not the API, not the\ndatabase, which carries no unique key on either table.\n\nA duplicate is not cosmetic here. Every spesifikasi becomes one size column on\nthe satker''s filling form, so a duplicate asks the operator for the same\nmeasurement twice; and the report resolves sizes with\n`MAX(CASE WHEN pp.spesifikasi_ukuran_group = ''BAJU'' THEN pu.ukuran END)`, which\nsilently picks one of the two without saying which.\n\nCreation now refuses a name already used under the same parent, matched\ncase- and whitespace-insensitively so \" celana \" cannot slip past \"Celana\" —\nthe same comparison V011''s seed guard uses.\n\nA unique index belongs underneath this, but adding one is a data migration:\nany environment already holding duplicates would have to be de-duplicated\nfirst, and a duplicate referenced by an existing campaign cannot simply be\ndeleted. That is left as its own change rather than smuggled in here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WQ99i4hsHtgtPr4pHRk6Vn\n\n* fix(perlengkapan): every label in perlengkapan pointed at nothing\n\n`FormField` renders `<label>` with no `for`, and puts the control in a sibling\n`<div>`. Nothing associates the two. Clicking a label does not focus its field,\nassistive technology announces the input as unlabelled, and `getByLabel(...)`\nfinds nothing — which is how this surfaced: the screenshot run driving the new\nspesifikasi form timed out waiting for a label that resolves to no control, and\nthe e2e tests written against it would have failed the same way in CI.\n\nThe fix has to be opt-in rather than automatic. Wrapping the children in the\nlabel would associate them implicitly and need no ids, but several callers\nmount a GROUP of controls that each carry their own `<label>` — the spesifikasi\ncheckboxes on the campaign form — and nested labels are invalid HTML that bind\nto the wrong control. So `FormField` gains `for_id`, and the fields on the new\npage carry matching ids.\n\nThe subspesifikasi ids are per-spesifikasi (`sub-nama-{id}`), because more than\none drawer can be open in the same document and duplicate ids would point every\nlabel at the first one.\n\nThis closes the gap for the fields added here. The rest of perlengkapan''s\nfields are still unassociated; that is a wider accessibility debt than this\nchange, recorded rather than half-fixed in passing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WQ99i4hsHtgtPr4pHRk6Vn\n\n* fix(perlengkapan): a column that can never hold anything is not a column\n\nThe read-only view of the spesifikasi table still carried an \"Aksi\" header and\nan empty cell in every row, because only the button inside was hidden from\nnon-admins. The column goes with the actions now, and the subspesifikasi\ndrawer''s colspan follows the real column count.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WQ99i4hsHtgtPr4pHRk6Vn\n\n* fix(perlengkapan): the spesifikasi filter was reading a name nobody sent\n\n`GET /pakaian-dinas/spesifikasi` narrows the list by jenis. The backend\ncalled that query parameter `jenis_id`; both frontend callers have always\nsent `jenis_pakaian_dinas_id` — the name of the column, and of the field in\nthe create DTO. serde drops query keys it does not know, so the filter\ndeserialised to `None` on every request and the endpoint answered 200 with\nEVERY jenis''s rows:\n\n  - the master drawer listed other jenis''s spesifikasi under the one being\n    edited,\n  - the campaign form''s picker offered Toga and Batik rows while the operator\n    had PDH selected — and a campaign freezes whatever is picked.\n\nNothing could see it. The status is 200, the JSON envelope is correct, and\nthe two names live in different crates that never meet at a type boundary, so\n`cargo check` cannot compare them. Renamed the backend field to the name the\nfrontend sends; nothing anywhere sent `jenis_id`, so nothing breaks.\n\nThe test asserts the FILTER, not the name — a rename alone would satisfy a\nname check while the filter stayed dead. It creates two jenis with one\nspesifikasi each and requires the response to carry one and not the other.\nReverting the field name makes it fail with the other jenis''s rows listed.\n\nGuard: `check-fe-query-params-reach-backend.py` derives every query key the\nbackend can read (structs behind a `Query<...>` extractor, following\n`serde(flatten)` and `rename`) and every parameter name the frontend builds\ninto a URL, and fails on a frontend parameter no handler reads. It fails on\nthis exact bug and passes on the fix; it exits 2 if either derivation comes\nback empty, so a broken scan cannot read as a clean one.\n\nAlso fixes the two ways this PR''s own e2e spec was broken, both mechanical:\n\n  - it carried its own `TEST_USERS.find` lookup, and `admin` is deliberately\n    not in that table — the shared helper''s docstring already records this\n    breaking twice before, so this was the third copy;\n  - `apiLogin` resolves to `{ accessToken, refreshToken }`, so\n    `Bearer ${token}` sent the literal `Bearer [object Object]` and the\n    backend answered 401.\n\nBoth disappear by using the shared `tokenFor`, which returns a string and\nknows about `admin`. The failures surfaced as `Cannot read properties of\nundefined (reading ''find'')` rather than the 401, because the spec read `.data`\noff an unchecked response; list reads now go through a helper that asserts the\nstatus and prints the body.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WQ99i4hsHtgtPr4pHRk6Vn\n\n* docs(antarmuka): the query direction was documented as the safe one\n\n`antarmuka/AGENTS.md` told every reader that the `Request`/`Query` direction\nof FE↔BE drift is safe, because \"FE selalu mengirim nilai\", and that only the\nresponse direction is dangerous. The spesifikasi filter disproved it: serde\nDROPS unknown query keys, so a misnamed parameter produces no 400, no\ndeserialise error, and no signal at all — just a 200 with the filter ignored.\nThat is quieter than the response direction, which at least breaks loudly.\n\nReplaces the claim with the rule and the guard, records the incident, and\nnotes what the guard does not check and why a wrong derivation would be worse\nthan none. Also names the existing DTO guard, which the file never mentioned.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WQ99i4hsHtgtPr4pHRk6Vn\n\n* fix(ci): the new query-param guard covered one of the two frontends\n\nIts frontend scan was scoped to `antarmuka/*/src/api/*.rs`. Portal has no\nsuch directory — its clients live in `src/utils/authenc_api.rs` — so the\nguard covered perlengkapan and left every portal query parameter unwatched.\nThat is the hand-written-scope failure the guard exists to prevent, committed\ninside the guard itself.\n\nIt now scans the whole frontend tree. Two measurements from widening it:\n\n  - 32 parameter names before, 37 after. Three perlengkapan api modules\n    (`workflow.rs`, `dokumen.rs`, `dashboard.rs`) build their paths through a\n    helper and never spell `/api/` themselves, so an attempt to keep the scan\n    cheap by skipping files without `/api/` silently dropped six more names.\n    Removed; there is no file filter.\n\n  - A FORM BODY is indistinguishable from a query string by shape.\n    `\"grant_type=authorization_code&code={}&...\"` is posted\n    `x-www-form-urlencoded` by the OAuth token exchange, and reading it as\n    query parameters made the guard demand an allowlist entry for correct\n    code. A literal now counts only when it contains `?` or begins with `&` —\n    the append form, which is how the spesifikasi filter was sent, so the\n    guard still fails on the bug it was written for.\n\nCanaries, all re-measured: reverting the field name fails (1); either\nderivation coming back empty fails (2); the form body''s fields are absent from\nthe scan; the appended `&jenis_pakaian_dinas_id=` is present; portal files\nappear in the results.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WQ99i4hsHtgtPr4pHRk6Vn\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ce76751d12aef4b9efe542c9639d7b5e9ef5e5b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/trees/ce76751d12aef4b9efe542c9639d7b5e9ef5e5b6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/commits/f21354a8975696576af3f87c791cce2672452702","verification":{"payload":"tree ce76751d12aef4b9efe542c9639d7b5e9ef5e5b6\nparent 623d7cf2501642b57bcb7d7be55b2d274785b207\nauthor analisaperlengkapan <analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com> 1788169150 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788169150 +0700\n\nfeat(perlengkapan): pakaian dinas could not be started by anyone (#901)\n\n* feat(perlengkapan): pakaian dinas could not be started by anyone\n\nA pengajuan pakaian dinas requires at least one spesifikasi — the form refuses\nan empty selection, and a campaign with no pakaian has no size columns to fill.\nNothing in either frontend could create one: the backend''s POST/PUT/DELETE for\n`/pakaian-dinas/spesifikasi` and `/subspesifikasi` had ZERO callers anywhere in\nthe repo. Staging shows what that produced: 8 jenis, 0 spesifikasi, 0\nsubspesifikasi. The whole workflow''s entry point was missing, and the approval\ntail behind it — which does work — had nothing to approve.\n\nThe page at `/pakaian-dinas/jenis/:id/spesifikasi` now writes as well as reads.\nEach row opens a drawer for its subspesifikasi, the gendered variants\n(\"Lengan Pendek - L\", \"Celana Wanita\") that decide which size boxes a person is\nshown later. Ukuran group and gender are picked from the closed lists the\nserver validates against (`services.rs` rejects anything else with 400), so\nneither is typed. Both levels are `require_admin` on the server, so the write\ncontrols are hidden from everyone else rather than offered and then refused —\nthe audit found \"Tambah Jenis\" and \"Buat Pengajuan\" shown to all seven roles.\n\nV011 carries the reference rows themselves. They are not invented: 7\nspesifikasi and 3 subspesifikasi lifted from `dbsimpelv1.sql.gz`, authored by\n\"Superadmin\" between 2023-07-31 and 2023-08-31 and still amended 2024-06-24.\nv1 ids are text, v2 ids are uuid, so the mapping goes through jenis NAME. The\njenis `PDU-I 2023` exists only in v1 and is restored; the four jenis v2 has\nthat v1 does not (Batik, Jas Almamater, Toga Jaksa, Toga TU) are left alone —\ndeleting data someone may have entered is not a seed migration''s business.\n\nVerified against a real Postgres, not reasoned about:\n\n    pass 1   4 jenis -> 5 jenis, 7 spesifikasi, 3 subspesifikasi\n    pass 2   5 jenis,   7 spesifikasi, 3 subspesifikasi     (idempotent)\n    canary   a row an admin had edited (\"  pakaian dinas \", deskripsi\n             \"diubah admin\") is neither duplicated nor overwritten\n\n`components/layout/data_table.rs` goes with it. It had exactly one consumer —\nthe list-only page this replaces — and `lib/ui` already carries the shared\n`data_table_v2`. A second, now-callerless copy is how dead code accumulates,\nso it is deleted rather than its warning silenced.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WQ99i4hsHtgtPr4pHRk6Vn\n\n* fix(perlengkapan): pressing Simpan twice made two identical size columns\n\nFound by making the mistake: driving the new spesifikasi page against staging\nleft \"Celana\", \"Pakaian Dinas\" and \"Sepatu Dinas\" recorded three times each,\nand \"Lengan Pendek - L/P\" twice each. Nothing objected — not the API, not the\ndatabase, which carries no unique key on either table.\n\nA duplicate is not cosmetic here. Every spesifikasi becomes one size column on\nthe satker''s filling form, so a duplicate asks the operator for the same\nmeasurement twice; and the report resolves sizes with\n`MAX(CASE WHEN pp.spesifikasi_ukuran_group = ''BAJU'' THEN pu.ukuran END)`, which\nsilently picks one of the two without saying which.\n\nCreation now refuses a name already used under the same parent, matched\ncase- and whitespace-insensitively so \" celana \" cannot slip past \"Celana\" —\nthe same comparison V011''s seed guard uses.\n\nA unique index belongs underneath this, but adding one is a data migration:\nany environment already holding duplicates would have to be de-duplicated\nfirst, and a duplicate referenced by an existing campaign cannot simply be\ndeleted. That is left as its own change rather than smuggled in here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WQ99i4hsHtgtPr4pHRk6Vn\n\n* fix(perlengkapan): every label in perlengkapan pointed at nothing\n\n`FormField` renders `<label>` with no `for`, and puts the control in a sibling\n`<div>`. Nothing associates the two. Clicking a label does not focus its field,\nassistive technology announces the input as unlabelled, and `getByLabel(...)`\nfinds nothing — which is how this surfaced: the screenshot run driving the new\nspesifikasi form timed out waiting for a label that resolves to no control, and\nthe e2e tests written against it would have failed the same way in CI.\n\nThe fix has to be opt-in rather than automatic. Wrapping the children in the\nlabel would associate them implicitly and need no ids, but several callers\nmount a GROUP of controls that each carry their own `<label>` — the spesifikasi\ncheckboxes on the campaign form — and nested labels are invalid HTML that bind\nto the wrong control. So `FormField` gains `for_id`, and the fields on the new\npage carry matching ids.\n\nThe subspesifikasi ids are per-spesifikasi (`sub-nama-{id}`), because more than\none drawer can be open in the same document and duplicate ids would point every\nlabel at the first one.\n\nThis closes the gap for the fields added here. The rest of perlengkapan''s\nfields are still unassociated; that is a wider accessibility debt than this\nchange, recorded rather than half-fixed in passing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WQ99i4hsHtgtPr4pHRk6Vn\n\n* fix(perlengkapan): a column that can never hold anything is not a column\n\nThe read-only view of the spesifikasi table still carried an \"Aksi\" header and\nan empty cell in every row, because only the button inside was hidden from\nnon-admins. The column goes with the actions now, and the subspesifikasi\ndrawer''s colspan follows the real column count.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WQ99i4hsHtgtPr4pHRk6Vn\n\n* fix(perlengkapan): the spesifikasi filter was reading a name nobody sent\n\n`GET /pakaian-dinas/spesifikasi` narrows the list by jenis. The backend\ncalled that query parameter `jenis_id`; both frontend callers have always\nsent `jenis_pakaian_dinas_id` — the name of the column, and of the field in\nthe create DTO. serde drops query keys it does not know, so the filter\ndeserialised to `None` on every request and the endpoint answered 200 with\nEVERY jenis''s rows:\n\n  - the master drawer listed other jenis''s spesifikasi under the one being\n    edited,\n  - the campaign form''s picker offered Toga and Batik rows while the operator\n    had PDH selected — and a campaign freezes whatever is picked.\n\nNothing could see it. The status is 200, the JSON envelope is correct, and\nthe two names live in different crates that never meet at a type boundary, so\n`cargo check` cannot compare them. Renamed the backend field to the name the\nfrontend sends; nothing anywhere sent `jenis_id`, so nothing breaks.\n\nThe test asserts the FILTER, not the name — a rename alone would satisfy a\nname check while the filter stayed dead. It creates two jenis with one\nspesifikasi each and requires the response to carry one and not the other.\nReverting the field name makes it fail with the other jenis''s rows listed.\n\nGuard: `check-fe-query-params-reach-backend.py` derives every query key the\nbackend can read (structs behind a `Query<...>` extractor, following\n`serde(flatten)` and `rename`) and every parameter name the frontend builds\ninto a URL, and fails on a frontend parameter no handler reads. It fails on\nthis exact bug and passes on the fix; it exits 2 if either derivation comes\nback empty, so a broken scan cannot read as a clean one.\n\nAlso fixes the two ways this PR''s own e2e spec was broken, both mechanical:\n\n  - it carried its own `TEST_USERS.find` lookup, and `admin` is deliberately\n    not in that table — the shared helper''s docstring already records this\n    breaking twice before, so this was the third copy;\n  - `apiLogin` resolves to `{ accessToken, refreshToken }`, so\n    `Bearer ${token}` sent the literal `Bearer [object Object]` and the\n    backend answered 401.\n\nBoth disappear by using the shared `tokenFor`, which returns a string and\nknows about `admin`. The failures surfaced as `Cannot read properties of\nundefined (reading ''find'')` rather than the 401, because the spec read `.data`\noff an unchecked response; list reads now go through a helper that asserts the\nstatus and prints the body.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WQ99i4hsHtgtPr4pHRk6Vn\n\n* docs(antarmuka): the query direction was documented as the safe one\n\n`antarmuka/AGENTS.md` told every reader that the `Request`/`Query` direction\nof FE↔BE drift is safe, because \"FE selalu mengirim nilai\", and that only the\nresponse direction is dangerous. The spesifikasi filter disproved it: serde\nDROPS unknown query keys, so a misnamed parameter produces no 400, no\ndeserialise error, and no signal at all — just a 200 with the filter ignored.\nThat is quieter than the response direction, which at least breaks loudly.\n\nReplaces the claim with the rule and the guard, records the incident, and\nnotes what the guard does not check and why a wrong derivation would be worse\nthan none. Also names the existing DTO guard, which the file never mentioned.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WQ99i4hsHtgtPr4pHRk6Vn\n\n* fix(ci): the new query-param guard covered one of the two frontends\n\nIts frontend scan was scoped to `antarmuka/*/src/api/*.rs`. Portal has no\nsuch directory — its clients live in `src/utils/authenc_api.rs` — so the\nguard covered perlengkapan and left every portal query parameter unwatched.\nThat is the hand-written-scope failure the guard exists to prevent, committed\ninside the guard itself.\n\nIt now scans the whole frontend tree. Two measurements from widening it:\n\n  - 32 parameter names before, 37 after. Three perlengkapan api modules\n    (`workflow.rs`, `dokumen.rs`, `dashboard.rs`) build their paths through a\n    helper and never spell `/api/` themselves, so an attempt to keep the scan\n    cheap by skipping files without `/api/` silently dropped six more names.\n    Removed; there is no file filter.\n\n  - A FORM BODY is indistinguishable from a query string by shape.\n    `\"grant_type=authorization_code&code={}&...\"` is posted\n    `x-www-form-urlencoded` by the OAuth token exchange, and reading it as\n    query parameters made the guard demand an allowlist entry for correct\n    code. A literal now counts only when it contains `?` or begins with `&` —\n    the append form, which is how the spesifikasi filter was sent, so the\n    guard still fails on the bug it was written for.\n\nCanaries, all re-measured: reverting the field name fails (1); either\nderivation coming back empty fails (2); the form body''s fields are absent from\nthe scan; the appended `&jenis_pakaian_dinas_id=` is present; portal files\nappear in the results.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WQ99i4hsHtgtPr4pHRk6Vn\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlUu+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhOkQAKsRga2ZDBSHk9zNFSJ/RBoY\n3/Nh3wm+ETygk7VcAewn8GP2zinqL0j83QCrQBlA3dkFVH4y6bwoxBu4TmK+VZaa\nvTDuXv9Z73cv8TTWd/2yOAuVQIBig6xMetN2AWz3tvrPARYaRqxsbVul0eGPRF0c\nU+Z41Vfa+w29DRKP3XFVMDZwogwSR/YBRrxXV9HYMBzTn9E19CQytXX0TaNC/tDz\nIxDkTU9swbeiWmtahbH5Kx55WiCbGC6JOVo3gba/nXuaZR4ptXCRQGxrbU9Y9AlT\nWhMdwTDhLBxBMtE6UgipZzY/QQGjsUdlLxb4D+an/AhvFPq8pQHyIz/mbR4rDXz8\nlrvWa+VC93L0qF34afx0Z9nl6o1qeRPZxWUEtmfq9FZor5+Eij3TRo30oRBq3YDC\nCKHZooA8wJWvVw7HTvY9YPbYZURcUdIunexQ/iQM3o+/HWooao4Lqd3AllmwYHS4\nDRoCYgnKCH9n/vPfGyIKzU0jSbEx6UnQflxkyZOD9vVGzkNdlpjDJGaw5/3M1T1o\n3t5cyak3RvbFtHtBYhnShAyNn1cbOvcYwKXgd50N47bMhK3FyEA3xmxpNUR2vNYB\nIuE0e9nip+srIHvSBv0aedwWm2Ho5Mbi3jlThiwUi8YpY/dDKLnsFwmgqA/gQ/jB\nsyuqiscfhZvWfwPEYr7S\n=2XBG\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T09:39:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/f21354a8975696576af3f87c791cce2672452702","node_id":"C_kwDOP93DxNoAKGYyMTM1NGE4OTc1Njk2NTc2YWYzZjg3Yzc5MWNjZTI2NzI0NTI3MDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/623d7cf2501642b57bcb7d7be55b2d274785b207","sha":"623d7cf2501642b57bcb7d7be55b2d274785b207","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/623d7cf2501642b57bcb7d7be55b2d274785b207"}],"sha":"f21354a8975696576af3f87c791cce2672452702","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/f21354a8975696576af3f87c791cce2672452702"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/220909633?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan","id":220909633,"login":"analisaperlengkapan","node_id":"U_kgDODSrQQQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/623d7cf2501642b57bcb7d7be55b2d274785b207/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T08:21:02Z","email":"analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com","name":"analisaperlengkapan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T08:21:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(perlengkapan): the pegawai photo was fetched, stored, and never shown (#903)\n\n`integrasi.mysimkari_pegawai.foto` has a column, the sync writes it\n(`storage.rs:274`), and the API returns it. The pemakaian form even reads it\ninto a signal — and then only sends it back to the server. There is not one\n`<img>` for a pegawai photo in either frontend; the only images are logos. The\ndata made the whole round trip without anybody seeing it.\n\nThe URL is `{media host}/{foto}`, and `foto` is a FILENAME, not a path: a\n32-character random prefix followed by whatever the original file was called.\nReal values from the v1 dump carry spaces, parentheses and repeated dots, so\npercent-encoding is not optional. Three of them were checked against the live\nhost and all return `200 image/jpeg` — after encoding. Pasting the filename\nraw produces a broken URL for most employees.\n\n`lib/ui`''s `Avatar` is reused rather than a fourth avatar written, but its\npalette had to be fixed first: it used `bg-primary`, and `primary` is defined\nin NEITHER tailwind config. The circle behind the initials was transparent\neverywhere — invisible only because the component had no callers at all.\n\n`PegawaiPicker` also had no `data-testid` of any kind, unlike `AsetPicker`, so\nnothing could address its identity card. It has one now.\n\nA CSP would have made all of this fail silently. Four different CSPs exist in\nthis repo, and the one that actually serves portal in the cluster\n(`configmaps/nginx.yaml`) reads `img-src ''self'' data:` — the media host is\nblocked with no error on screen, no failed request in any server log, just an\nimage that does not appear. `img-src` now comes from values the way\n`connect-src` already did, naming the host explicitly rather than opening\n`https:` wide.\n\n`check-csp-allows-referenced-hosts.py` keeps it that way. It DERIVES the host\nlist from the constants in `lib/ui` rather than restating it, because a\nhand-written list does not grow when a host is added. Tested in both\ndirections: host removed from values -> exit 1, constant removed from code ->\nexit 1 (it refuses to pass on an empty derivation), correct state -> exit 0.\nIts first version was wrong twice over — a `[^;\"'']` class that stopped at\n`''self''` and so accused two files that were already correct, and a single-line\nregex that found zero hosts the moment `cargo fmt` wrapped the constant.\n\nVerified against the deployed staging API: with no photo the card shows the\ninitials on a circle that is now actually visible; with a real MySIMKARI\nfilename the photo loads from the real host, 1103x1600, URL correctly encoded.\n`object-top` was tried for the crop and reverted — on a real portrait ID photo\nit shows the background above the head and cuts the face off the bottom, which\nthe screenshot showed and guesswork would not have.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WQ99i4hsHtgtPr4pHRk6Vn\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"feb76ea5a9f8dbb69985aca509d4211fece4f2ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/trees/feb76ea5a9f8dbb69985aca509d4211fece4f2ab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/commits/623d7cf2501642b57bcb7d7be55b2d274785b207","verification":{"payload":"tree feb76ea5a9f8dbb69985aca509d4211fece4f2ab\nparent 43abc96a5495b5aedb4a7d868f85ad7310181112\nauthor analisaperlengkapan <analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com> 1788164462 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788164462 +0700\n\nfeat(perlengkapan): the pegawai photo was fetched, stored, and never shown (#903)\n\n`integrasi.mysimkari_pegawai.foto` has a column, the sync writes it\n(`storage.rs:274`), and the API returns it. The pemakaian form even reads it\ninto a signal — and then only sends it back to the server. There is not one\n`<img>` for a pegawai photo in either frontend; the only images are logos. The\ndata made the whole round trip without anybody seeing it.\n\nThe URL is `{media host}/{foto}`, and `foto` is a FILENAME, not a path: a\n32-character random prefix followed by whatever the original file was called.\nReal values from the v1 dump carry spaces, parentheses and repeated dots, so\npercent-encoding is not optional. Three of them were checked against the live\nhost and all return `200 image/jpeg` — after encoding. Pasting the filename\nraw produces a broken URL for most employees.\n\n`lib/ui`''s `Avatar` is reused rather than a fourth avatar written, but its\npalette had to be fixed first: it used `bg-primary`, and `primary` is defined\nin NEITHER tailwind config. The circle behind the initials was transparent\neverywhere — invisible only because the component had no callers at all.\n\n`PegawaiPicker` also had no `data-testid` of any kind, unlike `AsetPicker`, so\nnothing could address its identity card. It has one now.\n\nA CSP would have made all of this fail silently. Four different CSPs exist in\nthis repo, and the one that actually serves portal in the cluster\n(`configmaps/nginx.yaml`) reads `img-src ''self'' data:` — the media host is\nblocked with no error on screen, no failed request in any server log, just an\nimage that does not appear. `img-src` now comes from values the way\n`connect-src` already did, naming the host explicitly rather than opening\n`https:` wide.\n\n`check-csp-allows-referenced-hosts.py` keeps it that way. It DERIVES the host\nlist from the constants in `lib/ui` rather than restating it, because a\nhand-written list does not grow when a host is added. Tested in both\ndirections: host removed from values -> exit 1, constant removed from code ->\nexit 1 (it refuses to pass on an empty derivation), correct state -> exit 0.\nIts first version was wrong twice over — a `[^;\"'']` class that stopped at\n`''self''` and so accused two files that were already correct, and a single-line\nregex that found zero hosts the moment `cargo fmt` wrapped the constant.\n\nVerified against the deployed staging API: with no photo the card shows the\ninitials on a circle that is now actually visible; with a real MySIMKARI\nfilename the photo loads from the real host, 1103x1600, URL correctly encoded.\n`object-top` was tried for the crop and reverted — on a real portrait ID photo\nit shows the background above the head and cuts the face off the bottom, which\nthe screenshot showed and guesswork would not have.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WQ99i4hsHtgtPr4pHRk6Vn\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlTluCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwR0QAIxuPWlNEUNlkJiCu5wVo1qC\nhec/pRbVB8LTOPPJCj9ZQ0w3Ak9cXLMt5eHgcCY7zOk+Nr5wZ2kuUbNk7d0kiwCo\nqQF5reu8sBn6dRrvClvh70HDkVWxX0crIA3dXbO4LJmYJuSXH35v0DpQsd/rGD4N\nwU1yxGlPNkoM+JfojcBqncNXn8Bo3+UyzAnXYM3zbMTrXawEFTTHo7qqkWW1q7Cu\nRXaY7mXsK7awIGW2T4H5q0umrwB3LTgNUvTR8pw1ZHWnrW7E3/ZyVNrQPunscywP\nwSrL8IwAhgM9qtEO35bn7yMpaskCfEUC/eAjO6SIqq0gJ1zKLHSuwdo/RhBeZn4C\nGT8XXX6dYK5ijZlFuuXPN4bjOQyj/LJQT6e7r7+U7cGNqFAZ6jTeLg+77mAdxMf/\nIwjQgXlwemSGdt3BL8wKA+GAuD9gWPJ+yrnj7L0NSb+gc9bZTsK76SCXfZ7+9ltw\nJHX6Lu4IxLUT4R/rckj2qmHCRZkksZfLQ+VdmqzGWiLWOOpDrTWR9nRBL4Mv+7dH\nV8FKScVOo7FpjmMyC72E7ZYPChnDmjN9wK8HU4vc5AtqXPcmqQ0uhqwxHIOxSj1w\nFma9QbOm1HKYBndD/X2Q6nRj0qMN3ythQg9a/1S+8EY0fqdGdH2JAunrgF29uin7\neIh4tG8flWCVdkrDnRUU\n=n9Ga\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T08:21:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/623d7cf2501642b57bcb7d7be55b2d274785b207","node_id":"C_kwDOP93DxNoAKDYyM2Q3Y2YyNTAxNjQyYjU3YmNiN2Q3YmU1NWIyZDI3NDc4NWIyMDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/43abc96a5495b5aedb4a7d868f85ad7310181112","sha":"43abc96a5495b5aedb4a7d868f85ad7310181112","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/43abc96a5495b5aedb4a7d868f85ad7310181112"}],"sha":"623d7cf2501642b57bcb7d7be55b2d274785b207","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/623d7cf2501642b57bcb7d7be55b2d274785b207"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/220909633?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan","id":220909633,"login":"analisaperlengkapan","node_id":"U_kgDODSrQQQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/43abc96a5495b5aedb4a7d868f85ad7310181112/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T06:55:06Z","email":"analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com","name":"analisaperlengkapan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T06:55:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(perlengkapan): the extra BMN rows still asked operators to type SIMAN (#900)\n\nThe main asset on both create forms is picked from SIMAN. The *extra* rows\nunder it were not: pemakaian asked for kode barang, nama barang and NUP as\nthree free-text boxes, penghapusan for those three plus a value. All of them\nsit in `integrasi.siman_aset`, so every row was a chance to mistype the one\nthing that identifies an asset.\n\nBoth now mount the same `AsetPicker` per row. `AsetPicker` gained an optional\n`slug` (and label): its ids and testids were hard-coded, so a second instance\non one page produced duplicate `id`s — the second row''s label would focus the\nfirst row''s box — and duplicate testids that fail Playwright''s strict mode.\nThe default keeps `aset-cari` / `aset-terpilih` / `aset-hasil` / `aset-kosong`,\nso no existing locator moves.\n\nKeying those rows by position was measurably wrong, not just untidy. Against\nthe old build: type AAA into row 0 and BBB into row 1 of the pemakaian form,\ndelete row 0, and the surviving row STILL SHOWS AAA while the payload carries\nBBB. Leptos reuses the DOM node when it rebuilds, and those inputs had no\n`prop:value`, so nothing overwrote the deleted row''s text — screen and payload\ndisagree with no error anywhere. Each row now owns an `RwSignal` and the list\nholds only a monotonic key, so `For` ties identity to the row.\n\nTwo things the operator could not previously supply now arrive on their own:\n\n- pemakaian extra rows hard-coded `bmn_merk`, `bmn_tahun_perolehan` and\n  `bmn_kondisi` to `None`, because the form had nowhere to enter them. The\n  picked row carries all three.\n- penghapusan extra rows keep only \"Nilai Perolehan\", pre-filled from SIMAN.\n  It stays editable on purpose: the server overrides `nilai_perolehan` from\n  SIMAN for the MAIN item only (`services.rs` create), so an extra item whose\n  asset carries no figure still needs somewhere to put one. Blank stays blank\n  rather than becoming 0 — a zero here would travel into the SK.\n\nVerified against the deployed staging API, not a mock: searching \"station\nwagon\" as operator_a returns one row and fills kode 3020101003, NUP 1, merk\n\"Innova 2.4 G M/T Dsl Vin 2022\", kondisi Baik, nilai 391559057.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WQ99i4hsHtgtPr4pHRk6Vn\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"43db9b4b3adbcdcc1a96876a35e9f65c8b48dac3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/trees/43db9b4b3adbcdcc1a96876a35e9f65c8b48dac3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/commits/43abc96a5495b5aedb4a7d868f85ad7310181112","verification":{"payload":"tree 43db9b4b3adbcdcc1a96876a35e9f65c8b48dac3\nparent 484a9c33057aea9803638526db0c1ec8120394b6\nauthor analisaperlengkapan <analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com> 1788159306 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788159306 +0700\n\nfeat(perlengkapan): the extra BMN rows still asked operators to type SIMAN (#900)\n\nThe main asset on both create forms is picked from SIMAN. The *extra* rows\nunder it were not: pemakaian asked for kode barang, nama barang and NUP as\nthree free-text boxes, penghapusan for those three plus a value. All of them\nsit in `integrasi.siman_aset`, so every row was a chance to mistype the one\nthing that identifies an asset.\n\nBoth now mount the same `AsetPicker` per row. `AsetPicker` gained an optional\n`slug` (and label): its ids and testids were hard-coded, so a second instance\non one page produced duplicate `id`s — the second row''s label would focus the\nfirst row''s box — and duplicate testids that fail Playwright''s strict mode.\nThe default keeps `aset-cari` / `aset-terpilih` / `aset-hasil` / `aset-kosong`,\nso no existing locator moves.\n\nKeying those rows by position was measurably wrong, not just untidy. Against\nthe old build: type AAA into row 0 and BBB into row 1 of the pemakaian form,\ndelete row 0, and the surviving row STILL SHOWS AAA while the payload carries\nBBB. Leptos reuses the DOM node when it rebuilds, and those inputs had no\n`prop:value`, so nothing overwrote the deleted row''s text — screen and payload\ndisagree with no error anywhere. Each row now owns an `RwSignal` and the list\nholds only a monotonic key, so `For` ties identity to the row.\n\nTwo things the operator could not previously supply now arrive on their own:\n\n- pemakaian extra rows hard-coded `bmn_merk`, `bmn_tahun_perolehan` and\n  `bmn_kondisi` to `None`, because the form had nowhere to enter them. The\n  picked row carries all three.\n- penghapusan extra rows keep only \"Nilai Perolehan\", pre-filled from SIMAN.\n  It stays editable on purpose: the server overrides `nilai_perolehan` from\n  SIMAN for the MAIN item only (`services.rs` create), so an extra item whose\n  asset carries no figure still needs somewhere to put one. Blank stays blank\n  rather than becoming 0 — a zero here would travel into the SK.\n\nVerified against the deployed staging API, not a mock: searching \"station\nwagon\" as operator_a returns one row and fills kode 3020101003, NUP 1, merk\n\"Innova 2.4 G M/T Dsl Vin 2022\", kondisi Baik, nilai 391559057.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WQ99i4hsHtgtPr4pHRk6Vn\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlSVKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWXsQADIU+kjsl9Kz1RNZNneFqQ4R\nt6ut4bDFpsl09Lkfs7AedCpAA/GUfi9FcWKMJYIjCOg4i9zxy/bhW23upq2e2Am2\nTi2mo8KLWJJA9NIb5tuEpl5oOisRb42DS9AnLKmne7l9+dsBs9sOL9++ccSli7TF\nqA2RJtHGbZ0rylKaxPLZVx5IkhDqJyZ94uFbiXSRZBp7ykbXDe1kHobNG1blSHE3\nUb8g0W3XKN8Rp9yAPTyWzch7r+plIz7INSZtxZixRTVxqEU8DsKv1jtLv6vihW0u\nw7a1qNtcG72eOQWNM1gwtG1+tTTMzz+CtTHkwceL/vvcVGf6gjOK8mUATfR4aEl8\nzgeR2KfehB0Qd4yXmEA1/8k31LVLQmJqORZc1+uxeJvE3KiUMdYBweZDXkEvSPfP\nEjECovv8aA7r52z4YdoVJ/ZgASxYp/ODVaLjxNNX7J2IawLEfy25nykAFDblQ/HO\nbPiT6Oy7AIeEx1OZLOjFx1RASYPnSRoNxtr5K/5hBb6zEtqIsJT1yOwi7GxiHH3B\nsENwHikCPceZPyw6luG7Q9SqfbKkZmw7GqPMSTi6LNYz95cr3IVBSHTcMd6DC1yF\nVGU4IUZxQNuFS8ng8g1BOLLuw8bUo9zkCBvajTXqWB4k4fgMpvi5/FE56UIjP1fc\nzC2+3n73qY//1jVZqSgP\n=XYr3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T06:55:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/43abc96a5495b5aedb4a7d868f85ad7310181112","node_id":"C_kwDOP93DxNoAKDQzYWJjOTZhNTQ5NWI1YWVkYjRhN2Q4NjhmODVhZDczMTAxODExMTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/484a9c33057aea9803638526db0c1ec8120394b6","sha":"484a9c33057aea9803638526db0c1ec8120394b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/484a9c33057aea9803638526db0c1ec8120394b6"}],"sha":"43abc96a5495b5aedb4a7d868f85ad7310181112","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/43abc96a5495b5aedb4a7d868f85ad7310181112"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/220909633?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan","id":220909633,"login":"analisaperlengkapan","node_id":"U_kgDODSrQQQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/484a9c33057aea9803638526db0c1ec8120394b6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T06:54:49Z","email":"analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com","name":"analisaperlengkapan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T06:54:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(perlengkapan): pick the barang from SIMAN''s codification, stop typing it (#899)\n\nThe \"Tambah Barang\" form on kebutuhan-BMN asked the operator to type both\nthe barang name and its code, side by side, as free text. SIMAN already\npublishes that pairing: over the 624 533 real assets in the staging\nsnapshot, 2 033 codes carry exactly one standard name each. Typing it is\ntherefore an invitation to spell an existing fact wrongly.\n\nSo the form now searches the codification instead. Type three characters,\npick the row, and both fields fill themselves — the same shape as the\npegawai and aset pickers that landed in #883.\n\nSearching it live is not affordable: the query is a parallel sequential\nscan over all of siman_aset and measured 1 285 ms per keystroke against\nstaging. The answer is 2 038 rows, so it is snapshotted —\nintegrasi.mv_kodefikasi_barang, alongside the satker map that already\nworks this way.\n\nTwo details the data settled, not the design:\n\n  - the unique index is on (kode_barang, nama_barang), not on the code.\n    Running the view body against staging as it stands returns 2 038 rows\n    for 2 034 codes: four codes carry two names. All four are old fixture\n    rows, but a UNIQUE index on the code alone would have failed the very\n    first REFRESH.\n  - a code is matched by PREFIX, a name by infix. A code prefix is a\n    branch of the taxonomy, so ?q=30201 legitimately returns both Station\n    Wagon and Sepeda Motor.\n\nThe CronJob that refreshed the satker map alone is now\n`layanan-integrasi-snapshot-refresh` and takes its list from\nDERIVED_SNAPSHOTS in migrate.rs, so the next snapshot is refreshed by\nadding one line rather than by remembering to add a CronJob.\n\nThe manual fallback stays: an operator who needs a barang SIMAN has not\ncatalogued can still type it. It is a fallback now, not the only door.\n\nThe test harness applies integrasi''s real 006 migration rather than a\nhand-written stub — a stub of a cross-schema object certifies whatever\nshape it was written against. Applying the real file also caught that the\nharness itself named two codes after the wrong items; the fixture guard\nnow reads it too.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WQ99i4hsHtgtPr4pHRk6Vn\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5621a448af7e5559a513a6a09b1fbdfac108229c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/trees/5621a448af7e5559a513a6a09b1fbdfac108229c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/commits/484a9c33057aea9803638526db0c1ec8120394b6","verification":{"payload":"tree 5621a448af7e5559a513a6a09b1fbdfac108229c\nparent ba6e5438ac5891b0d39b633f6f9398fa927458b2\nauthor analisaperlengkapan <analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com> 1788159289 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788159289 +0700\n\nfeat(perlengkapan): pick the barang from SIMAN''s codification, stop typing it (#899)\n\nThe \"Tambah Barang\" form on kebutuhan-BMN asked the operator to type both\nthe barang name and its code, side by side, as free text. SIMAN already\npublishes that pairing: over the 624 533 real assets in the staging\nsnapshot, 2 033 codes carry exactly one standard name each. Typing it is\ntherefore an invitation to spell an existing fact wrongly.\n\nSo the form now searches the codification instead. Type three characters,\npick the row, and both fields fill themselves — the same shape as the\npegawai and aset pickers that landed in #883.\n\nSearching it live is not affordable: the query is a parallel sequential\nscan over all of siman_aset and measured 1 285 ms per keystroke against\nstaging. The answer is 2 038 rows, so it is snapshotted —\nintegrasi.mv_kodefikasi_barang, alongside the satker map that already\nworks this way.\n\nTwo details the data settled, not the design:\n\n  - the unique index is on (kode_barang, nama_barang), not on the code.\n    Running the view body against staging as it stands returns 2 038 rows\n    for 2 034 codes: four codes carry two names. All four are old fixture\n    rows, but a UNIQUE index on the code alone would have failed the very\n    first REFRESH.\n  - a code is matched by PREFIX, a name by infix. A code prefix is a\n    branch of the taxonomy, so ?q=30201 legitimately returns both Station\n    Wagon and Sepeda Motor.\n\nThe CronJob that refreshed the satker map alone is now\n`layanan-integrasi-snapshot-refresh` and takes its list from\nDERIVED_SNAPSHOTS in migrate.rs, so the next snapshot is refreshed by\nadding one line rather than by remembering to add a CronJob.\n\nThe manual fallback stays: an operator who needs a barang SIMAN has not\ncatalogued can still type it. It is a fallback now, not the only door.\n\nThe test harness applies integrasi''s real 006 migration rather than a\nhand-written stub — a stub of a cross-schema object certifies whatever\nshape it was written against. Applying the real file also caught that the\nharness itself named two codes after the wrong items; the fixture guard\nnow reads it too.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WQ99i4hsHtgtPr4pHRk6Vn\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlSU5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAoRIQAEYxnGctX9QqfXvgbvWMagZg\nrFicjUoFaZRLln49C3Ztb1Nn0PDgOGtu5NUzfzjmgs08xXy6MJwCypK1bi/1Tik4\nVMFuZHzdYbmJIp6tJn+oL4AVhnJ1wB4rNWD8oTZ4cJ24XmW4BZ2UORNboUZptUjr\nK7KsbKr8bUrS1zjIW6TyYgQVyeObLd/7lFI55i5qM6kASC4ne1skxb0c/nunbOod\nGNBtfmhVxtTBgRkZoiAkIlhBkjRcCB9SXFM54egahGlRp6iv25e3wvZ1Ur4HkkcH\nt9yF9bNBIY6TK8Ib5mXGbT3kFkzUe5uhZYOKQAK6BYWry1AhK58joxwOZ6zwSR5y\nXIsaCkdvLIvFjUfLRCmqdcJ8nC5CV2ZryeQ1Wd8od7h0BExQI/ugFj4EmxNgYi8z\nwMEAg1iRvZY/TypnCDILVnbyIcE0A/1rhusSdQ+mulGSlC5Pw71Kri+LZytOCsuw\nk3J1gJGalzm7c3fObtwmVBkOFLtXNfS7TVvm5MGIcsyZBhxo