sers/analisaperlengkapan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/aab04a391a74449bd9fc578c2efdb6e4c4114a49/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T18:48:51Z","email":"analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com","name":"analisaperlengkapan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T18:48:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(perlengkapan): the form asked for two UUIDs that do not exist (#885)\n\nCreating a usulan penghapusan required typing `Satuan Kerja (Satker ID)`\nand `Asset ID (UUID)`. Both fields were `required`. Neither has a source.\n\n`asset_id` had none at all: SIMAN assets live in `integrasi.siman_aset`,\nkeyed BIGSERIAL, so there is no UUID anywhere to copy. Measured on\nstaging — 0 of the 3 stored rows match any `siman_aset.id`, all three are\ne2e fixtures with invented values, there is no foreign key, and the\ncolumn is never JOINed. An asset''s identity here is satker + kode barang\n+ NUP, which is what `verify_asset_siman` looks it up by. `satker_id` was\nshadowed by `satker_code`, derived from the creator''s claims and the\ncolumn the RBAC predicate actually filters on; the one list filter that\nread `satker_id` was never given a value by any caller. Both carried an\nindex, so the database maintained B-trees over columns pointing at\nnothing.\n\nThe asset is now picked. That tightens the flow as well as shortening\nit: the picker reads `/bank-aset`, which is scoped from claims on the\nserver, so an operator can only reach their own satker''s assets. The\ntyped satker was not merely redundant — it was never checked against\nanything.\n\nChasing the field found the UUID being handed to the SK document\ngenerator as `\"satker_id\"`. No template references it, so it could never\nhave printed, but it was the value on offer to the next template author;\nit is now `satker_code`.\n\nV010 drops the columns rather than relaxing them to NULL: a nullable\ncolumn that resolves to nothing is still a field the next form will\noffer to fill.\n\nThe test asserts on the catalogue, not on a successful insert — an\ninsert would keep passing if the columns came back nullable — and checks\nboth directions: the columns are gone AND the authoritative satker_code\nsurvives. The e2e seed and three test payloads that carried invented\nUUIDs are cleaned out too; a fixture that fills a dead column does not\nmiss the bug, it certifies it.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012ti9AujKmDnVjc75wyWsmE\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7fa63f53d9bb3ecb27be41880d93e4207032774f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/trees/7fa63f53d9bb3ecb27be41880d93e4207032774f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/commits/aab04a391a74449bd9fc578c2efdb6e4c4114a49","verification":{"payload":"tree 7fa63f53d9bb3ecb27be41880d93e4207032774f\nparent b71938c9b266952cbf909c62791103014b54b3bc\nauthor analisaperlengkapan <analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com> 1788115731 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788115731 +0700\n\nfix(perlengkapan): the form asked for two UUIDs that do not exist (#885)\n\nCreating a usulan penghapusan required typing `Satuan Kerja (Satker ID)`\nand `Asset ID (UUID)`. Both fields were `required`. Neither has a source.\n\n`asset_id` had none at all: SIMAN assets live in `integrasi.siman_aset`,\nkeyed BIGSERIAL, so there is no UUID anywhere to copy. Measured on\nstaging — 0 of the 3 stored rows match any `siman_aset.id`, all three are\ne2e fixtures with invented values, there is no foreign key, and the\ncolumn is never JOINed. An asset''s identity here is satker + kode barang\n+ NUP, which is what `verify_asset_siman` looks it up by. `satker_id` was\nshadowed by `satker_code`, derived from the creator''s claims and the\ncolumn the RBAC predicate actually filters on; the one list filter that\nread `satker_id` was never given a value by any caller. Both carried an\nindex, so the database maintained B-trees over columns pointing at\nnothing.\n\nThe asset is now picked. That tightens the flow as well as shortening\nit: the picker reads `/bank-aset`, which is scoped from claims on the\nserver, so an operator can only reach their own satker''s assets. The\ntyped satker was not merely redundant — it was never checked against\nanything.\n\nChasing the field found the UUID being handed to the SK document\ngenerator as `\"satker_id\"`. No template references it, so it could never\nhave printed, but it was the value on offer to the next template author;\nit is now `satker_code`.\n\nV010 drops the columns rather than relaxing them to NULL: a nullable\ncolumn that resolves to nothing is still a field the next form will\noffer to fill.\n\nThe test asserts on the catalogue, not on a successful insert — an\ninsert would keep passing if the columns came back nullable — and checks\nboth directions: the columns are gone AND the authoritative satker_code\nsurvives. The e2e seed and three test payloads that carried invented\nUUIDs are cleaned out too; a fixture that fills a dead column does not\nmiss the bug, it certifies it.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012ti9AujKmDnVjc75wyWsmE\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlHsTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOhEQAG0qHt9EB5ry6aNZ1fyD90l+\nxkz9RrQnQRMflTqHrNgGKNeHQjlCYmQtMgxlLq3Z5kO5slmYtgVWxuH/UmsxsG4K\ndB9ZhnEIfbwyKHI8MhCXpipSsc6YPaxwuj2xSbbZzdDGvNgmR4Kr+sQVW95LUx/C\nuswhLJ1oGOlL7+YQQSxScnGm0ZytFzlRwWfoFeFTAgBqYTNTnw8ZQbhxCa6UaGoU\n18esNtA+5fV8rFEyog/73CjCCnkB1SnaJ8zJ+UM6xQkiCKGopCHkItKM2lA9a9w/\nzwFO7h87oX4zRdNjqgOD3F5VQ9Dzrt803duhmWddhegoRfhaE1L9osCIJvoTEPA6\nq+Izzz9A+WiinvLUaWY9MUV+/A5oitCNLHRykBjmnAqDGPYrifjp1hGdnIgjR/PI\nQiEQsF7TjFHpwH+JqtWk63yAP2oX54a7wOrSuh6BccbFpA8og3XhtJF2yLJ/u6QD\n0i4ypg1DES2I0I3KzQ/co6aTiMUnNHuZJXm5HH0rQLHncJ5tlg0r3VQtmTuAtf82\ny0D6ksQrmxZxsbGk3/LIM5/meM9FfpR6XNr379uykRwd1O+OMpm11LzH412j40r6\nopiRpEJlDIkAw7sSgdg4TSgBJXtLO6a3fpIOPpqMT6V2jQpEye4yxE9H/nEzfqcz\nrjwCtmovZNAgIcOCjiaL\n=3kdp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-30T18:48:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/aab04a391a74449bd9fc578c2efdb6e4c4114a49","node_id":"C_kwDOP93DxNoAKGFhYjA0YTM5MWE3NDQ0OWJkOWZjNTc4YzJlZmRiNmU0YzQxMTRhNDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/b71938c9b266952cbf909c62791103014b54b3bc","sha":"b71938c9b266952cbf909c62791103014b54b3bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/b71938c9b266952cbf909c62791103014b54b3bc"}],"sha":"aab04a391a74449bd9fc578c2efdb6e4c4114a49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/aab04a391a74449bd9fc578c2efdb6e4c4114a49"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/220909633?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan","id":220909633,"login":"analisaperlengkapan","node_id":"U_kgDODSrQQQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/b71938c9b266952cbf909c62791103014b54b3bc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T18:16:53Z","email":"analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com","name":"analisaperlengkapan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T18:16:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: a stacked PR ran no jobs and still reported CLEAN (#887)\n\n* ci: a stacked PR ran no jobs and still reported CLEAN\n\n`ci.yml`, `security.yml` and `autofix.yml` each triggered on\n\n    pull_request:\n      branches: [main]\n\nwhich reads as \"gate pull requests\" and behaves as \"gate pull requests that\nhappen to target main\". A stacked PR — base = another PR''s branch, which is how\na dependent change gets reviewed — matched no trigger, so not one job ran.\n\nThe second half is what turns a coverage gap into a hole. The branch ruleset\nalso targets `main`, so `required_status_checks` did not apply to a PR based on\nanything else. No checks run and no checks required is not reported as unknown:\nGitHub reports `mergeStateStatus: CLEAN`, the same value a fully green PR gets.\nThree PRs in one stack sat at CLEAN with zero verification and a live merge\nbutton. I found it because a stacked PR showed five checks, all of them from the\nPR-metadata workflow, and none from CI.\n\nThe auto-retarget when the parent merges does not repair it either: a base\nchange fires `pull_request.edited`, which is not one of the default trigger\ntypes, so the child would reach main unbuilt.\n\nThe filter is removed from all three. `push` stays on main.\n\nThe guard states the rule as total rather than as a list of workflows, because\nthe recurring failure in this repo is a correct gate whose SCOPE is a\nhand-written list that does not grow with the thing it covers. Any workflow with\na `pull_request` trigger runs on every pull request; one that genuinely needs\nscoping goes in PERMITTED with a written reason. Five canaries, including the\ntwo \"must still pass\" directions and `branches-ignore`, which is the same hole\nspelled the other way.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WQ99i4hsHtgtPr4pHRk6Vn\n\n* ci: the guard that found the hole fell into the one next to it\n\nFollow-up to this branch''s first commit, from its own first CI run.\n\n`check-pr-workflows-run-on-every-pr.py` parsed the workflows with PyYAML. It\npassed locally and failed on the runner, because the ARC runner image ships a\nbare Python. So the step went red for a reason unrelated to what it checks, and\nthe finding it exists to make was never made — which is the same failure mode as\nthe hole it was written to close: a check that looks like it is running and is\nnot.\n\nRewritten with the line parser the other guards here already use. That choice\nlooks arbitrary until you have watched this happen; it is now written down.\n\nThe second commit is the guard for the class, because this is the third time in\nthis one job:\n\n  * `Workflow Syntax (actionlint)` reported all eight workflows as \"Invalid\n    YAML\" for 40+ days. The workflows were fine; the fallback `python3 -c\n    \"import yaml\"` was not, and its failure was read as the files'' failure.\n  * `bc` and `yq` produced exit 127 in later steps of the same job.\n  * this one.\n\n`check-guard-imports-are-stdlib.py` derives which scripts CI runs from the\nworkflows rather than from a list, and asks `sys.stdlib_module_names` — so the\ninterpreter CI actually uses decides, not a list maintained here. It found two\nmore scripts on the first run: both use the stdlib-first fallback\n\n    try:     import tomllib\n    except:  import tomli as tomllib\n\nwhich cannot fail on a runner whose Python has the stdlib module. That is\npermitted, and named in the output rather than silently allowed, so the\nexemption is visible. A fallback whose try half is ALSO third-party is not\npermitted — that is two dependencies wearing one coat — and neither is a bare\n`except:`. Nine canaries, including those two and the real repository scan,\nwhich must agree with them or the canaries are theatre.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WQ99i4hsHtgtPr4pHRk6Vn\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"68857bc53f746a8f9cce0b784485e5f342ad54bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/trees/68857bc53f746a8f9cce0b784485e5f342ad54bb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/commits/b71938c9b266952cbf909c62791103014b54b3bc","verification":{"payload":"tree 68857bc53f746a8f9cce0b784485e5f342ad54bb\nparent 9237506764af0ed3576f71f1175c7486b3f23365\nauthor analisaperlengkapan <analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com> 1788113813 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788113813 +0700\n\nci: a stacked PR ran no jobs and still reported CLEAN (#887)\n\n* ci: a stacked PR ran no jobs and still reported CLEAN\n\n`ci.yml`, `security.yml` and `autofix.yml` each triggered on\n\n    pull_request:\n      branches: [main]\n\nwhich reads as \"gate pull requests\" and behaves as \"gate pull requests that\nhappen to target main\". A stacked PR — base = another PR''s branch, which is how\na dependent change gets reviewed — matched no trigger, so not one job ran.\n\nThe second half is what turns a coverage gap into a hole. The branch ruleset\nalso targets `main`, so `required_status_checks` did not apply to a PR based on\nanything else. No checks run and no checks required is not reported as unknown:\nGitHub reports `mergeStateStatus: CLEAN`, the same value a fully green PR gets.\nThree PRs in one stack sat at CLEAN with zero verification and a live merge\nbutton. I found it because a stacked PR showed five checks, all of them from the\nPR-metadata workflow, and none from CI.\n\nThe auto-retarget when the parent merges does not repair it either: a base\nchange fires `pull_request.edited`, which is not one of the default trigger\ntypes, so the child would reach main unbuilt.\n\nThe filter is removed from all three. `push` stays on main.\n\nThe guard states the rule as total rather than as a list of workflows, because\nthe recurring failure in this repo is a correct gate whose SCOPE is a\nhand-written list that does not grow with the thing it covers. Any workflow with\na `pull_request` trigger runs on every pull request; one that genuinely needs\nscoping goes in PERMITTED with a written reason. Five canaries, including the\ntwo \"must still pass\" directions and `branches-ignore`, which is the same hole\nspelled the other way.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WQ99i4hsHtgtPr4pHRk6Vn\n\n* ci: the guard that found the hole fell into the one next to it\n\nFollow-up to this branch''s first commit, from its own first CI run.\n\n`check-pr-workflows-run-on-every-pr.py` parsed the workflows with PyYAML. It\npassed locally and failed on the runner, because the ARC runner image ships a\nbare Python. So the step went red for a reason unrelated to what it checks, and\nthe finding it exists to make was never made — which is the same failure mode as\nthe hole it was written to close: a check that looks like it is running and is\nnot.\n\nRewritten with the line parser the other guards here already use. That choice\nlooks arbitrary until you have watched this happen; it is now written down.\n\nThe second commit is the guard for the class, because this is the third time in\nthis one job:\n\n  * `Workflow Syntax (actionlint)` reported all eight workflows as \"Invalid\n    YAML\" for 40+ days. The workflows were fine; the fallback `python3 -c\n    \"import yaml\"` was not, and its failure was read as the files'' failure.\n  * `bc` and `yq` produced exit 127 in later steps of the same job.\n  * this one.\n\n`check-guard-imports-are-stdlib.py` derives which scripts CI runs from the\nworkflows rather than from a list, and asks `sys.stdlib_module_names` — so the\ninterpreter CI actually uses decides, not a list maintained here. It found two\nmore scripts on the first run: both use the stdlib-first fallback\n\n    try:     import tomllib\n    except:  import tomli as tomllib\n\nwhich cannot fail on a runner whose Python has the stdlib module. That is\npermitted, and named in the output rather than silently allowed, so the\nexemption is visible. A fallback whose try half is ALSO third-party is not\npermitted — that is two dependencies wearing one coat — and neither is a bare\n`except:`. Nine canaries, including those two and the real repository scan,\nwhich must agree with them or the canaries are theatre.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WQ99i4hsHtgtPr4pHRk6Vn\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlHOVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAK7UQAB4DpUvcdo87+BUHASriyDjg\nWrHPe+J4qNB7NSnC7NQwJWD1gl1a571P7iHWosbCt/uvcWEyo37wKPHc7ttIbwyB\nFXh7cjeQ9NVKtUsO7KnRUn/uRV+0txNaC2bvEh5q/JFpu64HKzNHw+v2apm6Zw9C\nQ0264w7D7sOz+JMOX1yNg4QCC40w/cVC9lSeWeXx2tK8Jrv/4qBXjgf9BJeKG7iH\nctO7vvwvXisbGH8mVPanGHsOCm+OhVcvT8L2Euc/fTrwQZ2HCPA7cZ18Ecr1dvKd\nT1MbD2gxuDCBEdEwF5e1rqYpvChCMkgeUf3TgMkc1KrjfK/cTLyBWy4v5xqXf2CL\nPAycwq9R8sDSDOTV39DxcoRRyc138zcHi86PmNL37ILNx0msmAhPR1lFknAnqSXK\n7BRhiDAX4K1ozdSxkfftPfzfRi4JFpsn5xXxoNhb4sktwP5YMHa+gbgixQGPhyXM\nlrmAd6E29oNizwCUObbSuwn76Q2rJsGWyATBTBd2Ospy5xhiikoa0TX89kPVa5N1\nfYWl4ZpJ7hKkbW7EgLRIiK1VyMaQGdrVWquf4I9onc1gvLNbUg/do2byWxZIfbyh\n05E2806DpBdGh5hSXrjTTWTO2voXhv3HEoVabF6hkWTZ2RUnFTbvZLtzCs6CFn41\n4/AqwhaWq2Xd0h89N8Db\n=UGVi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-30T18:16:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/b71938c9b266952cbf909c62791103014b54b3bc","node_id":"C_kwDOP93DxNoAKGI3MTkzOGM5YjI2Njk1MmNiZjkwOWM2Mjc5MTEwMzAxNGI1NGIzYmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/9237506764af0ed3576f71f1175c7486b3f23365","sha":"9237506764af0ed3576f71f1175c7486b3f23365","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/9237506764af0ed3576f71f1175c7486b3f23365"}],"sha":"b71938c9b266952cbf909c62791103014b54b3bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/b71938c9b266952cbf909c62791103014b54b3bc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/220909633?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan","id":220909633,"login":"analisaperlengkapan","node_id":"U_kgDODSrQQQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/9237506764af0ed3576f71f1175c7486b3f23365/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T17:43:52Z","email":"analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com","name":"analisaperlengkapan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T17:43:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(perlengkapan): pick the employee and the asset, stop retyping them (#883)\n\n* feat(perlengkapan): pick the employee and the asset, stop retyping them\n\nThe permit form asked an operator to type six employee fields and a NUP that\nall already exist in the database. Per the user''s instruction: don''t type data\nthat already has a reference, it invites wrong input and duplication.\n\nMeasured on staging, which decides the interaction:\n\n  * siman_aset holds 624 533 rows but only 2 030 distinct item names, so a\n    name averages 307 assets; \"station wagon\" alone matches 785.\n  * name+NUP is not unique either — \"Contacless Card Reader E-KTP\" NUP 1 is\n    515 different assets. Even the example in the request, \"station wagon NUP\n    2\", is ambiguous nationally.\n  * 21 328 employees, NIP unique on every one of them.\n\nSo a <select> is impossible and picking a NAME does not pick an ASSET. The\nasset picker searches and returns identified ROWS — name, NUP, kode barang,\nmerk, satker — scoped to the caller''s satker on the server, where a search\ncosts 6 ms (230 ms nationally), so a 300 ms debounce needs no new index. The\nemployee needs no list at all: 18 digits identify the person.\n\nOnce picked, the fields are read-only display. That is the part that actually\nprevents mistyping; only the reference key is submitted.\n\nThe NUP-only lookup goes with it. NUP is a sequence number WITHIN one satker\nfor one kode barang — 24 715 assets carry \"2\" — so resolving an asset from it\nwas guesswork. The picker returns the row whole, kode barang included, and\n`lookup_by_nup` is deleted rather than silenced with #[allow(dead_code)].\n\nGolongan is deliberately left empty. It shares one column with pangkat\n(`golpang`) whose shape is inconsistent: 21 141 rows read \"Pangkat / (Gol)\"\nand the other 187 are the reverse, \"III/d (Sena Wira)\". Splitting it means\nguessing, and a wrong guess files a golongan as a rank for hundreds of people.\nThe value is passed through whole and labelled \"Pangkat / Golongan\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ybw1TonfE4XqdYdqpLP3Tc\n\n* fix(perlengkapan): the e2e still typed the NUP the picker replaced\n\nThree pengelolaan tests drove the form this PR removed: fill \"Nomor Urut\nPendaftaran\", press \"Cek Ketersediaan\". Both are gone, so all three timed out\nwaiting for a placeholder that no longer renders.\n\nRewritten against the picker, and one of them changes what it asserts. The\ncross-satker case used to expect an error message, because the old flow let an\noperator type any NUP and asked the backend about it afterwards. The picker\nsearches server-side within the caller''s satker, so another satker''s asset is\nnever sent at all — the honest assertion is the empty state, not an error. It\nchecks `aset-kosong` rather than the absence of a list, since \"no list yet\" is\nalso what a still-running search looks like.\n\nThe picker gained three structural test ids (`aset-terpilih`, `aset-hasil`,\n`aset-kosong`). getByText matches substrings case-insensitively and has passed\nhere against the wrong element before.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WQ99i4hsHtgtPr4pHRk6Vn\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7c421cc89a1d8387547590f6a7b635d95261addc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/trees/7c421cc89a1d8387547590f6a7b635d95261addc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/commits/9237506764af0ed3576f71f1175c7486b3f23365","verification":{"payload":"tree 7c421cc89a1d8387547590f6a7b635d95261addc\nparent e817cc7d5cc10b359d67b489390aff54f1f9abff\nauthor analisaperlengkapan <analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com> 1788111832 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788111832 +0700\n\nfeat(perlengkapan): pick the employee and the asset, stop retyping them (#883)\n\n* feat(perlengkapan): pick the employee and the asset, stop retyping them\n\nThe permit form asked an operator to type six employee fields and a NUP that\nall already exist in the database. Per the user''s instruction: don''t type data\nthat already has a reference, it invites wrong input and duplication.\n\nMeasured on staging, which decides the interaction:\n\n  * siman_aset holds 624 533 rows but only 2 030 distinct item names, so a\n    name averages 307 assets; \"station wagon\" alone matches 785.\n  * name+NUP is not unique either — \"Contacless Card Reader E-KTP\" NUP 1 is\n    515 different assets. Even the example in the request, \"station wagon NUP\n    2\", is ambiguous nationally.\n  * 21 328 employees, NIP unique on every one of them.\n\nSo a <select> is impossible and picking a NAME does not pick an ASSET. The\nasset picker searches and returns identified ROWS — name, NUP, kode barang,\nmerk, satker — scoped to the caller''s satker on the server, where a search\ncosts 6 ms (230 ms nationally), so a 300 ms debounce needs no new index. The\nemployee needs no list at all: 18 digits identify the person.\n\nOnce picked, the fields are read-only display. That is the part that actually\nprevents mistyping; only the reference key is submitted.\n\nThe NUP-only lookup goes with it. NUP is a sequence number WITHIN one satker\nfor one kode barang — 24 715 assets carry \"2\" — so resolving an asset from it\nwas guesswork. The picker returns the row whole, kode barang included, and\n`lookup_by_nup` is deleted rather than silenced with #[allow(dead_code)].\n\nGolongan is deliberately left empty. It shares one column with pangkat\n(`golpang`) whose shape is inconsistent: 21 141 rows read \"Pangkat / (Gol)\"\nand the other 187 are the reverse, \"III/d (Sena Wira)\". Splitting it means\nguessing, and a wrong guess files a golongan as a rank for hundreds of people.\nThe value is passed through whole and labelled \"Pangkat / Golongan\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ybw1TonfE4XqdYdqpLP3Tc\n\n* fix(perlengkapan): the e2e still typed the NUP the picker replaced\n\nThree pengelolaan tests drove the form this PR removed: fill \"Nomor Urut\nPendaftaran\", press \"Cek Ketersediaan\". Both are gone, so all three timed out\nwaiting for a placeholder that no longer renders.\n\nRewritten against the picker, and one of them changes what it asserts. The\ncross-satker case used to expect an error message, because the old flow let an\noperator type any NUP and asked the backend about it afterwards. The picker\nsearches server-side within the caller''s satker, so another satker''s asset is\nnever sent at all — the honest assertion is the empty state, not an error. It\nchecks `aset-kosong` rather than the absence of a list, since \"no list yet\" is\nalso what a still-running search looks like.\n\nThe picker gained three structural test ids (`aset-terpilih`, `aset-hasil`,\n`aset-kosong`). getByText matches substrings case-insensitively and has passed\nhere against the wrong element before.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WQ99i4hsHtgtPr4pHRk6Vn\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlGvYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIdcQAFjYcJ/8poaxEAE+o7dC5Gox\nXqMST35xo5QoUYaPs31KK19MFJtY5A/LmNnIG0EN3hVFoKrgxUpvARg5Ivg3M4HF\nxCm2E2SQ0V/S8Pi3i11r7XXElIDmeLXVVyLTrrGbxkXANyQaZq0Nb8P8e6cYpYB6\nu5rTbDkWw1VFoKT2K5IvylCOtNYTZ5nRuwwHizuhz91etDF8EviiZcNuHUbNJiHA\nprdH0GyOPc6HluOtCXa8fjtr1EkvZguJnVOkk9/U+vptDaxiGRDfnUilsKi0lQzU\nTI0RQI8ZlefhsdYhvt+YZqU6ayIvQ3WtZYZlhOdkZm3NlpXKAnTQiizgY/bSXX3L\nMjkpV9mMKrXXYOMPhI5MOs+GzAd9m+Qi+tQI+0AjdEm7/RKRBox1p0Svv1lBCY2W\n3FeNmyNFjt7vgvU5NETgDa+w3iSOyYH/4sxpZxoK1Nng2XtPJsnI47f6jSLS3oAg\n68ic2iSs9JVM2KEjCOO7mEWoTwUwDC3EAtWkuzfZnyAvrYIfc8BNJHwgdlLWByW1\n258x1i4W2iz+79g7qSwpmI261ztFUx+H9Jw0jf2e3HdD/JsM2pwscfADNlWek9n8\navy+eLv0YMJrRxzqbpVO0QGDYPR3XHoeVyKIqmdzQUsXunkhs3tFo7WDPkDxxCk3\nKnPF5Lyv8YW4CUmg2NIx\n=NPWQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-30T17:43:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/9237506764af0ed3576f71f1175c7486b3f23365","node_id":"C_kwDOP93DxNoAKDkyMzc1MDY3NjRhZjBlZDM1NzZmNzFmMTE3NWM3NDg2YjNmMjMzNjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/e817cc7d5cc10b359d67b489390aff54f1f9abff","sha":"e817cc7d5cc10b359d67b489390aff54f1f9abff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/e817cc7d5cc10b359d67b489390aff54f1f9abff"}],"sha":"9237506764af0ed3576f71f1175c7486b3f23365","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/9237506764af0ed3576f71f1175c7486b3f23365"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/220909633?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan","id":220909633,"login":"analisaperlengkapan","node_id":"U_kgDODSrQQQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/e817cc7d5cc10b359d67b489390aff54f1f9abff/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T16:37:03Z","email":"analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com","name":"analisaperlengkapan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T16:37:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"perf(perlengkapan): five scans of 624 533 rows to answer one question (#884)\n\nThe bank-aset dashboard ran five sequential queries over the same table,\nand the landing page''s headline numbers stayed blank for as long as they\ntook. Measured on the staging snapshot: a bare scan is 53 ms, but the\n`rph_aset ~ ''^[0-9]+…$''` test plus the cast costs ~840 ms — and three of\nthe five paid it. One `GROUPING SETS` pass reads the table once and\nevaluates that regex once per row:\n\n  five queries  4 246 ms / 4 313 ms\n  one pass      1 469 ms / 1 628 ms\n\nVerified value-identical before trusting it: every total and every\nbreakdown compared to the queries it replaces with `EXCEPT` in both\ndirections over all 624 533 rows — 0 differing rows on each of the seven\ncomparisons. Ties, which the old queries left to the executor, now have\nan explicit tiebreaker, so equal counts come back in the same order\nevery time.\n\nTwo satker grouping sets rather than one, because the two numbers ask\ndifferent questions: the top-10 list is by NAME, `total_satker` counts\nCODES (556 codes against 554 names — counting names folds two satkers\ninto one). `tahun` is NULL for exactly the rows the old per-year query\nexcluded in its WHERE, so dropping that group reproduces it while\nkeeping those assets in every other breakdown.\n\nThe risk moves rather than disappears: instead of five queries that\ncould disagree there is one result set whose rows must be routed to the\nright breakdown, and a misrouted row yields a response that is\nwell-formed, plausible and wrong. The existing tests cover `total_aset`,\n`total_satker` and two breakdowns under scope; the new one asserts all\neight fields against a seed small enough to check by eye, including the\nfour nothing looked at — and seeds the values SIMAN really sends: an\nunparseable date, a non-numeric `rph_aset`, a satker with no name.\n\nThe dead-column guard failed this, correctly given what it could see: it\nreads `AS kondisi` as a read of the dead column. A CTE that binds the\ncorrected expression to that name has created a local column, so the\nguard now treats uses AFTER a binding as references to it — positionally,\nbecause `SELECT kondisi AS kondisi` is still a real read and a\nwhole-literal rule would unflag exactly that. Three canaries pin both\ndirections.\n\nThe remaining ~0.8 s is still that regex. It belongs in a generated\nnumeric column, which is a migration rather than a query change.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012ti9AujKmDnVjc75wyWsmE\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"03b2b2b9995b5cf786b295a8b404409f77f6ddec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/trees/03b2b2b9995b5cf786b295a8b404409f77f6ddec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/commits/e817cc7d5cc10b359d67b489390