"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/220909633?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan","id":220909633,"login":"analisaperlengkapan","node_id":"U_kgDODSrQQQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/ea0e212f49f903956c88614656a801c8fd05c42d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T00:37:19Z","email":"analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com","name":"analisaperlengkapan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T00:37:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(perlengkapan): the last light-palette screens on a navy app (#881)\n\nSeven screens were still written against Tailwind''s light defaults. On a\n\n  * /admin/roles drew four solid white cards, and its <h1> was text-gray-900\n    on the navy page — a near-black heading nobody could read.\n  * /admin/templates did the same, and its template names carried no colour\n    class at all, so they inherited the app''s light body colour onto a white\n    panel and vanished.\n  * /pengelolaan/pemakaian/buat and /pengelolaan/penghapusan/buat are large\n    white forms whose <select> elements had NEITHER a background NOR a text\n    colour. A control with a value selected looked empty.\n  * the batch toolbar''s two confirm modals and the workflow comment modal were\n    white boxes over the app''s own dark backdrop, while every other modal in\n    the app uses bg-surface-panel.\n\n46 form controls now carry an explicit field style rather than inheriting one,\nand 191 palette tokens were mapped in a single pass — the previous attempt\nsubstituted its own output and produced classes like bg-white/[0.04]/[0.04].\n\nbank_aset/qrcode_page.rs keeps its bg-white and now says why: it previews a\nlabel sheet that gets printed on paper, so darkening it would make the preview\nlie. It is the one documented exception in the new guard.\n\ncheck-dark-theme-palette.py is blocking in CI and scoped to\nantarmuka/perlengkapan — portal and lib/ui still carry unconverted light\nscreens, and a guard that fails on known-unconverted code teaches people to\nignore it. Alpha tints (bg-white/10) stay legal; only solid light shades are\nflagged. Canaried four ways, including comment-only text, since these files\ndocument their own history in prose that names the banned classes.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ybw1TonfE4XqdYdqpLP3Tc\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"87c5e02d83c32175421f0c4d34f8b98e61614ff7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/trees/87c5e02d83c32175421f0c4d34f8b98e61614ff7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/commits/ea0e212f49f903956c88614656a801c8fd05c42d","verification":{"payload":"tree 87c5e02d83c32175421f0c4d34f8b98e61614ff7\nparent f4e1aa5bceb9c67ad4e566a1d5220ae20edf8b1e\nauthor analisaperlengkapan <analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com> 1788050239 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788050239 +0000\n\nfix(perlengkapan): the last light-palette screens on a navy app (#881)\n\nSeven screens were still written against Tailwind''s light defaults. On a\n\n  * /admin/roles drew four solid white cards, and its <h1> was text-gray-900\n    on the navy page — a near-black heading nobody could read.\n  * /admin/templates did the same, and its template names carried no colour\n    class at all, so they inherited the app''s light body colour onto a white\n    panel and vanished.\n  * /pengelolaan/pemakaian/buat and /pengelolaan/penghapusan/buat are large\n    white forms whose <select> elements had NEITHER a background NOR a text\n    colour. A control with a value selected looked empty.\n  * the batch toolbar''s two confirm modals and the workflow comment modal were\n    white boxes over the app''s own dark backdrop, while every other modal in\n    the app uses bg-surface-panel.\n\n46 form controls now carry an explicit field style rather than inheriting one,\nand 191 palette tokens were mapped in a single pass — the previous attempt\nsubstituted its own output and produced classes like bg-white/[0.04]/[0.04].\n\nbank_aset/qrcode_page.rs keeps its bg-white and now says why: it previews a\nlabel sheet that gets printed on paper, so darkening it would make the preview\nlie. It is the one documented exception in the new guard.\n\ncheck-dark-theme-palette.py is blocking in CI and scoped to\nantarmuka/perlengkapan — portal and lib/ui still carry unconverted light\nscreens, and a guard that fails on known-unconverted code teaches people to\nignore it. Alpha tints (bg-white/10) stay legal; only solid light shades are\nflagged. Canaried four ways, including comment-only text, since these files\ndocument their own history in prose that names the banned classes.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ybw1TonfE4XqdYdqpLP3Tc\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqk3s/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhigQALIZ/R1665/TnWa0dQtW8SVS\nugwgC7jFfUE8VOZwKRSUQtvM67LejMG2/6aqEeE8chyLlil6wThk4PubmVoS1jre\nztSBapG7+uRBB4LPTP2eW287s5sboWyKDIuRMn89jzkTfwZhFbcCq8VPFtbwikNO\ntrlKryJbVvOEtrKjfc5b2VuRcmbwO9OyFp2R5HOlqVA9f6ZD7J2ylXj/6kezFr3b\nydWSjK0ykFrbWn2P5jB6efwCDNeJOEE8k297Q38vkreo9E7gbs59tvzShZx93yF6\nO789c4uLYV2hERA04JA2/rTJY/QJhDFo9aTwUagq720fBO2xhrrWXmmN8jxsL+IN\ngcVF2KllBAtMpFPsNALl3qtgNbj8lX+tBrQbwkYIQbGoyD4Qv613d+QQ60pbAenJ\n2hhurAC6QTNTAQvykhuQJcXt/fRQA4Kqlw1fm4Zywf7C578ubn10mvg6dU4gd0eT\nnnydVs5/blbm65QhGAwhkQahPSEtDk2z9sVTYKzMw6b27qdk84NNgkp/ax0P7r9T\nWmyCjadqiNzwRhHV/2Z2KS6xCZO+OAZE1jC56tX6C3D0GPN1k/J1DAGX8zGoBIYw\naJK+xs1tLTJ6lB6yronWiyo6J9js+ulBKvXWJPCQsfqDo8IPJINq9NRVEajA55x6\nqRbOeg0sSe1QtpYaz6RE\n=WZQu\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-30T00:37:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/ea0e212f49f903956c88614656a801c8fd05c42d","node_id":"C_kwDOP93DxNoAKGVhMGUyMTJmNDlmOTAzOTU2Yzg4NjE0NjU2YTgwMWM4ZmQwNWM0MmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/f4e1aa5bceb9c67ad4e566a1d5220ae20edf8b1e","sha":"f4e1aa5bceb9c67ad4e566a1d5220ae20edf8b1e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/f4e1aa5bceb9c67ad4e566a1d5220ae20edf8b1e"}],"sha":"ea0e212f49f903956c88614656a801c8fd05c42d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/ea0e212f49f903956c88614656a801c8fd05c42d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/220909633?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan","id":220909633,"login":"analisaperlengkapan","node_id":"U_kgDODSrQQQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/f4e1aa5bceb9c67ad4e566a1d5220ae20edf8b1e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T21:34:31Z","email":"analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com","name":"analisaperlengkapan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T21:34:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(perlengkapan): one workflow, four copies of its status vocabulary (#880)\n\nA workflow status has one authority: the enum that writes the column. The\nfrontend restated that mapping anyway, and the copy grew to four — each with\ndifferent gaps, all of them silent.\n\n  * pemakaian list + detail: no arm for SUBMITTED_APPROVER_SATKER or\n    REVISI_OPERATOR, the two states the whole V035 three-step approval runs\n    through. A permit waiting on the Approver Satker read \"Lainnya\".\n  * penghapusan list + detail: no arm for KONSEP_SK_WILAYAH_GENERATED or\n    SK_SIGNED_WILAYAH, so the entire wilayah authority branch read \"Lainnya\"\n    and its detail page said \"Fase tidak dikenal.\" about a proposal running\n    perfectly normally.\n  * the monitoring tables mapped nothing and printed a raw ACTIVE.\n\nAdding the missing arms would only postpone the fifth copy. The vocabulary\nmoves to the enum instead: tone() and hint() are exhaustive matches over the\nvariants, so a new status cannot be added without being named. describe()\nreturns label + tone (+ hint), and hands back an unrecognised state verbatim\nrather than renaming it \"Lainnya\" — showing the value is what helps.\n\nThe backend now sends status_label and status_tone per row; the frontend keeps\na five-tone → CSS map, and five does not grow when the workflow does.\n\ncheck-fe-status-vocabulary.py derives the state names from to_state_name()\nrather than listing them, and tests the direction: a state name in a match\nPATTERN is a display table, a state name in the BODY is a filter enum and is\nleft alone. Canaried five ways — the one-line variant failed the first version\nof the guard, which extracted patterns per line and so was blind exactly where\nthe previous view!-attribute guard had been.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ybw1TonfE4XqdYdqpLP3Tc\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8596795e557ff6180aaeff49d21fb3801694743b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/trees/8596795e557ff6180aaeff49d21fb3801694743b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/commits/f4e1aa5bceb9c67ad4e566a1d5220ae20edf8b1e","verification":{"payload":"tree 8596795e557ff6180aaeff49d21fb3801694743b\nparent f4585cf4f25dd3808308f0cc5da508c59b6df17a\nauthor analisaperlengkapan <analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com> 1788039271 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788039271 +0000\n\nfix(perlengkapan): one workflow, four copies of its status vocabulary (#880)\n\nA workflow status has one authority: the enum that writes the column. The\nfrontend restated that mapping anyway, and the copy grew to four — each with\ndifferent gaps, all of them silent.\n\n  * pemakaian list + detail: no arm for SUBMITTED_APPROVER_SATKER or\n    REVISI_OPERATOR, the two states the whole V035 three-step approval runs\n    through. A permit waiting on the Approver Satker read \"Lainnya\".\n  * penghapusan list + detail: no arm for KONSEP_SK_WILAYAH_GENERATED or\n    SK_SIGNED_WILAYAH, so the entire wilayah authority branch read \"Lainnya\"\n    and its detail page said \"Fase tidak dikenal.\" about a proposal running\n    perfectly normally.\n  * the monitoring tables mapped nothing and printed a raw ACTIVE.\n\nAdding the missing arms would only postpone the fifth copy. The vocabulary\nmoves to the enum instead: tone() and hint() are exhaustive matches over the\nvariants, so a new status cannot be added without being named. describe()\nreturns label + tone (+ hint), and hands back an unrecognised state verbatim\nrather than renaming it \"Lainnya\" — showing the value is what helps.\n\nThe backend now sends status_label and status_tone per row; the frontend keeps\na five-tone → CSS map, and five does not grow when the workflow does.\n\ncheck-fe-status-vocabulary.py derives the state names from to_state_name()\nrather than listing them, and tests the direction: a state name in a match\nPATTERN is a display table, a state name in the BODY is a filter enum and is\nleft alone. Canaried five ways — the one-line variant failed the first version\nof the guard, which extracted patterns per line and so was blind exactly where\nthe previous view!-attribute guard had been.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ybw1TonfE4XqdYdqpLP3Tc\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqk1BnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJOoQAGBfqTF58/999FlpYePbPszb\nPwpHwk0+/xz+FIPNLDHgVf2GDc31dNOd/pyyaAt52rggT+prKcJfv/5RdKq+dspa\ncXgYz325VmQJvWMh2pMsFh4btPQh+OwCngYdKlGeLUXPScGpmoZPy89fs9hQJ9I7\nF7L5n4wcn04EF+IWIRxyBmkvHE2jdLkLrUwEMTY6pRlQlNqf07MrMy4wD8pNDq16\nUariK+IJ764nDV/p81VURVSo1tyxSB0nvfrjUjXi1IBvSQaSw5uRS7n937HzTcE2\nURV4yosMxqyPR+Nd2T+LNlen4CYP3eKYQh57UochYEuoJHSKyME2iaqFp6FyVJ39\nYNz3rWQgruBIEO/ManXMtlNndzRhXk7RFQHfgbkh57NDQ2D2fsNoXyuuiya6rERY\nXEBeD1kK1GBgBSxNByZSqqlKzAmY8G6RIju8VTSUDK/7NVhoCFWpodkUQcWZbPz9\nYY8Bqbiz22frF5gkj6TJR2VjyTr/uY+s7oBwCUDKeCXsR9n3NVD3whu8PhvuMdAn\nOHcbTTC3nzmou1siT2srRx24NWD+lod9SfXBcjyCS+hnSizB1y46efn6FrS9uW+A\nIekwpJyZowUo/VWfGEKa48ZpnPkwpTsnMO3QOJZTvyb+29ov4Upy95mdULZ1P4F6\nWni6WBpQVkCALd/5Ukdq\n=ThwP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-29T21:34:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/f4e1aa5bceb9c67ad4e566a1d5220ae20edf8b1e","node_id":"C_kwDOP93DxNoAKGY0ZTFhYTViY2ViOWM2N2FkNGU1NjZhMWQ1MjIwYWUyMGVkZjhiMWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/f4585cf4f25dd3808308f0cc5da508c59b6df17a","sha":"f4585cf4f25dd3808308f0cc5da508c59b6df17a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/f4585cf4f25dd3808308f0cc5da508c59b6df17a"}],"sha":"f4e1aa5bceb9c67ad4e566a1d5220ae20edf8b1e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/f4e1aa5bceb9c67ad4e566a1d5220ae20edf8b1e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/220909633?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan","id":220909633,"login":"analisaperlengkapan","node_id":"U_kgDODSrQQQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/f4585cf4f25dd3808308f0cc5da508c59b6df17a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T20:11:53Z","email":"analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com","name":"analisaperlengkapan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T20:11:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(perlengkapan): the dashboard redesign, and what its screenshot sweep found (#879)\n\n* feat(perlengkapan): the dashboard shows what the backend has been computing all along\n\nSeven aggregates reached no screen. `/dashboard/perlengkapan` computes kebutuhan\nstatus, gap analysis, uniform-size distribution, workflow bottlenecks, SLA\nbreaches and the permit/removal status splits — and had no frontend caller at\nall (#97), which is why the 500 it used to return went unnoticed until an e2e\nprobed it directly (#116). The landing page rendered four numbers.\n\nThis wires it, and reorders the page around how it is read: what the asset base\nlooks like, what needs a decision today, then the analysis behind both.\n\n  * KPI row now carries SHARE as well as count. 76 459 damaged assets is not a\n    number anyone can reason with; 12,2% of 624 533 is.\n  * \"Perlu Tindakan\": SLA breaches, mean processing hours, permit and removal\n    volumes.\n  * \"Analisis Aset\": composition by SIMAN taxonomy, acquisition VALUE by\n    taxonomy (a second panel, not a second column — Tanah is 0,3% of units and a\n    fifth of the value, and a count-only view hides where the money is),\n    acquisition trend per year, and a satker ranking for tiers that oversee more\n    than one satker.\n  * \"Kebutuhan & Alur\": status split, bottleneck queue, request trend, per-satker\n    requests, and the gap table — surplus shown as surplus rather than clamped,\n    because \"asked for 3, holds 1 903\" is the more useful sentence.\n  * \"Perlengkapan & Pengelolaan\": uniform-size distribution (the figure\n    procurement orders against) and the two module status splits.\n\nCharts are new primitives in `lib/ui/components/charts/primitives.rs`: plain\nSVG, no chart dependency, colours and container class as props. The reason the\nexisting in-house widgets (`components::dashboard`, 821 lines, plus\n`monitoring_dashboard`, 439) have never had a single user is that they hard-code\n`bg-white dark:bg-gray-800` — every one of them would arrive as a white card in\nthe middle of a navy-and-gold design system. Colour is never the only carrier of\nmeaning here: every series is named and its value written out, and each chart\nexposes `role=\"img\"` with an aria-label carrying the numbers.\n\nNo sample data anywhere. Every figure is a query result from one of two\nserver-scoped endpoints; where the backend has no such measurement the panel\nsays so rather than drawing something plausible. `asset_utilization` is\ndeliberately NOT mirrored — it is a third count of \"how many assets, how many in\ngood condition\", the question the condition cards already answer, and putting\ntwo independently-computed answers to one question on one screen is the fault\nthis page was just consolidated to remove.\n\n\"Real time\" is polling, and the page says so: both queries refetch every 60 s,\nand the header stamps the moment the last load landed, with a manual refresh\nbeside it. It deliberately does NOT subscribe to `/dashboard/ws`. That socket\nauthenticates and then delivers nothing, because `broadcast_dashboard_update`\nhas no callers anywhere in the backend — subscribing would look like live push\nand be a spinner that never turns. (If it is ever given producers: the broadcast\nis unscoped, so per-satker fan-out has to come first.)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\n* feat(perlengkapan): the dashboard can be drilled into, and the drill cannot dig sideways\n\nPusat asked for \"show me one region, or one satker\"; a wilayah validator for\n\"one satker in my region\". A satker operator needs neither — their scope is\nalready a single satker.\n\nThe obvious shape is an extra `AND satker = $n` on each query. That is wrong\nhere in a specific way: this module applies a scope in THIRTEEN places, and a\nfilter that lives beside the scope rather than inside it is one refactor away\nfrom being applied INSTEAD of it. That is not hypothetical — it is exactly what\n#871 was: `?satker_id=` on the laporan export replaced the scope instead of\nnarrowing it, and a nationwide report came back.\n\nSo the drill-down is a scope TRANSFORM, not a condition:\n\n    SatkerScope::narrowed_to(code, in_scope) -> Satker(code) | Denied\n    SatkerScope::narrowed_to_wilayah(w, caller_w) -> WilayahKode(w) | Denied\n    AsetScope::   (the same pair, mirrored)\n\n`narrow_for_request` resolves what the request asked for against what the claims\ngrant and hands back a scope that is narrower or `Denied` — never wider. All\nthirteen application sites inherit it without knowing the feature exists, and\n\"a filter cannot widen\" stops being a convention about statement order and\nbecomes a property of the value.\n\nAdding the `WilayahKode` variant made the compiler name the three predicates\nthat had to learn it (the kebutuhan recap and both campaign-visibility\nbuilders). A hand-kept list would have found none of them.\n\nTHE TWO WILAYAH CODES ARE NOT THE SAME CODE. `SatkerScope` compares the Kejati''s\nMySIMKARI `wilayah_code`; `AsetScope` compares SIMAN''s `wilayah_kode` (digits\n6-9 of `kdsatker_keu`). They are a measured bijection but different values, so\n`narrow_for_request` TRANSLATES between them via `v_satker_code_map`. Passing\none string to both — which is what I wrote first — scopes the perlengkapan half\nto nothing while the SIMAN half narrows correctly: a half-filtered dashboard,\nwhich is worse than an unfiltered one because it looks like it worked.\n\nAlso here, because the filters need somewhere real to come from:\n\n  * `/bank-aset/dashboard` now takes the same filter set as the list, through\n    ONE shared `AsetFilter` + `push_asset_filters`. The summary used to ignore\n    every filter, so narrowing the table below left the totals above describing\n    the whole population.\n  * `/bank-aset/filter-options` gains `satker_kode` (value = `kdsatker_keu`,\n    label = name) and `wilayah` (value = the SIMAN region code, label from\n    `v_satker_wilayah`). The existing name-keyed `satker` list is untouched so\n    the Bank Aset page keeps working — but names collide (554 distinct names for\n    556 distinct codes) and the drill-down keys on the code.\n  * acquisition-date bounds, compared as TEXT. `tgl_perlh` IS text and all\n    624 533 staging rows are ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` (measured: zero exceptions), for\n    which lexicographic and calendar order agree. A `::date` cast is equivalent\n    today and throws on the first malformed row a future ingest writes — and\n    `panic = \"abort\"` makes that the process, not the request.\n  * the pemakaian/penghapusan rekaps resolve their status labels from\n    `ms_workflow_status` instead of printing the raw column: users were reading\n    `KONSEP_SK_GENERATED`, `SUBMIT_WILAYAH`, `SUBMIT_PUSAT`, `ACTIVE`. The\n    kebutuhan rekap beside them already did this. The first fallback I wrote\n    produced \"Kode DRAFT\" for a row with no code; the test caught it.\n  * the trend axis thins its labels — twenty-eight acquisition years rendered\n    as an unbroken bar of digits.\n\nTests: a drill-down returns exactly the drilled satker''s own view (asserted\nequal to that operator''s own dashboard); an operator naming another satker gets\nzeros, not that satker; a wilayah validator reaches a satker in their region and\nnot one outside it; the exports resolve the drill-down the same way. Canary:\nremoving the fail-closed branch makes the operator see SKR002''s 2 assets, and\nthe test goes red on exactly that.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\n* feat(perlengkapan): the dashboard filter bar, offering only what its reader can act on\n\nBackend already accepted the drill-down; this is the control for it.\n\nTier-aware because the tiers genuinely differ: pusat picks a region and then a\nsatker, a wilayah validator picks a satker (their region is fixed by their\nclaims, so a region selector would offer nothing they could widen to), and a\nsatker operator gets no selector at all — their scope IS one satker, so the\ncontrol would show a single option that changes nothing.\n\nThe options come from `/bank-aset/filter-options`, which is scoped server-side:\nmeasured on staging it answers 1 satker to an operator, 7 to a wilayah validator\nand 554 to pusat. So the dropdown cannot offer a satker its reader may not see,\nand the server refuses it regardless.\n\nTwo things worth stating:\n\n  * the satker option''s VALUE is now the MySIMKARI `kode_satker`, not\n    `kdsatker_keu`. One selection has to narrow both halves of the dashboard,\n    and they key on different codes; unifying on the canonical identity (#43,\n    #94) means the server maps it where needed instead of the frontend guessing\n    which code a given endpoint wants.\n  * selecting a region re-fetches the OPTIONS as well as the data, so the satker\n    list shrinks to that region. The first version filtered the list in the\n    browser by slicing digits 6-9 out of the code — a frontend re-implementing\n    how a satker code is composed, which is the kind of assumption that is right\n    until the day it is not.\n\nFilters are part of the query key, so a selection refetches rather than being\nanswered from cache.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\n* fix(ui): a comparison in a view! attribute ends the tag, so 26 controls were inert\n\n`view!` tokenises `>` as the end of the opening tag — inside an attribute value\ntoo. So this does not compile to what it reads as:\n\n    prop:disabled=move || page.get() >= total_pages\n    on:click=next_handler\n\nThe macro closes the tag at the `>`. Everything after it becomes a text node:\n\n  * `on:click` is never attached — the button does nothing.\n  * `prop:disabled` receives an `i32`, truthy for every page but 0, so the\n    button is also disabled.\n  * The Rust source renders on the page. Users read\n    `= total_pages on : click = move | _ | on_next.run(()) >Selanjutnya`\n    between the pager arrows.\n\nThe fix is a brace group, which the tokeniser reads as one token tree:\n\n    prop:disabled=move || { page.get() >= total_pages }\n\n26 attribute values across both frontends and `lib/ui`, `DarkPagination` among\nthem. No paginated list in either app could reach page two.\n\nWhat let it live, and a correction to my own first fix\n-----------------------------------------------------\n`cargo check` sees valid markup and a valid text node. No test clicks page two.\nA route sweep loads the page happily. The one honest signal is rustc reporting\nthe callback as an unused variable, and it had been silenced two different\nways: a hand-written `#[allow(unused_variables)]` on `DarkPagination` and\n`PaginationControls`, whose comments asserted the lint was mistaken; and\n`_`-prefix renames on a component prop (`_total_pages`) and two handlers\n(`_next_handler`). The second form leaves no `#[allow]` to grep for.\n\nI first read this as a formatter accident and \"fixed\" it by rejoining the `>=`\nonto the attribute line without bracing it. That silently reproduced the bug:\nthe guard I had just written went green while the handler was still detached,\nbecause it matched the reflowed *shape* rather than the cause. It was also\nblind to `pemakaian_bmn_monitoring.rs`, still on one line and never reflowed.\nThe guard now tests the cause — an attribute closure whose body carries a bare\n`<` or `>` outside any bracket group — and is canaried in both directions,\nincluding the one-line variant. Verification is the absence of the\n`unused variable` warnings, not the guard''s own green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\n* fix(perlengkapan): one workflow, two numberings, and the wrong one named the step\n\nTwo master tables describe the kebutuhan-BMN workflow and they part ways at\n2004:\n\n    kode  KebutuhanBmnStatus (writes the column)   ms_aktivitas_bmn (was joined)\n    2002  SubmitWilayah  \"Diajukan ke Validator Wilayah\"   SUBMIT_SATKER\n    2004  SubmitPusat    \"Diajukan ke Validator Pusat\"     ANALISIS_KELAYAKAN\n    2005  AnalisisKelayakan \"Analisis Kelayakan\"           PENYUSUNAN_PRIORITAS\n\n`ms_workflow_status` agrees with the enum. `ms_aktivitas_bmn` does not, and\n`PENYUSUNAN_PRIORITAS` is a step the workflow config itself records as merged\naway and never separate.\n\nThis was not a cosmetic problem. Reading the wrong master told a Validator\nPusat that a request merely *queued* for them was already under feasibility\nanalysis, and it did so on the report they use to triage.\n\nFive copies of the numbering, one of them right:\n\n  1. `ms_aktivitas_bmn` seed (V002) — old numbering, and its `nama` is the\n     machine token, so `/kebutuhan-bmn/laporan` printed `SUBMIT_SATKER` and\n     `ANALISIS_KELAYAKAN` verbatim.\n  2. `vw_kebutuhan_bmn_summary` joined it too, so every row of the campaign\n     list read a bare `DRAFT`.\n  3. `STATUS_OPTIONS`, a `const` in the report page, carried the old numbering:\n     picking \"Analisis Kelayakan\" filtered for 2004, one state off from the\n     label, and \"Penyusunan Prioritas\" filtered for a step that does not exist.\n  4. `KebutuhanBmnStatus` mirrored in the frontend had the old numbering and\n     had lost 2010 (RevisiWilayah) entirely, so every badge on a request queued\n     for Pusat announced the analysis, and 2010 rendered unlabelled.\n  5. `WorkflowStateCode` in `workflow/config.rs` — old numbering, and dead: no\n     caller outside its own file. Left in place; removing it needs its own\n     check of the \"unused\" premise.\n\nAnd a routing consequence, not just a label one: `sla.rs` found the approver to\nescalate to with `WHERE nama IN (''ANALISIS_KELAYAKAN'', ''APPROVED'')`, which\nresolved through the wrong master to 2004 and 2006. The \"approver\" it found was\ntherefore often the Validator Wilayah who forwarded the request, so SLA\nescalations went to the wrong official. Now derived from the enum''s codes.\n\nFixes, each pointing the same way:\n\n  * The recap query and `vw_kebutuhan_bmn_summary` (V009) join\n    `ms_workflow_status`, keyed by `modul` because codes are only unique within\n    a module. `ms_aktivitas_bmn` stays — pakaian-dinas reads it through\n    `COALESCE(deskripsi, nama)`, which is why it never showed a raw token.\n  * `GET /kebutuhan-bmn/laporan/status-options` serves the filter from the same\n    rows the status column resolves through, replacing the `const`. A\n    hand-written list is what drifted; the fix is to stop keeping one.\n  * The frontend enum mirrors the backend code for code, and the badge mapping\n    it duplicated in two other files now delegates to it. `period_management`\n    also stops labelling 2006 \"Selesai\" and 2008/2010 \"Unknown\".\n  * `is_terminal` is COALESCEd at the source: the column is nullable and this\n    workspace builds release with `panic = \"abort\"`, so a NULL decoded into\n    `bool` would take the process down, not the request.\n\nOne caller had to change with the vocabulary: `/kebutuhan-bmn/search?status=`\nmatched the view''s label exactly, and that label went from `DRAFT` to `Draft`.\nThe comparison is now case-insensitive, so a caller who wrote the old token for\na state whose two masters agreed still works. The tokens that named the WRONG\nstep are deliberately not matched — keeping `ANALISIS_KELAYAKAN` resolvable\nwould keep the mistake reachable through the API. Its test says so in both\ndirections.\n\n`check-fe-be-dto-drift.py` now compares mirrored enums by discriminant as well\nas structs. The struct pass could never have caught this: nothing failed to\ndeserialise, because the code is an integer either way — it silently relabels.\nCanaried by restoring the old numbering, which reports exactly the three\nrenumbered variants.\n\nFour integration tests, canaried against the wrong master.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\n* fix(perlengkapan): every notification title was white text on a white card\n\n`/notifikasi` was written against Tailwind''s light palette while the app is\nnavy. The title `<span>` carried no colour class, so it inherited the app''s\nlight body colour and rendered white-on-white: not one title on the page was\nreadable. \"Tandai dibaca\" and \"Tandai semua dibaca\" were blank rectangles for\nthe same reason — the page''s primary action was invisible.\n\nFour more things the screenshots showed, in the text the backend stores:\n\n  * The module slug was the label. Titles read `penghapusan_bmn: berpindah ke\n    SUBMIT_PUSAT`; both halves are internal identifiers.\n  * The body named the actor by raw id: `oleh\n    33333333-3333-4333-8333-333333333333`.\n  * Timestamps were printed exactly as stored, microseconds and offset\n    included, and stored in UTC — a notification created at 16:26 WIB was shown\n    as 09:26. A wrong time, not just an ugly one.\n  * Priority chips read `URGENT` and `HIGH`, the enum values, on a page that is\n    otherwise Indonesian.\n\nBackend: `module_label`, `state_label` and `role_label` translate the slugs.\n`state_label` resolves through each module''s own status enum rather than a\ntable here — every hand-written copy of that mapping in this repo has drifted\nfrom the enum it copied, so a fifth would have been the fourth to rot. A token\nno enum claims is title-cased, so the worst case is imprecise prose, never a\nraw `SUBMIT_PUSAT`.\n\n`actor_label` returns `None` for a bare UUID and the caller drops the clause.\nWe do not have the person''s name and will not invent one, but printing 36 hex\ncharacters at a reader is not the alternative. The scheduled paths pass the\nliteral \"system\", which does name an actor, and reads \"sistem\".\n\nThis only affects notifications written from here on: title and body are\nrendered at send time and stored, so rows already in the database keep their\nold text.\n\nFrontend: the page now uses the palette the dashboard and laporan pages use.\nUnread is an amber left edge rather than a filled card — on a dark surface a\ntinted card reads as disabled, the opposite of the intent. The row is keyed on\n`read` as well as `id`, because with the id alone \"Tandai dibaca\" updated the\nsignal and left the card unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\n* fix(perlengkapan): four surfaces printed the stored timestamp, and one was seven hours out\n\nThe notification inbox was not the only place a raw RFC 3339 string reached the\nscreen. Once the sweep was scoped to page content instead of the app shell, two\nmore turned up on pages this branch had not touched:\n\n  * `/bantuan/helpdesk` — the \"Tiket Saya\" table''s DIBUAT column reads\n    `2026-08-28T09:28:53.886456Z`, and its PRIORITAS column reads `high`, the\n    `support_tickets_priority_valid` CHECK''s own vocabulary, on an otherwise\n    Indonesian page.\n  * `/bank-aset/dashboard` — \"sinkron terakhir\" the same way; `/bank-aset` detail\n    prints `updated_at` the same way.\n\nThese are stored in UTC, so the hour shown is not merely ugly — it is wrong by\nseven for a reader in WIB. Measured rather than assumed: the same notification\nrenders `09:28` in a UTC browser and `16:28` in `Asia/Jakarta`.\n\n`format_iso_local` now lives in `lib/ui/src/utils/formatters.rs` beside the\nother Indonesian formatters, and all four surfaces use it — including the\nnotification inbox, whose private copy is deleted. A fifth private copy is\nexactly what the rest of this branch has been unpicking. `priority_label` sits\nnext to the `status_label` it was missing from: the ticket table translated one\nand printed the other raw.\n\nThe sweep harness needed three corrections of its own, each one a way of\nlooking without seeing:\n\n  * Its route list grepped `path!(\"…\")` without reading the nesting, so the\n    seven children of `<ParentRoute path=path!(\"/admin\")>` came out as `/roles`,\n    `/audit`, `/master` and so on. None is a URL this app serves — 24 of the 99\n    screenshots were of the 404 page, filed under \"halaman-nyaris-kosong\", a\n    content observation about a page that does not exist. The admin surfaces had\n    therefore never been swept at all. `_routes.py` walks the nesting, the sweep\n    derives the list on every run, and a 404 is now reported as `RUTE-404` — a\n    statement about the route, not about its contents.\n  * `innerText` returns text after `text-transform: uppercase`, so every styled\n    table header looked like a raw enum and the capital-word rule flagged 87\n    pages. It reads `textContent` now.\n  * Its fixed 4500 ms wait was shorter than `/bank-aset/dashboard` takes against\n    real staging data (4.75 s over 624 533 rows), so the dashboard was\n    photographed mid-skeleton. It waits for the page''s own traffic to settle.\n\nThat last measurement is worth recording on its own: the dashboard''s headline\nnumbers are blank for nearly five seconds. Not addressed here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\n* fix(perlengkapan): the helpdesk said \"Tinggi\" in its form and \"high\" in its table\n\nSame page, same value, two vocabularies — and my first fix would have made it\nthree. `priority_label` was written out by hand as \"Penting\"/\"Segera\" while\n`PRIORITY_OPTIONS`, twenty lines above the table it feeds, has always rendered\n\"Tinggi\"/\"Mendesak\" in the submit form.\n\nThe list moves next to `status_label` in `api/bantuan.rs` and `priority_label`\nlooks its answer up in it. Restating four arms is precisely how a page ends up\nnaming one value two ways, which is the whole subject of this branch.\n\nThe form''s `<option value>` is untouched, so `helpdesk-priority` still\n`selectOption(''high'')` in the e2e spec.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\n* test(e2e): track the visual sweep, because re-deriving it got it wrong\n\nThe exhaustive per-route screenshot sweep found every defect in this branch, and\nit lived in a scratch directory. Kept out of the repo it is rewritten from\nmemory each session — and on 2026-08-29 the rewrite was wrong in four ways, each\none a report of full coverage over a hole:\n\n  * The route list grepped `path!(\"…\")` without reading the nesting, so the\n    seven children of `<ParentRoute path=path!(\"/admin\")>` came out as `/roles`,\n    `/audit`, `/master` and so on. 24 of 99 screenshots were of the 404 page and\n    the admin surfaces had never been visited. `_routes.py` walks the nesting\n    and the sweep re-derives on every run.\n  * The user list was hand-written with three entries; the seed has eight. The\n    admin''s pages, both satker-chain roles, the second operator and the pegawai\n    had never been photographed. Derived from `seed-multisatker.sql` now, and it\n    throws rather than returning an empty list.\n  * A 404 and a 403 were both filed as \"halaman-nyaris-kosong\" — a remark about\n    the contents of a page that does not exist, or that the reader is not\n    allowed to open. They are `RUTE-404` and `AKSES-DITOLAK` now, matched on the\n    app''s own copy rather than on a bare `404` (an asset count of 404 is not a\n    dead route).\n  * A fixed 4500 ms wait was shorter than `/bank-aset/dashboard` takes against\n    real staging data, so the dashboard was photographed mid-skeleton. It waits\n    for the page''s own traffic to settle.\n\nThe `**/*.js` ignore it fell under is about wasm-bindgen output, so the\nexception is narrow and scoped to the e2e directory.\n\nOne heuristic is deliberately left noisy rather than removed, with the reason\nwritten down: flagging single capitalised words does not work here, because\nsatker names are stored uppercase (`KEJAKSAAN NEGERI JAKARTA PUSAT`) and it\ntherefore flags correct data on nearly every page. The SCREAMING_SNAKE rule is\nthe one that earns its place.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\n* test(e2e): the sweep printed a coverage number it had not earned\n\nThe run logged `pegawai-bandung: login 401`, skipped that role, and then printed\n\"32 rute x 8 peran = 256 screenshot\" over 224 files on disk. The failure was\nvisible and the summary contradicted it — which is the same shape as every\ndefect this branch has been unpicking: a report of full coverage over a hole.\n\nTwo changes:\n\n  * A role that cannot log in is a finding (`LOGIN-GAGAL … peran ini TIDAK\n    tersapu`), not a line in the log, and the roles it skipped are named again\n    at the end.\n  * The summary counts the roles actually swept instead of multiplying the\n    planned matrix.\n\nThe underlying mismatch is worth stating: the user list is derived from\n`tests/fixtures/e2e/seed-multisatker.sql`, which seeds the CI stack, while this\nharness points at staging. `200000000000000009` exists in that fixture and\nanswers 401 on staging (verified directly), so deriving from the fixture\nover-promises against this target. Left as-is deliberately — the fixture is\nstill the right source for \"which roles should exist\", and the run now says\nplainly which of them it could not reach.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\n* fix(perlengkapan): two pages were white cards on a navy app, and one was unreadable\n\nSame defect as the notification inbox, on two pages the sweep reached only once\nits route list was fixed.\n\n`/pengelolaan/pemakaian/monitoring` is the serious one. Seven white cards, and\ninside them most of the table cannot be read: satker name, item name, employee,\ndate range and status all render light grey on white. Only the second line of\neach cell — the codes and the day counts — survives. The page heading sits\noutside the cards and is dark grey on navy, so it is barely visible either, and\nboth pager buttons are blank.\n\n`/analitik/roadmap/buat` is milder: a white form card whose two selects show\ntheir placeholder in light grey on a light grey field.\n\nBoth are mechanical palette swaps onto the pairs the rest of the app already\nuses (`helpdesk.rs`, `kebutuhan_bmn_list.rs`), so no new vocabulary is\nintroduced — these two pages simply stop being the exception.\n\nA census of what is left, so it is not buried: 17 more solid `bg-white`\ncontainers across 8 files, of which `bank_aset/qrcode_page.rs` is correct (it\nis a print surface) and the `batch_operations_toolbar` ones are modals that may\nbe contrasting on purpose. They are NOT changed here. Each needs its own look\nat a screenshot before being touched — converting them from a grep is exactly\nthe unverified sweeping change the rest of this branch argues against.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\n* fix(perlengkapan): my own palette swap produced seven invalid classes\n\nCaught by reading the after-screenshot I took to prove the previous commit, which\nis the only reason it was caught at all.\n\nTwo defects, both mine:\n\n  * The swap list re-substituted its own output. `bg-white rounded-lg shadow-sm\n    border border-gray-100` became `… bg-white/[0.04]`, and the later plain\n    `bg-white` rule then hit that result again, yielding\n    `bg-white/[0.04]/[0.04]` — not a class Tailwind emits anything for. Seven of\n    them, every card on the page I had just declared fixed. A mechanical\n    substitution has to be checked against its own output, not only against its\n    input.\n  * Three form controls carried no colour class at all, so a swap keyed on\n    `text-gray-*` / `bg-white` could not see them. On a dark app that leaves\n    the browser default: the \"Berdasarkan NUP BMN\" select was still unreadable\n    in the after-shot, directly beneath a table I had just made legible.\n\n`_shoot.js` is tracked alongside the sweep. It takes after-shots for named\nroutes without re-running all 256, and the before/after obligation is the\nmechanism that found both of the above.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\n* fix(perlengkapan): clippy gates the wasm target, and I had been linting the host\n\nFive hard-gate errors that `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets` never showed\nme, because the frontend crates are dual-cfg and CI lints them for\n`wasm32-unknown-unknown` while a workspace run lints them for the host. The code\npaths differ; `map_err(Into::into)` is a real conversion on one and an identity\non the other.\n\n  * `dashboard.rs` — `useless_conversion`. This is the SAME lint that reddened\n    #878, where I wrote that the lesson was about my output filter. The filter\n    was half of it. The target was the other half, and I fixed the half I had\n    noticed.\n  * `dashboard_panels.rs` ×4 — `unnecessary_sort_by` on descending sorts;\n    `sort_by_key(Reverse(..))` says the intent more plainly anyway.\n  * `satker_scope.rs` — `items_after_test_module`: `narrow_for_request` had been\n    appended below `#[cfg(test)] mod tests`, so 119 lines of production code sat\n    after the tests. Moved above.\n\nVerified by running the gate the way CI runs it, per crate, with each crate''s\nown target and scope taken from `ci.yml` rather than approximated — and the\nextraction of that matrix is itself worth a note: the first version required\n`extra_args` to precede `scope` and silently produced 10 entries out of 12,\ndropping exactly the two wasm frontends this commit is about. It now refuses to\nemit a runner it cannot fully derive.\n\nOnly the four crates this branch touches were re-run (`antarmuka/perlengkapan`,\n`antarmuka/portal`, `layanan/perlengkapan`, `lib/ui`); the other eight are\nuntouched and already green on CI.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"31b7e22838092f436ef31cdac4eb3c8e966854e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/trees/31b7e22838092f436ef31cdac4eb3c8e966854e5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/commits/f4585cf4f25dd3808308f0cc5da508c59b6df17a","verification":{"payload":"tree 31b7e22838092f436ef31cdac4eb3c8e966854e5\nparent a5be3132fe147ce63e07425d74ead7f33a8fd102\nauthor analisaperlengkapan <analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com> 1788034313 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788034313 +0700\n\nfeat(perlengkapan): the dashboard redesign, and what its screenshot sweep found (#879)\n\n* feat(perlengkapan): the dashboard shows what the backend has been computing all along\n\nSeven aggregates reached no screen. `/dashboard/perlengkapan` computes kebutuhan\nstatus, gap analysis, uniform-size distribution, workflow bottlenecks, SLA\nbreaches and the permit/removal status splits — and had no frontend caller at\nall (#97), which is why the 500 it used to return went unnoticed until an e2e\nprobed it directly (#116). The landing page rendered four numbers.\n\nThis wires it, and reorders the page around how it is read: what the asset base\nlooks like, what needs a decision today, then the analysis behind both.\n\n  * KPI row now carries SHARE as well as count. 76 459 damaged assets is not a\n    number anyone can reason with; 12,2% of 624 533 is.\n  * \"Perlu Tindakan\": SLA breaches, mean processing hours, permit and removal\n    volumes.\n  * \"Analisis Aset\": composition by SIMAN taxonomy, acquisition VALUE by\n    taxonomy (a second panel, not a second column — Tanah is 0,3% of units and a\n    fifth of the value, and a count-only view hides where the money is),\n    acquisition trend per year, and a satker ranking for tiers that oversee more\n    than one satker.\n  * \"Kebutuhan & Alur\": status split, bottleneck queue, request trend, per-satker\n    requests, and the gap table — surplus shown as surplus rather than clamped,\n    because \"asked for 3, holds 1 903\" is the more useful sentence.\n  * \"Perlengkapan & Pengelolaan\": uniform-size distribution (the figure\n    procurement orders against) and the two module status splits.\n\nCharts are new primitives in `lib/ui/components/charts/primitives.rs`: plain\nSVG, no chart dependency, colours and container class as props. The reason the\nexisting in-house widgets (`components::dashboard`, 821 lines, plus\n`monitoring_dashboard`, 439) have never had a single user is that they hard-code\n`bg-white dark:bg-gray-800` — every one of them would arrive as a white card in\nthe middle of a navy-and-gold design system. Colour is never the only carrier of\nmeaning here: every series is named and its value written out, and each chart\nexposes `role=\"img\"` with an aria-label carrying the numbers.\n\nNo sample data anywhere. Every figure is a query result from one of two\nserver-scoped endpoints; where the backend has no such measurement the panel\nsays so rather than drawing something plausible. `asset_utilization` is\ndeliberately NOT mirrored — it is a third count of \"how many assets, how many in\ngood condition\", the question the condition cards already answer, and putting\ntwo independently-computed answers to one question on one screen is the fault\nthis page was just consolidated to remove.\n\n\"Real time\" is polling, and the page says so: both queries refetch every 60 s,\nand the header stamps the moment the last load landed, with a manual refresh\nbeside it. It deliberately does NOT subscribe to `/dashboard/ws`. That socket\nauthenticates and then delivers nothing, because `broadcast_dashboard_update`\nhas no callers anywhere in the backend — subscribing would look like live push\nand be a spinner that never turns. (If it is ever given producers: the broadcast\nis unscoped, so per-satker fan-out has to come first.)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\n* feat(perlengkapan): the dashboard can be drilled into, and the drill cannot dig sideways\n\nPusat asked for \"show me one region, or one satker\"; a wilayah validator for\n\"one satker in my region\". A satker operator needs neither — their scope is\nalready a single satker.\n\nThe obvious shape is an extra `AND satker = $n` on each query. That is wrong\nhere in a specific way: this module applies a scope in THIRTEEN places, and a\nfilter that lives beside the scope rather than inside it is one refactor away\nfrom being applied INSTEAD of it. That is not hypothetical — it is exactly what\n#871 was: `?satker_id=` on the laporan export replaced the scope instead of\nnarrowing it, and a nationwide report came back.\n\nSo the drill-down is a scope TRANSFORM, not a condition:\n\n    SatkerScope::narrowed_to(code, in_scope) -> Satker(code) | Denied\n    SatkerScope::narrowed_to_wilayah(w, caller_w) -> WilayahKode(w) | Denied\n    AsetScope::   (the same pair, mirrored)\n\n`narrow_for_request` resolves what the request asked for against what the claims\ngrant and hands back a scope that is narrower or `Denied` — never wider. All\nthirteen application sites inherit it without knowing the feature exists, and\n\"a filter cannot widen\" stops being a convention about statement order and\nbecomes a property of the value.\n\nAdding the `WilayahKode` variant made the compiler name the three predicates\nthat had to learn it (the kebutuhan recap and both campaign-visibility\nbuilders). A hand-kept list would have found none of them.\n\nTHE TWO WILAYAH CODES ARE NOT THE SAME CODE. `SatkerScope` compares the Kejati''s\nMySIMKARI `wilayah_code`; `AsetScope` compares SIMAN''s `wilayah_kode` (digits\n6-9 of `kdsatker_keu`). They are a measured bijection but different values, so\n`narrow_for_request` TRANSLATES between them via `v_satker_code_map`. Passing\none string to both — which is what I wrote first — scopes the perlengkapan half\nto nothing while the SIMAN half narrows correctly: a half-filtered dashboard,\nwhich is worse than an unfiltered one because it looks like it worked.\n\nAlso here, because the filters need somewhere real to come from:\n\n  * `/bank-aset/dashboard` now takes the same filter set as the list, through\n    ONE shared `AsetFilter` + `push_asset_filters`. The summary used to ignore\n    every filter, so narrowing the table below left the totals above describing\n    the whole population.\n  * `/bank-aset/filter-options` gains `satker_kode` (value = `kdsatker_keu`,\n    label = name) and `wilayah` (value = the SIMAN region code, label from\n    `v_satker_wilayah`). The existing name-keyed `satker` list is untouched so\n    the Bank Aset page keeps working — but names collide (554 distinct names for\n    556 distinct codes) and the drill-down keys on the code.\n  * acquisition-date bounds, compared as TEXT. `tgl_perlh` IS text and all\n    624 533 staging rows are ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` (measured: zero exceptions), for\n    which lexicographic and calendar order agree. A `::date` cast is equivalent\n    today and throws on the first malformed row a future ingest writes — and\n    `panic = \"abort\"` makes that the process, not the request.\n  * the pemakaian/penghapusan rekaps resolve their status labels from\n    `ms_workflow_status` instead of printing the raw column: users were reading\n    `KONSEP_SK_GENERATED`, `SUBMIT_WILAYAH`, `SUBMIT_PUSAT`, `ACTIVE`. The\n    kebutuhan rekap beside them already did this. The first fallback I wrote\n    produced \"Kode DRAFT\" for a row with no code; the test caught it.\n  * the trend axis thins its labels — twenty-eight acquisition years rendered\n    as an unbroken bar of digits.\n\nTests: a drill-down returns exactly the drilled satker''s own view (asserted\nequal to that operator''s own dashboard); an operator naming another satker gets\nzeros, not that satker; a wilayah validator reaches a satker in their region and\nnot one outside it; the exports resolve the drill-down the same way. Canary:\nremoving the fail-closed branch makes the operator see SKR002''s 2 assets, and\nthe test goes red on exactly that.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\n* feat(perlengkapan): the dashboard filter bar, offering only what its reader can act on\n\nBackend already accepted the drill-down; this is the control for it.\n\nTier-aware because the tiers genuinely differ: pusat picks a region and then a\nsatker, a wilayah validator picks a satker (their region is fixed by their\nclaims, so a region selector would offer nothing they could widen to), and a\nsatker operator gets no selector at all — their scope IS one satker, so the\ncontrol would show a single option that changes nothing.\n\nThe options come from `/bank-aset/filter-options`, which is scoped server-side:\nmeasured on staging it answers 1 satker to an operator, 7 to a wilayah validator\nand 554 to pusat. So the dropdown cannot offer a satker its reader may not see,\nand the server refuses it regardless.\n\nTwo things worth stating:\n\n  * the satker option''s VALUE is now the MySIMKARI `kode_satker`, not\n    `kdsatker_keu`. One selection has to narrow both halves of the dashboard,\n    and they key on different codes; unifying on the canonical identity (#43,\n    #94) means the server maps it where needed instead of the frontend guessing\n    which code a given endpoint wants.\n  * selecting a region re-fetches the OPTIONS as well as the data, so the satker\n    list shrinks to that region. The first version filtered the list in the\n    browser by slicing digits 6-9 out of the code — a frontend re-implementing\n    how a satker code is composed, which is the kind of assumption that is right\n    until the day it is not.\n\nFilters are part of the query key, so a selection refetches rather than being\nanswered from cache.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\n* fix(ui): a comparison in a view! attribute ends the tag, so 26 controls were inert\n\n`view!` tokenises `>` as the end of the opening tag — inside an attribute value\ntoo. So this does not compile to what it reads as:\n\n    prop:disabled=move || page.get() >= total_pages\n    on:click=next_handler\n\nThe macro closes the tag at the `>`. Everything after it becomes a text node:\n\n  * `on:click` is never attached — the button does nothing.\n  * `prop:disabled` receives an `i32`, truthy for every page but 0, so the\n    button is also disabled.\n  * The Rust source renders on the page. Users read\n    `= total_pages on : click = move | _ | on_next.run(()) >Selanjutnya`\n    between the pager arrows.\n\nThe fix is a brace group, which the tokeniser reads as one token tree:\n\n    prop:disabled=move || { page.get() >= total_pages }\n\n26 attribute values across both frontends and `lib/ui`, `DarkPagination` among\nthem. No paginated list in either app could reach page two.\n\nWhat let it live, and a correction to my own first fix\n-----------------------------------------------------\n`cargo check` sees valid markup and a valid text node. No test clicks page two.\nA route sweep loads the page happily. The one honest signal is rustc reporting\nthe callback as an unused variable, and it had been silenced two different\nways: a hand-written `#[allow(unused_variables)]` on `DarkPagination` and\n`PaginationControls`, whose comments asserted the lint was mistaken; and\n`_`-prefix renames on a component prop (`_total_pages`) and two handlers\n(`_next_handler`). The second form leaves no `#[allow]` to grep for.\n\nI first read this as a formatter accident and \"fixed\" it by rejoining the `>=`\nonto the attribute line without bracing it. That silently reproduced the bug:\nthe guard I had just written went green while the handler was still detached,\nbecause it matched the reflowed *shape* rather than the cause. It was also\nblind to `pemakaian_bmn_monitoring.rs`, still on one line and never reflowed.\nThe guard now tests the cause — an attribute closure whose body carries a bare\n`<` or `>` outside any bracket group — and is canaried in both directions,\nincluding the one-line variant. Verification is the absence of the\n`unused variable` warnings, not the guard''s own green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\n* fix(perlengkapan): one workflow, two numberings, and the wrong one named the step\n\nTwo master tables describe the kebutuhan-BMN workflow and they part ways at\n2004:\n\n    kode  KebutuhanBmnStatus (writes the column)   ms_aktivitas_bmn (was joined)\n    2002  SubmitWilayah  \"Diajukan ke Validator Wilayah\"   SUBMIT_SATKER\n    2004  SubmitPusat    \"Diajukan ke Validator Pusat\"     ANALISIS_KELAYAKAN\n    2005  AnalisisKelayakan \"Analisis Kelayakan\"           PENYUSUNAN_PRIORITAS\n\n`ms_workflow_status` agrees with the enum. `ms_aktivitas_bmn` does not, and\n`PENYUSUNAN_PRIORITAS` is a step the workflow config itself records as merged\naway and never separate.\n\nThis was not a cosmetic problem. Reading the wrong master told a Validator\nPusat that a request merely *queued* for them was already under feasibility\nanalysis, and it did so on the report they use to triage.\n\nFive copies of the numbering, one of them right:\n\n  1. `ms_aktivitas_bmn` seed (V002) — old numbering, and its `nama` is the\n     machine token, so `/kebutuhan-bmn/laporan` printed `SUBMIT_SATKER` and\n     `ANALISIS_KELAYAKAN` verbatim.\n  2. `vw_kebutuhan_bmn_summary` joined it too, so every row of the campaign\n     list read a bare `DRAFT`.\n  3. `STATUS_OPTIONS`, a `const` in the report page, carried the old numbering:\n     picking \"Analisis Kelayakan\" filtered for 2004, one state off from the\n     label, and \"Penyusunan Prioritas\" filtered for a step that does not exist.\n  4. `KebutuhanBmnStatus` mirrored in the frontend had the old numbering and\n     had lost 2010 (RevisiWilayah) entirely, so every badge on a request queued\n     for Pusat announced the analysis, and 2010 rendered unlabelled.\n  5. `WorkflowStateCode` in `workflow/config.rs` — old numbering, and dead: no\n     caller outside its own file. Left in place; removing it needs its own\n     check of the \"unused\" premise.\n\nAnd a routing consequence, not just a label one: `sla.rs` found the approver to\nescalate to with `WHERE nama IN (''ANALISIS_KELAYAKAN'', ''APPROVED'')`, which\nresolved through the wrong master to 2004 and 2006. The \"approver\" it found was\ntherefore often the Validator Wilayah who forwarded the request, so SLA\nescalations went to the wrong official. Now derived from the enum''s codes.\n\nFixes, each pointing the same way:\n\n  * The recap query and `vw_kebutuhan_bmn_summary` (V009) join\n    `ms_workflow_status`, keyed by `modul` because codes are only unique within\n    a module. `ms_aktivitas_bmn` stays — pakaian-dinas reads it through\n    `COALESCE(deskripsi, nama)`, which is why it never showed a raw token.\n  * `GET /kebutuhan-bmn/laporan/status-options` serves the filter from the same\n    rows the status column resolves through, replacing the `const`. A\n    hand-written list is what drifted; the fix is to stop keeping one.\n  * The frontend enum mirrors the backend code for code, and the badge mapping\n    it duplicated in two other files now delegates to it. `period_management`\n    also stops labelling 2006 \"Selesai\" and 2008/2010 \"Unknown\".\n  * `is_terminal` is COALESCEd at the source: the column is nullable and this\n    workspace builds release with `panic = \"abort\"`, so a NULL decoded into\n    `bool` would take the process down, not the request.\n\nOne caller had to change with the vocabulary: `/kebutuhan-bmn/search?status=`\nmatched the view''s label exactly, and that label went from `DRAFT` to `Draft`.\nThe comparison is now case-insensitive, so a caller who wrote the old token for\na state whose two masters agreed still works. The tokens that named the WRONG\nstep are deliberately not matched — keeping `ANALISIS_KELAYAKAN` resolvable\nwould keep the mistake reachable through the API. Its test says so in both\ndirections.\n\n`check-fe-be-dto-drift.py` now compares mirrored enums by discriminant as well\nas structs. The struct pass could never have caught this: nothing failed to\ndeserialise, because the code is an integer either way — it silently relabels.\nCanaried by restoring the old numbering, which reports exactly the three\nrenumbered variants.\n\nFour integration tests, canaried against the wrong master.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\n* fix(perlengkapan): every notification title was white text on a white card\n\n`/notifikasi` was written against Tailwind''s light palette while the app is\nnavy. The title `<span>` carried no colour class, so it inherited the app''s\nlight body colour and rendered white-on-white: not one title on the page was\nreadable. \"Tandai dibaca\" and \"Tandai semua dibaca\" were blank rectangles for\nthe same reason — the page''s primary action was invisible.\n\nFour more things the screenshots showed, in the text the backend stores:\n\n  * The module slug was the label. Titles read `penghapusan_bmn: berpindah ke\n    SUBMIT_PUSAT`; both halves are internal identifiers.\n  * The body named the actor by raw id: `oleh\n    33333333-3333-4333-8333-333333333333`.\n  * Timestamps were printed exactly as stored, microseconds and offset\n    included, and stored in UTC — a notification created at 16:26 WIB was shown\n    as 09:26. A wrong time, not just an ugly one.\n  * Priority chips read `URGENT` and `HIGH`, the enum values, on a page that is\n    otherwise Indonesian.\n\nBackend: `module_label`, `state_label` and `role_label` translate the slugs.\n`state_label` resolves through each module''s own status enum rather than a\ntable here — every hand-written copy of that mapping in this repo has drifted\nfrom the enum it copied, so a fifth would have been the fourth to rot. A token\nno enum claims is title-cased, so the worst case is imprecise prose, never a\nraw `SUBMIT_PUSAT`.\n\n`actor_label` returns `None` for a bare UUID and the caller drops the clause.\nWe do not have the person''s name and will not invent one, but printing 36 hex\ncharacters at a reader is not the alternative. The scheduled paths pass the\nliteral \"system\", which does name an actor, and reads \"sistem\".\n\nThis only affects notifications written from here on: title and body are\nrendered at send time and stored, so rows already in the database keep their\nold text.\n\nFrontend: the page now uses the palette the dashboard and laporan pages use.\nUnread is an amber left edge rather than a filled card — on a dark surface a\ntinted card reads as disabled, the opposite of the intent. The row is keyed on\n`read` as well as `id`, because with the id alone \"Tandai dibaca\" updated the\nsignal and left the card unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\n* fix(perlengkapan): four surfaces printed the stored timestamp, and one was seven hours out\n\nThe notification inbox was not the only place a raw RFC 3339 string reached the\nscreen. Once the sweep was scoped to page content instead of the app shell, two\nmore turned up on pages this branch had not touched:\n\n  * `/bantuan/helpdesk` — the \"Tiket Saya\" table''s DIBUAT column reads\n    `2026-08-28T09:28:53.886456Z`, and its PRIORITAS column reads `high`, the\n    `support_tickets_priority_valid` CHECK''s own vocabulary, on an otherwise\n    Indonesian page.\n  * `/bank-aset/dashboard` — \"sinkron terakhir\" the same way; `/bank-aset` detail\n    prints `updated_at` the same way.\n\nThese are stored in UTC, so the hour shown is not merely ugly — it is wrong by\nseven for a reader in WIB. Measured rather than assumed: the same notification\nrenders `09:28` in a UTC browser and `16:28` in `Asia/Jakarta`.\n\n`format_iso_local` now lives in `lib/ui/src/utils/formatters.rs` beside the\nother Indonesian formatters, and all four surfaces use it — including the\nnotification inbox, whose private copy is deleted. A fifth private copy is\nexactly what the rest of this branch has been unpicking. `priority_label` sits\nnext to the `status_label` it was missing from: the ticket table translated one\nand printed the other raw.\n\nThe sweep harness needed three corrections of its own, each one a way of\nlooking without seeing:\n\n  * Its route list grepped `path!(\"…\")` without reading the nesting, so the\n    seven children of `<ParentRoute path=path!(\"/admin\")>` came out as `/roles`,\n    `/audit`, `/master` and so on. None is a URL this app serves — 24 of the 99\n    screenshots were of the 404 page, filed under \"halaman-nyaris-kosong\", a\n    content observation about a page that does not exist. The admin surfaces had\n    therefore never been swept at all. `_routes.py` walks the nesting, the sweep\n    derives the list on every run, and a 404 is now reported as `RUTE-404` — a\n    statement about the route, not about its contents.\n  * `innerText` returns text after `text-transform: uppercase`, so every styled\n    table header looked like a raw enum and the capital-word rule flagged 87\n    pages. It reads `textContent` now.\n  * Its fixed 4500 ms wait was shorter than `/bank-aset/dashboard` takes against\n    real staging data (4.75 s over 624 533 rows), so the dashboard was\n    photographed mid-skeleton. It waits for the page''s own traffic to settle.\n\nThat last measurement is worth recording on its own: the dashboard''s headline\nnumbers are blank for nearly five seconds. Not addressed here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\n* fix(perlengkapan): the helpdesk said \"Tinggi\" in its form and \"high\" in its table\n\nSame page, same value, two vocabularies — and my first fix would have made it\nthree. `priority_label` was written out by hand as \"Penting\"/\"Segera\" while\n`PRIORITY_OPTIONS`, twenty lines above the table it feeds, has always rendered\n\"Tinggi\"/\"Mendesak\" in the submit form.\n\nThe list moves next to `status_label` in `api/bantuan.rs` and `priority_label`\nlooks its answer up in it. Restating four arms is precisely how a page ends up\nnaming one value two ways, which is the whole subject of this branch.\n\nThe form''s `<option value>` is untouched, so `helpdesk-priority` still\n`selectOption(''high'')` in the e2e spec.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\n* test(e2e): track the visual sweep, because re-deriving it got it wrong\n\nThe exhaustive per-route screenshot sweep found every defect in this branch, and\nit lived in a scratch directory. Kept out of the repo it is rewritten from\nmemory each session — and on 2026-08-29 the rewrite was wrong in four ways, each\none a report of full coverage over a hole:\n\n  * The route list grepped `path!(\"…\")` without reading the nesting, so the\n    seven children of `<ParentRoute path=path!(\"/admin\")>` came out as `/roles`,\n    `/audit`, `/master` and so on. 24 of 99 screenshots were of the 404 page and\n    the admin surfaces had never been visited. `_routes.py` walks the nesting\n    and the sweep re-derives on every run.\n  * The user list was hand-written with three entries; the seed has eight. The\n    admin''s pages, both satker-chain roles, the second operator and the pegawai\n    had never been photographed. Derived from `seed-multisatker.sql` now, and it\n    throws rather than returning an empty list.\n  * A 404 and a 403 were both filed as \"halaman-nyaris-kosong\" — a remark about\n    the contents of a page that does not exist, or that the reader is not\n    allowed to open. They are `RUTE-404` and `AKSES-DITOLAK` now, matched on the\n    app''s own copy rather than on a bare `404` (an asset count of 404 is not a\n    dead route).\n  * A fixed 4500 ms wait was shorter than `/bank-aset/dashboard` takes against\n    real staging data, so the dashboard was photographed mid-skeleton. It waits\n    for the page''s own traffic to settle.\n\nThe `**/*.js` ignore it fell under is about wasm-bindgen output, so the\nexception is narrow and scoped to the e2e directory.\n\nOne heuristic is deliberately left noisy rather than removed, with the reason\nwritten down: flagging single capitalised words does not work here, because\nsatker names are stored uppercase (`KEJAKSAAN NEGERI JAKARTA PUSAT`) and it\ntherefore flags correct data on nearly every page. The SCREAMING_SNAKE rule is\nthe one that earns its place.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\n* test(e2e): the sweep printed a coverage number it had not earned\n\nThe run logged `pegawai-bandung: login 401`, skipped that role, and then printed\n\"32 rute x 8 peran = 256 screenshot\" over 224 files on disk. The failure was\nvisible and the summary contradicted it — which is the same shape as every\ndefect this branch has been unpicking: a report of full coverage over a hole.\n\nTwo changes:\n\n  * A role that cannot log in is a finding (`LOGIN-GAGAL … peran ini TIDAK\n    tersapu`), not a line in the log, and the roles it skipped are named again\n    at the end.\n  * The summary counts the roles actually swept instead of multiplying the\n    planned matrix.\n\nThe underlying mismatch is worth stating: the user list is derived from\n`tests/fixtures/e2e/seed-multisatker.sql`, which seeds the CI stack, while this\nharness points at staging. `200000000000000009` exists in that fixture and\nanswers 401 on staging (verified directly), so deriving from the fixture\nover-promises against this target. Left as-is deliberately — the fixture is\nstill the right source for \"which roles should exist\", and the run now says\nplainly which of them it could not reach.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\n* fix(perlengkapan): two pages were white cards on a navy app, and one was unreadable\n\nSame defect as the notification inbox, on two pages the sweep reached only once\nits route list was fixed.\n\n`/pengelolaan/pemakaian/monitoring` is the serious one. Seven white cards, and\ninside them most of the table cannot be read: satker name, item name, employee,\ndate range and status all render light grey on white. Only the second line of\neach cell — the codes and the day counts — survives. The page heading sits\noutside the cards and is dark grey on navy, so it is barely visible either, and\nboth pager buttons are blank.\n\n`/analitik/roadmap/buat` is milder: a white form card whose two selects show\ntheir placeholder in light grey on a light grey field.\n\nBoth are mechanical palette swaps onto the pairs the rest of the app already\nuses (`helpdesk.rs`, `kebutuhan_bmn_list.rs`), so no new vocabulary is\nintroduced — these two pages simply stop being the exception.\n\nA census of what is left, so it is not buried: 17 more solid `bg-white`\ncontainers across 8 files, of which `bank_aset/qrcode_page.rs` is correct (it\nis a print surface) and the `batch_operations_toolbar` ones are modals that may\nbe contrasting on purpose. They are NOT changed here. Each needs its own look\nat a screenshot before being touched — converting them from a grep is exactly\nthe unverified sweeping change the rest of this branch argues against.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\n* fix(perlengkapan): my own palette swap produced seven invalid classes\n\nCaught by reading the after-screenshot I took to prove the previous commit, which\nis the only reason it was caught at all.\n\nTwo defects, both mine:\n\n  * The swap list re-substituted its own output. `bg-white rounded-lg shadow-sm\n    border border-gray-100` became `… bg-white/[0.04]`, and the later plain\n    `bg-white` rule then hit that result again, yielding\n    `bg-white/[0.04]/[0.04]` — not a class Tailwind emits anything for. Seven of\n    them, every card on the page I had just declared fixed. A mechanical\n    substitution has to be checked against its own output, not only against its\n    input.\n  * Three form controls carried no colour class at all, so a swap keyed on\n    `text-gray-*` / `bg-white` could not see them. On a dark app that leaves\n    the browser default: the \"Berdasarkan NUP BMN\" select was still unreadable\n    in the after-shot, directly beneath a table I had just made legible.\n\n`_shoot.js` is tracked alongside the sweep. It takes after-shots for named\nroutes without re-running all 256, and the before/after obligation is the\nmechanism that found both of the above.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\n* fix(perlengkapan): clippy gates the wasm target, and I had been linting the host\n\nFive hard-gate errors that `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets` never showed\nme, because the frontend crates are dual-cfg and CI lints them for\n`wasm32-unknown-unknown` while a workspace run lints them for the host. The code\npaths differ; `map_err(Into::into)` is a real conversion on one and an identity\non the other.\n\n  * `dashboard.rs` — `useless_conversion`. This is the SAME lint that reddened\n    #878, where I wrote that the lesson was about my output filter. The filter\n    was half of it. The target was the other half, and I fixed the half I had\n    noticed.\n  * `dashboard_panels.rs` ×4 — `unnecessary_sort_by` on descending sorts;\n    `sort_by_key(Reverse(..))` says the intent more plainly anyway.\n  * `satker_scope.rs` — `items_after_test_module`: `narrow_for_request` had been\n    appended below `#[cfg(test)] mod tests`, so 119 lines of production code sat\n    after the tests. Moved above.\n\nVerified by running the gate the way CI runs it, per crate, with each crate''s\nown target and scope taken from `ci.yml` rather than approximated — and the\nextraction of that matrix is itself worth a note: the first version required\n`extra_args` to precede `scope` and silently produced 10 entries out of 12,\ndropping exactly the two wasm frontends this commit is about. It now refuses to\nemit a runner it cannot fully derive.\n\nOnly the four crates this branch touches were re-run (`antarmuka/perlengkapan`,\n`antarmuka/portal`, `layanan/perlengkapan`, `lib/ui`); the other eight are\nuntouched and already green on CI.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkz0JCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARQkQAJf9ubbtx0DfiYD8jQU6VS7n\nYz6aIO1NDPZRYLOjl6z/doYzvrJzCNXdMa37T3EYmQJwhFFhLvZ6mGpyeAER4bxE\nHwSS14T079YyK1l7NshH1z62l16lag5y5zrJJM/jUrkFjJldfIMCNslrq5Wx47gT\nZugnIp6OiFiDY7NsbDnSyGHXaNkTHkVJWmDVzlRuFvhDipGQtMaHsySUuecec9/G\nY8X0i8W3NqqeRIXoOWgA8RsN0b5iQBp9hE3LL+ZaX1H++2hfZ+jI7ZZcY+RiJKzO\n/O934TysYv1i3eDVpwCUAj/LsmcsX37Ac6H+hC1KvhOxL3kLeqriyKN6QafPNCWz\nicoZzH+BNxxgVjP3Kb7qMHgscwRvgNB7mgwQoBuaR1n+NLmg0Ux+O4O1de/IZEBi\nKcGZj46SzIXGA5i9258bhF/ezxeNESsYlhEnSaPaPSaZBzWoL0089loo2V29ifvl\nEdDGxWlqGm0ylCSZ5T+V1QrPqMhV+jwnN+2yeUumVCw7K4/+mpiMEVzStw4EcOHd\n3Blq1hpzYddGajR5+fVylZgGpy8B2ChqZbCXQNjPTzPKg6GYyxB0sEwDvIkLOFAH\nuVAQPSlhW0bmRC5ZfG45XhIvSJ5DZkrDsl5Z33PBdjHV8GUp0coibusByq/eyqdk\ngEHaVAf8rYUMBkSK15Q8\n=NFli\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-29T20:11:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/f4585cf4f25dd3808308f0cc5da508c59b6df17a","node_id":"C_kwDOP93DxNoAKGY0NTg1Y2Y0ZjI1ZGQzODA4MzA4ZjBjYzVkYTUwOGM1OWI2ZGYxN2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/a5be3132fe147ce63e07425d74ead7f33a8fd102","sha":"a5be3132fe147ce63e07425d74ead7f33a8fd102","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/a5be3132fe147ce63e07425d74ead7f33a8fd102"}],"sha":"f4585cf4f25dd3808308f0cc5da508c59b6df17a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/f4585cf4f25dd3808308f0cc5da508c59b6df17a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/220909633?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan","id":220909633,"login":"analisaperlengkapan","node_id":"U_kgDODSrQQQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/a5be3132fe147ce63e07425d74ead7f33a8fd102/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T08:22:37Z","email":"analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com","name":"analisaperlengkapan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T08:22:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(perlengkapan): four dashboards, three definitions of the same number (#878)\n\n* refactor(perlengkapan): four dashboards, three definitions of the same number\n\nThe dashboards were the last read in this service that still answered\nnationwide, and they did it to every caller. Measured against deployed\nstaging (rc29) as operator_a, whose satker is 0200010:\n\n  GET /bank-aset/dashboard      1 681 aset,   1 satker, Rp 204,5 M  (scoped)\n  GET /dashboard/stats        624 533 aset, 556 satker, Rp 81,9 T\n  GET /dashboard/perlengkapan total_by_satker NAMES other satkers —\n                              \"KEJAKSAAN NEGERI JAKARTA SELATAN\" (0200020),\n                              \"KEJAKSAAN NEGERI BANDUNG\" (0300010)\n  GET /kebutuhan-bmn/dashboard total_satker_terlibat: 3, national totals\n  GET .../export/{excel,pdf}   200, the same aggregates in a file\n\nThe obvious fix is to scope all three. That is what I started, and it was\nwrong: it would have added ~600 lines to defend surfaces that should not\nexist. Two of the four were duplicates.\n\n`/dashboard/stats` was a SECOND aggregate over `integrasi.siman_aset` whose\npayload is a strict SUBSET of `/bank-aset/dashboard` — same table, second\nquery, one of them scoped and one not. Deleted; the home page reads the\nscoped superset. `/kebutuhan-bmn/dashboard` had no caller in either frontend\nand no e2e, and counted campaigns a third way. Deleted.\n\nSo this lands well under the patch it replaces, and one rule now lives in\none place instead of three.\n\n`/dashboard/perlengkapan` and its two exports survive, and are scoped — with\nBOTH scopes, because neither substitutes for the other: perlengkapan''s\nworkflow rows are keyed by the MySIMKARI `kode_satker` in the caller''s JWT,\nSIMAN assets by the disjoint finance code `kdsatker_keu`. Filtering one and\nnot the other still reports the country''s assets. Both go on the repository\nSIGNATURES so an eighth aggregate that forgets to scope will not compile.\n\nTwo corrections found while consolidating, both measured on staging:\n\n  * `/bank-aset/dashboard` counted `COUNT(DISTINCT nama_satker)`. That is 554\n    where `COUNT(DISTINCT kdsatker_keu)` is 556 — two satkers sharing a name\n    folded into one. A satker''s identity is its code (#43).\n  * its condition breakdown read `COALESCE(ur_kondisi, ...)`, a fifth spelling\n    of \"an asset''s condition\" that ignores `kondisi` entirely. Harmless today\n    (`kondisi` is populated in 0 of 624 533 rows) and precisely the kind of\n    harmless that stops being harmless when the ingest is fixed. Now reads the\n    shared `ASSET_KONDISI_SQL`.\n\nCopy audit of the landing page, since the numbers on it changed meaning:\n\n  * \"Tahun Anggaran 2025\" was a hard-coded literal — wrong since 1 January,\n    and already disagreeing with the export button on the same page, which has\n    always taken the year from the clock. Derived now.\n  * \"Perlu Perbaikan\" summed every RUSAK* bucket: 76 459 on staging, of which\n    64 522 (84%) are \"Rusak Berat\" — in BMN practice a PENGHAPUSAN candidate,\n    not a repair one. The card pointed at the wrong next action for most of\n    what it counted. Split into \"Rusak Ringan / Kandidat perbaikan\" and\n    \"Rusak Berat / Kandidat penghapusan\".\n  * \"Satuan Kerja / Unit kerja aktif\" claimed an activity nothing measures,\n    and once scoped reads a constant 1 for every operator. Moved out of the\n    headline row into a \"Cakupan: N satuan kerja\" chip beside the role, where\n    it says what the page covers instead of pretending to be a metric.\n  * the heading said \"Ringkasan Sistem Manajemen\" to everyone. With scoped\n    numbers underneath that is the exact ambiguity the scoping was meant to\n    end, so it now names the tier: Satuan Kerja Anda / Wilayah Anda / Nasional.\n  * \"Portal Perlengkapan Kejaksaan\" — Portal is a DIFFERENT application here.\n  * \"Kondisi Baik / Siap pakai\" asserted availability from a condition grade;\n    \"Bank Aset / Katalog dan registrasi BMN\" implied assets are registered here\n    when the page only reads SIMAN; \"Disposal\", \"monitoring\", \"Workflow Config\",\n    \"Audit Log\" and \"RBAC\" replaced with Indonesian.\n\nTests: 6 new scope tests (three tiers each, both directions) plus the guards\n`/dashboard/stats` had earned — the NULL `kondisi`, the non-numeric `rph_aset`,\nthe distinct-satker count — rehomed onto the endpoint that survived rather than\ndeleted with the one that did not. Canary: forcing both `from_claims` to\n`Self::All` fails 5 of 6; the sixth asserts document format, not scope, and\nsays so in its body.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\n* fix(perlengkapan): two failures my own change caused, both caught by CI\n\n`useless_conversion`: `fetch_dashboard()` already returns the same error type,\nso `map_err(Into::into)` is a no-op that `-D warnings` rejects. I missed it\nlocally because I filtered clippy''s output to `^error|warning: unused` — a\nfilter narrow enough to hide the one line that mattered. The lesson is about\nthe filter, not the lint.\n\nThe e2e looked for buttons named \"Export Excel\" / \"Export PDF\"; the copy audit\nrenamed them to \"Excel\" / \"PDF\" because the section header beside them already\nreads \"Unduh rekap\" and the old labels stated the verb twice. The test was\nright to fail — a rename it did not know about is exactly what it is for — so\nthe spec moves to the new names rather than the names moving back.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"757ad30397887fe160cd3446518bf039f3d709cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/trees/757ad30397887fe160cd3446518bf039f3d709cb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/commits/a5be3132fe147ce63e07425d74ead7f33a8fd102","verification":{"payload":"tree 757ad30397887fe160cd3446518bf039f3d709cb\nparent f381b6ff6e045e9eb511452b7baa8ca6597fafed\nauthor analisaperlengkapan <analisaperlengkap