taught: the cluster and the repo\ndescribed different systems for two months because the tag was passed with\n`--set` instead of recorded here.\n\nEight of the ten changes close cross-satker data leaks that were MEASURED\nagainst the running rc29, not inferred — permit details and their decision\nletters, employee rosters and profiles, campaign responses, feasibility\nreports served as PDF to satkers with no claim to them. Two more repair\nendpoints that could never have worked: one that failed to parse its own\nquery, one that panicked on the first row it matched.\n\nNothing in this list has ever run in an image. The evidence for every one of\nthem comes from rc29, which contains none of the fixes.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"538ae9bbebc1442a32be902b05b58fa75a667e10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/trees/538ae9bbebc1442a32be902b05b58fa75a667e10"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/commits/f381b6ff6e045e9eb511452b7baa8ca6597fafed","verification":{"payload":"tree 538ae9bbebc1442a32be902b05b58fa75a667e10\nparent d384cdcd4534a7dbe78e2f088f4b7e432ab05cc1\nauthor analisaperlengkapan <analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com> 1787962036 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787962036 +0000\n\nrelease(staging): rc30 — ten changes, eight of them measured leaks (#877)\n\nBumps `global.imageTag` to `v0.1.0-rc30` so the tag and the values file land\ntogether, per the rule the rc24 drift taught: the cluster and the repo\ndescribed different systems for two months because the tag was passed with\n`--set` instead of recorded here.\n\nEight of the ten changes close cross-satker data leaks that were MEASURED\nagainst the running rc29, not inferred — permit details and their decision\nletters, employee rosters and profiles, campaign responses, feasibility\nreports served as PDF to satkers with no claim to them. Two more repair\nendpoints that could never have worked: one that failed to parse its own\nquery, one that panicked on the first row it matched.\n\nNothing in this list has ever run in an image. The evidence for every one of\nthem comes from rc29, which contains none of the fixes.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkiK0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9nAQAFV5jRItffpB15QKiYe/zhfm\nhRs0C5YNFPAng2u42ztr69k7tPai4Il4pUMgqzrD28LiWTUDgwrS5wum3wmnb+4Z\ngYM7TBGj0373JYm83kIsU6qfs1R2K3k6baR8SKXf3rKpU1D2nLLYKw+OgdFsknfw\nyi6fuxMGo27rwXZDA8iwdDMurSRDdHb9BEpcKhess12mwN9KrLHEkiUOci71asjW\n3oixf8KepZ1R7NY3UuttNKC03SNY/svEQZwPc3ZrOHXU67ujDF+UqcXTQURO5tqU\nadM1q43gi1LO2WsvENDZBygXeXlJudTpIQqhsxA/WM4xIAJPzQxuzobAgnUSxqeA\n7hZc+IVDCHnxLYEVzwM8G2h1kNR+sM8WXR6N1YkbxNZkTUvJZmp2mDI4lQUb1zZZ\nH+6YrIQi6jYpizJMzTEQ+LaDMfvvgD9OJXa/U5Ru21ybdYJ6aSVR66/0Dj10CiDd\nQ4xH5JQJbfmYsl+hqKBaBhdEvpjjPRKvft6HvtjAfCITkSuYWbxdmEb2JIfBd7HY\n4K5YMm63SFKqd1RgJFiAlXygQP3TfjCqVwuA9zxpnVOzUodjH9u+Xw0/l8JnTfcj\nkm3lPT7YDOkvS9FxeCvQzf4/9CioqD0petqlhH+sMQV5j08cqf4jvLtj8YP/P/EW\nJkBx78CURDCn0/dx7cle\n=HT9w\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-29T00:07:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/f381b6ff6e045e9eb511452b7baa8ca6597fafed","node_id":"C_kwDOP93DxNoAKGYzODFiNmZmNmUwNDVlOWViNTExNDUyYjdiYWE4Y2E2NTk3ZmFmZWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/d384cdcd4534a7dbe78e2f088f4b7e432ab05cc1","sha":"d384cdcd4534a7dbe78e2f088f4b7e432ab05cc1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/d384cdcd4534a7dbe78e2f088f4b7e432ab05cc1"}],"sha":"f381b6ff6e045e9eb511452b7baa8ca6597fafed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/f381b6ff6e045e9eb511452b7baa8ca6597fafed"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/220909633?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan","id":220909633,"login":"analisaperlengkapan","node_id":"U_kgDODSrQQQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/d384cdcd4534a7dbe78e2f088f4b7e432ab05cc1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T20:35:57Z","email":"analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com","name":"analisaperlengkapan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T20:35:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(perlengkapan): the feasibility analysis never once looked at SIMAN (#876)\n\n`get_analisis_kelayakan` exists to answer one question: how much of what a\nsatker asked for does it already hold. It never asked. The comparison hung\noff an `Option<SimanIntegration>` that no code path in the application ever\nfilled — `with_siman` and `set_siman` had zero callers outside their own\ndefinitions — so every request fell through to the stored `existing_count`\ncolumn and an empty asset list, while the screen reported a SIMAN\ncomparison had been made. Two endpoints built on the same client answered\n500 to everyone, which is how it surfaced.\n\nWiring that client would not have fixed it. It talks to a remote SIMAN JSON\nAPI through `MonsaktiClient` — the Monsakti path is documented dormant — and\nits own comment concedes the shape problem: \"SIMAN API uses BA_KEY from\nconfig, not per-satker query\". A per-satker summary would have returned the\nsame aggregate for every satker, with `value: 0.0` and an empty\n`by_condition` beside it. So it is deleted, along with the two endpoints and\nthe constructors nothing called.\n\nThe analysis reads `integrasi.siman_aset` instead — the live source of\ntruth `bank_aset` and `penghapusan_bmn` already read, and where both traps\nare already solved in one place:\n\n  - the barang code. SIMAN stores undotted digits; the rest of the system\n    carries the dotted presentation form. Comparing them raw is an equality\n    that never holds, and it fails as an EMPTY RESULT rather than an error.\n    Both halves go through the shared normaliser.\n  - the satker. SIMAN keys assets by `kdsatker_keu`, which is a different\n    coding scheme from MySIMKARI `kode_satker`; the integrasi-owned\n    `v_satker_code_map` is what bridges them, and matching on `nama_satker`\n    is the string-equality trap that map exists to replace.\n\nMatching is by satker + barang code. That is not a preference: an asset''s\nidentity is kode satker + kode barang + NUP, and NUP is the sequence number\nWITHIN a code at a satker, so \"the same kind of asset this satker already\nhas\" is exactly satker + code.\n\nThe tests then found a second defect, one that could not show while the\ncomparison was dead. `BarangWithExistingInventory` flattens the barang row,\nso `existing_count` on the wire is the row''s STORED column — not the number\nthe `gap` beside it was computed from. With both at zero they agreed by\naccident. With a live count the payload contradicted itself: `existing_count\n0`, `gap 3`, and two matching assets listed underneath. The computed value\nis carried onto the serialised row now.\n\nWorth stating plainly: THE NUMBERS ON THE ANALYSIS SCREEN WILL CHANGE.\nThey will be computed for the first time. A satker that holds matching\nassets will see a smaller gap than it did yesterday, and the recommendation\nderived from that gap changes with it.\n\nFour tests, each pinning a failure whose symptom is an empty answer rather\nthan an error: the count and the listed assets for a satker that holds two;\nthe same code at a satker that holds none, so the mapping is doing work\nrather than merely finding nothing; the dotted and undotted spellings\nreaching the same assets; and a barang with no code matching nothing rather\nthan everything the satker owns.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b921684bcbd3e27d80ad2530f7197f6a69aaf456","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/trees/b921684bcbd3e27d80ad2530f7197f6a69aaf456"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/commits/d384cdcd4534a7dbe78e2f088f4b7e432ab05cc1","verification":{"payload":"tree b921684bcbd3e27d80ad2530f7197f6a69aaf456\nparent 0758f698b7af63309186d4c2e812dc102696f095\nauthor analisaperlengkapan <analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com> 1787949357 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787949357 +0000\n\nfix(perlengkapan): the feasibility analysis never once looked at SIMAN (#876)\n\n`get_analisis_kelayakan` exists to answer one question: how much of what a\nsatker asked for does it already hold. It never asked. The comparison hung\noff an `Option<SimanIntegration>` that no code path in the application ever\nfilled — `with_siman` and `set_siman` had zero callers outside their own\ndefinitions — so every request fell through to the stored `existing_count`\ncolumn and an empty asset list, while the screen reported a SIMAN\ncomparison had been made. Two endpoints built on the same client answered\n500 to everyone, which is how it surfaced.\n\nWiring that client would not have fixed it. It talks to a remote SIMAN JSON\nAPI through `MonsaktiClient` — the Monsakti path is documented dormant — and\nits own comment concedes the shape problem: \"SIMAN API uses BA_KEY from\nconfig, not per-satker query\". A per-satker summary would have returned the\nsame aggregate for every satker, with `value: 0.0` and an empty\n`by_condition` beside it. So it is deleted, along with the two endpoints and\nthe constructors nothing called.\n\nThe analysis reads `integrasi.siman_aset` instead — the live source of\ntruth `bank_aset` and `penghapusan_bmn` already read, and where both traps\nare already solved in one place:\n\n  - the barang code. SIMAN stores undotted digits; the rest of the system\n    carries the dotted presentation form. Comparing them raw is an equality\n    that never holds, and it fails as an EMPTY RESULT rather than an error.\n    Both halves go through the shared normaliser.\n  - the satker. SIMAN keys assets by `kdsatker_keu`, which is a different\n    coding scheme from MySIMKARI `kode_satker`; the integrasi-owned\n    `v_satker_code_map` is what bridges them, and matching on `nama_satker`\n    is the string-equality trap that map exists to replace.\n\nMatching is by satker + barang code. That is not a preference: an asset''s\nidentity is kode satker + kode barang + NUP, and NUP is the sequence number\nWITHIN a code at a satker, so \"the same kind of asset this satker already\nhas\" is exactly satker + code.\n\nThe tests then found a second defect, one that could not show while the\ncomparison was dead. `BarangWithExistingInventory` flattens the barang row,\nso `existing_count` on the wire is the row''s STORED column — not the number\nthe `gap` beside it was computed from. With both at zero they agreed by\naccident. With a live count the payload contradicted itself: `existing_count\n0`, `gap 3`, and two matching assets listed underneath. The computed value\nis carried onto the serialised row now.\n\nWorth stating plainly: THE NUMBERS ON THE ANALYSIS SCREEN WILL CHANGE.\nThey will be computed for the first time. A satker that holds matching\nassets will see a smaller gap than it did yesterday, and the recommendation\nderived from that gap changes with it.\n\nFour tests, each pinning a failure whose symptom is an empty answer rather\nthan an error: the count and the listed assets for a satker that holds two;\nthe same code at a satker that holds none, so the mapping is doing work\nrather than merely finding nothing; the dotted and undotted spellings\nreaching the same assets; and a barang with no code matching nothing rather\nthan everything the satker owns.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkfEtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkLkQAK5iq7Nokuo4fTz6/0psfxyG\n2KWq0ARBoyjp3mWKkTTOj4gb87Vt+8YTDJv8PWfggzpLAmIS/pjSwS73rTZUCGkW\nMvrNmnYbgv5x/ugqvh706h0+8EI93e8ngsMUhNUzYhzvZwC7HGktLAKHOmACAhx4\nEhPgPF0doeCe4unejDIdmOlOe3QmsfVLE8/umH9TwwKrgKdDeZbDE+OidtuBMmw1\nTTu6b9QklhPt3vwsLkFp5kgHQSlErq+XF802myi0wgPhHc6RIdrYXwk+Jn2Is5HV\nwe2xa6JQEGrfYMlvPyMTmoNsiMJZUf1ls4TTtPYrmXG4a2xCeIb3LPhKVKYkWz5h\nUY1QTyfeNm7b93GwLmOaH1kfB6HjQZhjtzuRD1/sCO6rAoSOC8o3DS1n0CMLM5Y/\nMr3XhZheH95D0djwQRpr3il0TvhAu6y5UWlEFyak2sD+wJBkcx7e8iW6Jmi5zANK\nqYgHnubrhT0Y59H8Oac69LG2s+IcAXs7Y6Hzgtq99Y2KDbGM6m6bjkhahSK0EzRU\nxxCRnfyjs6XD+aMUJ33oYINL1o6ZdHZC97DE7p7Ne+nWeccApN2ATtO7Q4Jwq65L\ne7MSoAkxrpkoVsT0AUdy8YLxMwLTYkNGa0DhyAQgO2CaphzvIMKaJRUL8rA85YBE\nDHytFcYUI77Vz1ibgrWr\n=3vB+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-28T20:35:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/d384cdcd4534a7dbe78e2f088f4b7e432ab05cc1","node_id":"C_kwDOP93DxNoAKGQzODRjZGNkNDUzNGE3ZGJlNzhlMmYwODhmNGI3ZTQzMmFiMDVjYzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/0758f698b7af63309186d4c2e812dc102696f095","sha":"0758f698b7af63309186d4c2e812dc102696f095","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/0758f698b7af63309186d4c2e812dc102696f095"}],"sha":"d384cdcd4534a7dbe78e2f088f4b7e432ab05cc1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/d384cdcd4534a7dbe78e2f088f4b7e432ab05cc1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/220909633?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan","id":220909633,"login":"analisaperlengkapan","node_id":"U_kgDODSrQQQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/0758f698b7af63309186d4c2e812dc102696f095/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T20:14:59Z","email":"analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com","name":"analisaperlengkapan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T20:14:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(perlengkapan): the permit list was scoped, the permit behind it was not (#875)\n\nPemakaian BMN monitoring has been tiered since #66 — pusat sees everything,\nwilayah its region, satker its own — and `pemakaian_monitoring_scope_test`\npins that. The LIST. The detail behind it was never scoped, and neither\nwere the eleven other places that reach a permit by id.\n\nMeasured against deployed staging (rc29), operator_a (0200010) against\noperator_b''s permit (0200020):\n\n    GET /pemakaian-bmn/{foreign}             -> 200, the whole record\n    GET /pemakaian-bmn/{foreign}/sk-izin.pdf -> 200, application/pdf,\n                                                5 057 bytes\n\nA permit is a named person holding a named asset for a stated period —\nwhich is the thing the stakeholder asked to be limited per role, in those\nwords. So the boundary was right on the screen people look at, and open to\nanyone who kept or guessed a single UUID.\n\n`get_permit_by_id` DID read the caller''s claims — to trim\n`allowed_transitions` so the API would not advertise a button that answers\n403. The record itself came back in full. A handler that uses `claims` is\nnot thereby a handler that authorizes, which is why the unused-`_claims`\ncensus could not see this one; the same blind spot hid `create_barang` and\n`delete_barang` in #872.\n\n`scope` goes in `get_by_id`''s signature, predicate inside the SELECT, and\nthe compiler then listed all twelve call sites. Three deliberately pass\n`All`, each with the reason written down — the reload after create reads\nthe row this call just wrote; the update''s status pre-check was already\nscoped by the service that reached it; and auto-activation after approval\nmust not skip a permit because the approver happens to sit elsewhere.\n\nSix integration cases and three e2e. One of them was a false pass: the\nworkflow-action test used `validator_satker`, which the policy refuses for\nRevoke regardless of satker, so it passed on the ROLE gate and stayed green\nwith the scope disabled. The canary caught it. It uses `approver_satker`\nnow — the only role the policy admits — and asserts 404 rather than\n\"not 200\", so the object gate is what it measures. Verified in both\nstates: before, three of six failed with the scope off; after, four of six,\nwith the two positive controls green as they should be.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6092f23c372e6eea5aac8d6980a312fbf2918330","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/trees/6092f23c372e6eea5aac8d6980a312fbf2918330"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/commits/0758f698b7af63309186d4c2e812dc102696f095","verification":{"payload":"tree 6092f23c372e6eea5aac8d6980a312fbf2918330\nparent 876d17b6b9ec922c261e1b19adc9d7699ff309ee\nauthor analisaperlengkapan <analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com> 1787948099 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787948099 +0000\n\nfix(perlengkapan): the permit list was scoped, the permit behind it was not (#875)\n\nPemakaian BMN monitoring has been tiered since #66 — pusat sees everything,\nwilayah its region, satker its own — and `pemakaian_monitoring_scope_test`\npins that. The LIST. The detail behind it was never scoped, and neither\nwere the eleven other places that reach a permit by id.\n\nMeasured against deployed staging (rc29), operator_a (0200010) against\noperator_b''s permit (0200020):\n\n    GET /pemakaian-bmn/{foreign}             -> 200, the whole record\n    GET /pemakaian-bmn/{foreign}/sk-izin.pdf -> 200, application/pdf,\n                                                5 057 bytes\n\nA permit is a named person holding a named asset for a stated period —\nwhich is the thing the stakeholder asked to be limited per role, in those\nwords. So the boundary was right on the screen people look at, and open to\nanyone who kept or guessed a single UUID.\n\n`get_permit_by_id` DID read the caller''s claims — to trim\n`allowed_transitions` so the API would not advertise a button that answers\n403. The record itself came back in full. A handler that uses `claims` is\nnot thereby a handler that authorizes, which is why the unused-`_claims`\ncensus could not see this one; the same blind spot hid `create_barang` and\n`delete_barang` in #872.\n\n`scope` goes in `get_by_id`''s signature, predicate inside the SELECT, and\nthe compiler then listed all twelve call sites. Three deliberately pass\n`All`, each with the reason written down — the reload after create reads\nthe row this call just wrote; the update''s status pre-check was already\nscoped by the service that reached it; and auto-activation after approval\nmust not skip a permit because the approver happens to sit elsewhere.\n\nSix integration cases and three e2e. One of them was a false pass: the\nworkflow-action test used `validator_satker`, which the policy refuses for\nRevoke regardless of satker, so it passed on the ROLE gate and stayed green\nwith the scope disabled. The canary caught it. It uses `approver_satker`\nnow — the only role the policy admits — and asserts 404 rather than\n\"not 200\", so the object gate is what it measures. Verified in both\nstates: before, three of six failed with the scope off; after, four of six,\nwith the two positive controls green as they should be.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkexDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASDAQAKX75mEZ1ZKrW+uB9Fce+yF2\n9u541nPrr6OD5UdRjAzAcjx1Rwe3QPJuUh2SLzGn8JFtRYYyKfm6x1AGz+VgC2o/\nMB4rdj4JIFUxIRG4VsLI9zDX8s8BXnZ+OefwESpDKfyrNnKs5exf6/M8HqB95rfA\n3U4JECgbbuIoONQhTuDpYZJ2P0Xy08ks0rVyNUKwHRdhOcg/3zeqn4oP1dhcZIBt\n5D3mFScGCfK56aDCKUDWzDGL15o3MjCnrgPAy+Bd91c6/K9c/oHKHv5s8zmLwV1W\ndh0g10Ul1E7BAnoaFyhiridW+MjZQMZiH/jkxCw9DkxbnfpfOGkAbuulVudlzL+R\nqTMbG7tXXOKUOWCksZTFolEGI0VtgXNcrWEFQ0fekZF6C4Dd/UYDP8qwwewoZFdD\nI8q0Jz/kKnjHKAoqccVqVtJrcJS8uVdKxsHGSArY2n63d2BOEiz3IsBBMVwk77PW\nKX53r4s61dRC96JSn7DRUkVcm6diAgeUFMWWGuF08CWp4HdkUEcn6nwdepPF0q6B\nD5225gRlzHci1rjfpQ2115p+0u3+wNsWye87wXZDRT3yldgmdK+dyE32OguZGIxt\nyF3g8RqMqszz3EgGYciMz8PCyj6YZd/GmCUjftD2KYz2nwALucBQvVeDPkDpbsCv\niPoJDzFeEhSrWA0kDw9A\n=GWsg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-28T20:14:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/0758f698b7af63309186d4c2e812dc102696f095","node_id":"C_kwDOP93DxNoAKDA3NThmNjk4YjdhZjYzMzA5MTg2ZDRjMmU4MTJkYzEwMjY5NmYwOTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/876d17b6b9ec922c261e1b19adc9d7699ff309ee","sha":"876d17b6b9ec922c261e1b19adc9d7699ff309ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/876d17b6b9ec922c261e1b19adc9d7699ff309ee"}],"sha":"0758f698b7af63309186d4c2e812dc102696f095","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/0758f698b7af63309186d4c2e812dc102696f095"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/220909633?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan","id":220909633,"login":"analisaperlengkapan","node_id":"U_kgDODSrQQQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/876d17b6b9ec922c261e1b19adc9d7699ff309ee/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T19:21:10Z","email":"analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com","name":"analisaperlengkapan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T19:21:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(perlengkapan): the kebutuhan search failed on every path that returned a row (#874)\n\n* fix(perlengkapan): the kebutuhan search failed on every path that returned a row\n\n`/kebutuhan-bmn/search` has never returned a row. A probe against staging\nanswers 200, but only because the search happens to match nothing — which\nis exactly the state in which this endpoint looks healthy. The moment a row\nmatched, it panicked.\n\nSix faults, each sufficient on its own:\n\n1. `SELECT k.*` from `pengajuan_kebutuhan_bmn`, handed to a mapper that\n   reads `vw_kebutuhan_bmn_summary`. The first matching row panicked on\n   `invalid column status_nama`, and with `panic = \"abort\"` in the release\n   profile that ends the process, not the request. Rows now come from the\n   view, joined to the base table for the columns the full-text expression\n   needs.\n2. `k.satker_id` — a campaign has no satker column; the satkers hang off it.\n   The filter was typed `Uuid` besides, against a key that has been\n   MySIMKARI `kode_satker` (TEXT) since V006/#94. It reaches the\n   participation rows now, as a String.\n3. `k.kode_barang` — lives two levels down, on the barang rows.\n4. `k.is_sbsk` — no such column anywhere in the schema. Removed from the\n   query, from `SearchFilters`, and from the HTTP params rather than left as\n   a filter that cannot be honoured. No frontend sends it.\n5. `k.status_kode = ANY($n)` with a `Vec<String>` — integer against text[],\n   a bind-time failure. It now matches the name the view resolves OR the\n   code written as text, so both `?status=DRAFT` and `?status=2000` work.\n6. `created_at >= $n` with a String. `$n::timestamptz` is NOT enough — that\n   was my first attempt and it still 500''d: Postgres resolves an otherwise\n   unconstrained parameter to the cast''s TARGET type, so the placeholder\n   stays timestamptz while the client sends text. `$n::text::timestamptz`\n   pins it.\n\n`SortOptions::to_sql` is shared across surfaces and names `priority_score`,\n`gap` and `tahun_anggaran` — none of which exist on a campaign row. Three of\nsix sort options were a \"column does not exist\" waiting for a caller to pick\nthat sort. Ordering is a parsed enum, not user text, so the exposure was a\n500 rather than an injection; each surface now says which columns it has.\n\nThe count query was built by splitting the data query''s text on the word\nLIMIT. It is built from the same FROM/WHERE now.\n\nTen tests, one per fault rather than one per endpoint, and every one of them\ninsists the search MATCHES something — an empty result is what made this\nendpoint look fine for as long as it did. The sort case walks all nine\nspellings a caller can send in both directions, 18 combinations, each of\nwhich must answer AND still match.\n\nNothing caught any of this because nothing ever called the endpoint: the\nroute-coverage gate walks frontend routes, and a backend endpoint with no\ncaller has no route to walk.\n\nStill open, and named rather than fixed: `search_kebutuhan_barang` in the\nsame file has zero callers.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\n* style: trailing blank line left by dropping the is_sbsk filter\n\n`cargo fmt -p layanan-perlengkapan` does not reach lib-perlengkapan, so the\ngap the removed field left behind survived local formatting and only the\nworkspace-wide check saw it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"55819c1800dfc732a4e6e7848f761a50405fc001","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/trees/55819c1800dfc732a4e6e7848f761a50405fc001"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/commits/876d17b6b9ec922c261e1b19adc9d7699ff309ee","verification":{"payload":"tree 55819c1800dfc732a4e6e7848f761a50405fc001\nparent 96b8cb1699bc739e4eca5ff027bf954e362e3799\nauthor analisaperlengkapan <analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com> 1787944870 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787944870 +0000\n\nfix(perlengkapan): the kebutuhan search failed on every path that returned a row (#874)\n\n* fix(perlengkapan): the kebutuhan search failed on every path that returned a row\n\n`/kebutuhan-bmn/search` has never returned a row. A probe against staging\nanswers 200, but only because the search happens to match nothing — which\nis exactly the state in which this endpoint looks healthy. The moment a row\nmatched, it panicked.\n\nSix faults, each sufficient on its own:\n\n1. `SELECT k.*` from `pengajuan_kebutuhan_bmn`, handed to a mapper that\n   reads `vw_kebutuhan_bmn_summary`. The first matching row panicked on\n   `invalid column status_nama`, and with `panic = \"abort\"` in the release\n   profile that ends the process, not the request. Rows now come from the\n   view, joined to the base table for the columns the full-text expression\n   needs.\n2. `k.satker_id` — a campaign has no satker column; the satkers hang off it.\n   The filter was typed `Uuid` besides, against a key that has been\n   MySIMKARI `kode_satker` (TEXT) since V006/#94. It reaches the\n   participation rows now, as a String.\n3. `k.kode_barang` — lives two levels down, on the barang rows.\n4. `k.is_sbsk` — no such column anywhere in the schema. Removed from the\n   query, from `SearchFilters`, and from the HTTP params rather than left as\n   a filter that cannot be honoured. No frontend sends it.\n5. `k.status_kode = ANY($n)` with a `Vec<String>` — integer against text[],\n   a bind-time failure. It now matches the name the view resolves OR the\n   code written as text, so both `?status=DRAFT` and `?status=2000` work.\n6. `created_at >= $n` with a String. `$n::timestamptz` is NOT enough — that\n   was my first attempt and it still 500''d: Postgres resolves an otherwise\n   unconstrained parameter to the cast''s TARGET type, so the placeholder\n   stays timestamptz while the client sends text. `$n::text::timestamptz`\n   pins it.\n\n`SortOptions::to_sql` is shared across surfaces and names `priority_score`,\n`gap` and `tahun_anggaran` — none of which exist on a campaign row. Three of\nsix sort options were a \"column does not exist\" waiting for a caller to pick\nthat sort. Ordering is a parsed enum, not user text, so the exposure was a\n500 rather than an injection; each surface now says which columns it has.\n\nThe count query was built by splitting the data query''s text on the word\nLIMIT. It is built from the same FROM/WHERE now.\n\nTen tests, one per fault rather than one per endpoint, and every one of them\ninsists the search MATCHES something — an empty result is what made this\nendpoint look fine for as long as it did. The sort case walks all nine\nspellings a caller can send in both directions, 18 combinations, each of\nwhich must answer AND still match.\n\nNothing caught any of this because nothing ever called the endpoint: the\nroute-coverage gate walks frontend routes, and a backend endpoint with no\ncaller has no route to walk.\n\nStill open, and named rather than fixed: `search_kebutuhan_barang` in the\nsame file has zero callers.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\n* style: trailing blank line left by dropping the is_sbsk filter\n\n`cargo fmt -p layanan-perlengkapan` does not reach lib-perlengkapan, so the\ngap the removed field left behind survived local formatting and only the\nworkspace-wide check saw it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkd+mCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMagQAEsGHddFTfbw1pwu5hovTcpi\nEAcDT+XAc9I0lqCUj7vUgbeQWg4BGMfb163s9Bqy694MPdalQmaupjJof7ouAd4W\nBU2Zgc2M7vaCg4OKhK2F6LfR2r80ubClccKtjN4panQnSHSopWPP5i8/BDZcNC/W\n6x4se5YXUJRRalfIYUg2giGIScW5eKIkI5ONOZ7XuzZlV/0shFlHpnXKIiZRVdQp\npR1okHgvmNl5Vfp6wqlEiDpaplna34HQG8j/UfprPt+iUAM31uKd3I0mjMXnmIra\ngUi5zcMqwj6yE0N7vl7cb/afq5OMHSEqZNSY5OW2Ch0tb1UWXWIXLCUPkc+i+gIS\nITOOjMRADKe1yTTBnnkjnsX0is9mSDXqTLF3AqJJPklR3Rqk/iR28JoD3qcqHwAj\nN449SmFGP7VSmkn1N9QIx4Z+8VGZdtZtMMz/dM9zGdaGTaAO1p+0xEeVxnBY0zh+\neTgc3Yc+aQ38Zbhzz8g/8L5dcUuFkHAnXxQfRuxbIBmVFW3jbMvvaG2e2uvD4/9x\nCsjjPYPhlTTvSbKx+y/1MCRJq33e2StgWZDVIAs2gwzam2H6OyAnisRtn5+qtw+l\nG/K/zKZFI086+oLbNMuY3XpnRSePh+of3Kd03lFRZnQKd2NlMYVX7U6tSu9hbxwZ\n2xCqeGLBF6z1xMUdoPMa\n=9Hrl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-28T19:21:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/876d17b6b9ec922c261e1b19adc9d7699ff309ee","node_id":"C_kwDOP93DxNoAKDg3NmQxN2I2YjllYzkyMmMyNjFlMWIxOWFkYzlkNzY5OWZmMzA5ZWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/96b8cb1699bc739e4eca5ff027bf954e362e3799","sha":"96b8cb1699bc739e4eca5ff027bf954e362e3799","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/96b8cb1699bc739e4eca5ff027bf954e362e3799"}],"sha":"876d17b6b9ec922c261e1b19adc9d7699ff309ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/876d17b6b9ec922c261e1b19adc9d7699ff309ee"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/220909633?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan","id":220909633,"login":"analisaperlengkapan","node_id":"U_kgDODSrQQQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/96b8cb1699bc739e4eca5ff027bf954e362e3799/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T17:59:31Z","email":"analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com","name":"analisaperlengkapan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T17:59:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(perlengkapan): five siblings of the endpoint #93 closed stayed open (#872)\n\n* fix(perlengkapan): #93 scoped one endpoint and left its five siblings open\n\n#93 closed the cross-satker read on `get_satker_detail`. Every sibling on\nthe very same `satker/{id}` path kept fetching the row unscoped, because\nthe rule lived at one call site instead of in the type system.\n\nMeasured against deployed staging (rc29), operator_a (0200010) against\nanother satker''s participation row:\n\n    GET /kebutuhan-bmn/satker/{foreign}            -> 404   (#93, working)\n    GET /kebutuhan-bmn/satker/{foreign}/aktivitas  -> 200\n    GET /kebutuhan-bmn/satker/{foreign}/analisis   -> 200\n    GET .../laporan/preview  and  .../download     -> 200, application/pdf,\n                                                     4 973 bytes\n    GET /kebutuhan-bmn/pengajuan/{id}/satker       -> 200, all three\n                                                     participants, one of\n                                                     them in another wilayah\n\nThe trail carries each validator''s user id and NIP; the analysis is the\nwhole of another satker''s case — what they asked for, what SIMAN says they\nhold, and the gap; the report endpoints render exactly that into a PDF an\noperator could download.\n\nThe fix is `scope` in `get_satker_by_id`''s SIGNATURE, with the predicate\ninside the SELECT. That is what makes the coverage mechanical rather than\nremembered: the compiler then listed all nine call sites, including four\nworkflow actions that write. Those stamp a validator identity onto the row,\nso each now reads it scoped BEFORE the write — `require_role` above them\nanswers \"may a validator_wilayah ever do this\", never \"may THIS one, to\nTHIS satker\".\n\nTwo more that the census by unused-`_claims` could not see, because their\nhandlers do use claims — for a user id: `create_barang` reaches a satker by\nits id, and `delete_barang` reaches one through the barang''s own id, so the\nowning satker was never consulted. Both go through the same scoped fetch\nnow. The status checks beside them are workflow guards; a row in the right\nstate still belongs to whoever owns it.\n\nTwo call sites deliberately pass `All`, both with the reason written down:\nthe campaign-level transition fans out over its own children (a narrower\nscope would advance some participants and silently leave the rest behind —\na partial transition is worse than a refused one), and the create path\nbuilds a detail for a campaign that has no participants yet.\n\n`get_pengajuan_satkers` is scoped per tier: pusat sees three, the operator\nsees one, KJT01''s validator sees the two satkers in its region and not the\none under KJT02.\n\nThe kebutuhan workflow fixture carried the same `WIL001` that the\npenghapusan one did — not a satker code, naming nothing in the fixture and\nnothing in MySIMKARI, harmless until a by-id handler read the claim. It is\nKJT01 now, the Kejati the fixture actually puts above SKR001 and SKR002.\n\nTests: 6 integration cases against a real Postgres and 3 e2e against the\nreal stack. One of them was a false pass first time round — the trail\nassertion held because NO activity rows existed, so \"scoped out\" and\n\"nothing happened yet\" were the same empty list. The seed now writes one\nrow per participant and the positive half asserts it is non-empty, which is\nwhat makes the negative half mean anything. Verified by canary in both\nstates: before that fix five of six failed with the scope disabled; after\nit, six of six.\n\nCensus: 45 -> 39. What remains in kebutuhan_bmn is a different shape —\nsearch, dashboard aggregates, SIMAN lookups and campaign-level reference\nlists — which is list-scoping, not object-scoping, and wants its own change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\n* test(e2e): the kebutuhan seed had participation rows with no history\n\nA participation row sitting at SubmitWilayah or SubmitPusat with an EMPTY\napproval trail is not a state the workflow can produce — something moved it\nthere. The seed created the rows and none of the history.\n\nThat emptiness was not harmless. The RBAC assertion added alongside this\nwork says another satker''s trail comes back empty; against a seed with no\ntrail at all, it passes while proving nothing, because \"scoped out\" and\n\"nothing has happened yet\" are the same empty list. Staging did not show\nthis — it has accumulated real trails from previous runs — so the\ndifference only appeared on a fresh CI database.\n\nThe suite already refuses to draw the conclusion unless the OWNING satker\nsees a non-empty trail, and that guard is what failed here rather than the\nscope: it did its job, and the fixture is what was wrong. One row per\nsatker now, each matching the status its row sits at.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"292254900409282f2010367c40e5dab69431bb50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/trees/292254900409282f2010367c40e5dab69431bb50"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/commits/96b8cb1699bc739e4eca5ff027bf954e362e3799","verification":{"payload":"tree 292254900409282f2010367c40e5dab69431bb50\nparent bd88742d6c968624acc3fae0d41a365b26ac4e2d\nauthor analisaperlengkapan <analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com> 1787939971 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787939971 +0000\n\nfix(perlengkapan): five siblings of the endpoint #93 closed stayed open (#872)\n\n* fix(perlengkapan): #93 scoped one endpoint and left its five siblings open\n\n#93 closed the cross-satker read on `get_satker_detail`. Every sibling on\nthe very same `satker/{id}` path kept fetching the row unscoped, because\nthe rule lived at one call site instead of in the type system.\n\nMeasured against deployed staging (rc29), operator_a (0200010) against\nanother satker''s participation row:\n\n    GET /kebutuhan-bmn/satker/{foreign}            -> 404   (#93, working)\n    GET /kebutuhan-bmn/satker/{foreign}/aktivitas  -> 200\n    GET /kebutuhan-bmn/satker/{foreign}/analisis   -> 200\n    GET .../laporan/preview  and  .../download     -> 200, application/pdf,\n                                                     4 973 bytes\n    GET /kebutuhan-bmn/pengajuan/{id}/satker       -> 200, all three\n                                                     participants, one of\n                                                     them in another wilayah\n\nThe trail carries each validator''s user id and NIP; the analysis is the\nwhole of another satker''s case — what they asked for, what SIMAN says they\nhold, and the gap; the report endpoints render exactly that into a PDF an\noperator could download.\n\nThe fix is `scope` in `get_satker_by_id`''s SIGNATURE, with the predicate\ninside the SELECT. That is what makes the coverage mechanical rather than\nremembered: the compiler then listed all nine call sites, including four\nworkflow actions that write. Those stamp a validator identity onto the row,\nso each now reads it scoped BEFORE the write — `require_role` above them\nanswers \"may a validator_wilayah ever do this\", never \"may THIS one, to\nTHIS satker\".\n\nTwo more that the census by unused-`_claims` could not see, because their\nhandlers do use claims — for a user id: `create_barang` reaches a satker by\nits id, and `delete_barang` reaches one through the barang''s own id, so the\nowning satker was never consulted. Both go through the same scoped fetch\nnow. The status checks beside them are workflow guards; a row in the right\nstate still belongs to whoever owns it.\n\nTwo call sites deliberately pass `All`, both with the reason written down:\nthe campaign-level transition fans out over its own children (a narrower\nscope would advance some participants and silently leave the rest behind —\na partial transition is worse than a refused one), and the create path\nbuilds a detail for a campaign that has no participants yet.\n\n`get_pengajuan_satkers` is scoped per tier: pusat sees three, the operator\nsees one, KJT01''s validator sees the two satkers in its region and not the\none under KJT02.\n\nThe kebutuhan workflow fixture carried the same `WIL001` that the\npenghapusan one did — not a satker code, naming nothing in the fixture and\nnothing in MySIMKARI, harmless until a by-id handler read the claim. It is\nKJT01 now, the Kejati the fixture actually puts above SKR001 and SKR002.\n\nTests: 6 integration cases against a real Postgres and 3 e2e against the\nreal stack. One of them was a false pass first time round — the trail\nassertion held because NO activity rows existed, so \"scoped out\" and\n\"nothing happened yet\" were the same empty list. The seed now writes one\nrow per participant and the positive half asserts it is non-empty, which is\nwhat makes the negative half mean anything. Verified by canary in both\nstates: before that fix five of six failed with the scope disabled; after\nit, six of six.\n\nCensus: 45 -> 39. What remains in kebutuhan_bmn is a different shape —\nsearch, dashboard aggregates, SIMAN lookups and campaign-level reference\nlists — which is list-scoping, not object-scoping, and wants its own change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\n* test(e2e): the kebutuhan seed had participation rows with no history\n\nA participation row sitting at SubmitWilayah or SubmitPusat with an EMPTY\napproval trail is not a state the workflow can produce — something moved it\nthere. The seed created the rows and none of the history.\n\nThat emptiness was not harmless. The RBAC assertion added alongside this\nwork says another satker''s trail comes back empty; against a seed with no\ntrail at all, it passes while proving nothing, because \"scoped out\" and\n\"nothing has happened yet\" are the same empty list. Staging did not show\nthis — it has accumulated real trails from previous runs — so the\ndifference only appeared on a fresh CI database.\n\nThe suite already refuses to draw the conclusion unless the OWNING satker\nsees a non-empty trail, and that guard is what failed here rather than the\nscope: it did its job, and the fixture is what was wrong. One row per\nsatker now, each matching the status its row sits at.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkcyDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwzcQAJUIOO+CPXb/m/FqtdjJFRNl\negjdcVL7pyASu3mHXfkMpiBE0g8D4DK5JN0n3lDBGRJn6gynCS9Siybfnm+/WiyK\nx0Sc+c4EBZ47MiJK78oCFEVhIhxfEyKSBKExIYkI0oYO5O9OFjaXmJIi5j3DQ2Ez\n4mA9RU3dxAJ0RqfzSX8B9wQXJ7q+E2+NT95P8ue54JdXVP9DqZmi/4dQ2PQQyLFV\npseZzWhw9SxGTisEKLNSob41ZKmFcIWytjn34Ter8Uy7UeMW81iH/YE6Ux5pv6/m\ntpVovwREHav/ohPjO3s3c7WLorBVdxLh4RGRN/bxqgEH6ITrxPNFkcob0BDrdu9U\nfLdYOs+bL+lUvVm9E3AZLOGHqF6q9YDtOZYa0XNrAm9eYm9/ErBmvSsXlIsuv7PA\nDbDFohmyQ56Xb9r43UHQAhTlwoMO7VzBO5sE41G6LtrzF7rptQ6K1iwwb9UuYf8T\n6EHcCuIeuem3+fAZQZldYP+ztT86372Pws5bJXP/iIP77Mk3EuCUxNkAnZ/poHKC\nIoDo9YbDn+GfrCpceVOaFGp2cERNK5IsyUGPVm4JVqvknq35EKPQFYXeV5k+tAkr\nsotxArSOrE3vBBnLtnjX0VACrYERgRwxULCWc7UkeK83SCKRgJIRXnNsxv0yCrH2\nMeiGW//v4apAAo0qBcIM\n=MmpC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-28T17:59:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/96b8cb1699bc739e4eca5ff027bf954e362e3799","node_id":"C_kwDOP93DxNoAKDk2YjhjYjE2OTliYzczOWU0ZWNhNWZmMDI3YmY5NTRlMzYyZTM3OTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/bd88742d6c968624acc3fae0d41a365b26ac4e2d","sha":"bd88742d6c968624acc3fae0d41a365b26ac4e2d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/bd88742d6c968624acc3fae0d41a365b26ac4e2d"}],"sha":"96b8cb1699bc739e4eca5ff027bf954e362e3799","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/96b8cb1699bc739e4eca5ff027bf954e362e3799"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/220909633?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan","id":220909633,"login":"analisaperlengkapan","node_id":"U_kgDODSrQQQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/bd88742d6c968624acc3fae0d41a365b26ac4e2d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T17:34:35Z","email":"analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com","name":"analisaperlengkapan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T17:34:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(perlengkapan): the suggestions endpoint could not parse its own query (#873)\n\n`/kebutuhan-bmn/search/suggestions` answered 500 to every caller in every\nenvironment from the day it was written. The query was\n\n    SELECT DISTINCT nama … ORDER BY similarity(nama, $2) DESC\n\nand Postgres rejects that outright: \"for SELECT DISTINCT, ORDER BY\nexpressions must appear in select list\". It fails at PARSE time, so no\ninput reached it, no data was needed to trigger it, and no environment\ndiffered. Reproduced against staging''s own database before touching\nanything.\n\n`GROUP BY nama` yields the same distinct set while making the ordering\nexpression legal — under the group key, `similarity(nama, $2)` is\nfunctionally dependent and therefore addressable. `nama ASC` breaks ties so\ntwo identical calls agree.\n\nSecond fault in the same eight lines, and it could never have surfaced\nwhile the first stopped the statement at parse: `LIMIT $3` was bound from\nan `i32`. Postgres infers that placeholder as int8. This is the third time\nthat exact trap has been paid for here — the sibling list query already\ncarries a comment about it, dated #33.\n\nNothing caught either one because nothing ever called the endpoint. The\nroute-coverage gate walks FRONTEND routes; a backend endpoint with no\ncaller has no route to walk, so \"covered\" and \"never executed\" looked the\nsame. The tests added here are deliberately shallow and deliberately\ninsistent on one thing: it answers, with a shape, for a real role — a\nmatch, a distinct set (which is what `SELECT DISTINCT` was there for, and\nwhat made the ordering illegal), and no match at all, which is how a\ncaller''s first keystroke behaves.\n\nWhile proving the fix, the sibling `/kebutuhan-bmn/search` turned out to be\nbroken too, and worse: it selects `k.*` from the base table and maps the\nresult into the shape of `vw_kebutuhan_bmn_summary`, so the first matching\nrow panics on `invalid column status_nama` — and with `panic = \"abort\"` in\nthe release profile that ends the process, not the request. Three of its\nfilters also name columns the base table does not have. A staging probe\nsees 200 there only because the search happens to match nothing. That is\nits own change with its own tests, not a fix smuggled in beside this one;\nthe reason is recorded at the foot of the new test file so it cannot be\nlost.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b96012e57a39422fcaa431c79eda847ca4d69389","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/trees/b96012e57a39422fcaa431c79eda847ca4d69389"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/commits/bd88742d6c968624acc3fae0d41a365b26ac4e2d","verification":{"payload":"tree b96012e57a39422fcaa431c79eda847ca4d69389\nparent 2738ae07218483a1521d7bda88ace06f8c0d3ecb\nauthor analisaperlengkapan <analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com> 1787938475 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787938475 +0000\n\nfix(perlengkapan): the suggestions endpoint could not parse its own query (#873)\n\n`/kebutuhan-bmn/search/suggestions` answered 500 to every caller in every\nenvironment from the day it was written. The query was\n\n    SELECT DISTINCT nama … ORDER BY similarity(nama, $2) DESC\n\nand Postgres rejects that outright: \"for SELECT DISTINCT, ORDER BY\nexpressions must appear in select list\". It fails at PARSE time, so no\ninput reached it, no data was needed to trigger it, and no environment\ndiffered. Reproduced against staging''s own database before touching\nanything.\n\n`GROUP BY nama` yields the same distinct set while making the ordering\nexpression legal — under the group key, `similarity(nama, $2)` is\nfunctionally dependent and therefore addressable. `nama ASC` breaks ties so\ntwo identical calls agree.\n\nSecond fault in the same eight lines, and it could never have surfaced\nwhile the first stopped the statement at parse: `LIMIT $3` was bound from\nan `i32`. Postgres infers that placeholder as int8. This is the third time\nthat exact trap has been paid for here — the sibling list query already\ncarries a comment about it, dated #33.\n\nNothing caught either one because nothing ever called the endpoint. The\nroute-coverage gate walks FRONTEND routes; a backend endpoint with no\ncaller has no route to walk, so \"covered\" and \"never executed\" looked the\nsame. The tests added here are deliberately shallow and deliberately\ninsistent on one thing: it answers, with a shape, for a real role — a\nmatch, a distinct set (which is what `SELECT DISTINCT` was there for, and\nwhat made the ordering illegal), and no match at all, which is how a\ncaller''s first keystroke behaves.\n\nWhile proving the fix, the sibling `/kebutuhan-bmn/search` turned out to be\nbroken too, and worse: it selects `k.*` from the base table and maps the\nresult into the shape of `vw_kebutuhan_bmn_summary`, so the first matching\nrow panics on `invalid column status_nama` — and with `panic = \"abort\"` in\nthe release profile that ends the process, not the request. Three of its\nfilters also name columns the base table does not have. A staging probe\nsees 200 there only because the search happens to match nothing. That is\nits own change with its own tests, not a fix smuggled in beside this one;\nthe reason is recorded at the foot of the new test file so it cannot be\nlost.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkcarCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArSsQAIXuSGnVKa/MTECNe83OLi2y\ntJkYgBj7BvfjALaFIZ94fFjjyKYD96khTECbSAP4tCHDrxhpRzUIxP+8MKXHrzQP\n9yEG37OE6ZB+zr1uCAWo3VSTtuf88CqgzpevBKUK88Toz2lh3QAUd2U21NrT2HB+\naow+lMDnnLpMG2AqkWga4M0fa31qdhmFrOlaEu/dCFz61h+qIoLuWEEUFb10Pbkj\n+/xd/mi6bdzGlipffAs//93MjoI9Y9AME+u5fHbxBjZ78jjivXxAs8KIOp7bWAk3\nV5wi7qlPvkF6rCoKQS8owFvf/FmfDdeMiWVtkOC3DkMXnOAYfLC3EDGdgg37t7jP\nvvxhsnXvW6iTKS3Rw93DnWVpgB0DbdMaUkpIOyRMMK53bEpmRicOiurWfp/doKs4\nZF15p+iLdTrFLoPPGgwJZQicRH2DN9j4Ihv9Vz6F9uEs+EZnKbFOFkP7aGuLQEnu\n5rwm5aMkknEnpRn4zKyas7RIGHE4UsouJ9E2IkK3Hwjq8KeKxCN4S8eXjlzD7Fth\n1XFOFj0tD7+OqNfeQQdhedD7BRjHBp2GGNdc575tXHvM/jnh3USkP9FdN4c+DDH2\n0379Fp30gyHxyhw2KxWQ5I+APLXTZvaYoTJTetWOVQ1cwakuyxgNyd1s661UHy+4\nVs3IwkgNb08jiG9WVec8\n=/xsF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-28T17:34:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/bd88742d6c968624acc3fae0d41a365b26ac4e2d","node_id":"C_kwDOP93DxNoAKGJkODg3NDJkNmM5Njg2MjRhY2MzZmFlMGQ0MWEzNjViMjZhYzRlMmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/2738ae07218483a1521d7bda88ace06f8c0d3ecb","sha":"2738ae07218483a1521d7bda88ace06f8c0d3ecb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/2738ae07218483a1521d7bda88ace06f8c0d3ecb"}],"sha":"bd88742d6c968624acc3fae0d41a365b26ac4e2d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/bd88742d6c968624acc3fae0d41a365b26ac4e2d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/220909633?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan","id":220909633,"login":"analisaperlengkapan","node_id":"U_kgDODSrQQQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/2738ae07218483a1521d7bda88ace06f8c0d3ecb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T15:17:56Z","email":"analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com","name":"analisaperlengkapan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T15:17:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(perlengkapan): a satker saw every other satker''s campaign response (#871)\n\nA pakaian-dinas campaign is nationwide and pusat-authored. A satker''s\nRESPONSE to it — who they listed, what sizes, where it sits in the\nworkflow, who approved it — is that satker''s data. Nothing enforced the\ndifference: the participation surfaces and the reports built from them all\ntook an unused `_claims`.\n\nMeasured against deployed staging (rc29), operator_a (0200010) against\noperator_b''s satker (0200020):\n\n    GET /pakaian-dinas/pengajuan/{id}/satker  -> 200, BOTH participants\n    GET /pakaian-dinas/satker/{foreign_id}    -> 200, full row\n    GET .../satker/{foreign_id}/aktivitas     -> 200, the other satker''s\n                                                approval trail, with the\n                                                validators'' names and NIPs\n    GET /pakaian-dinas/laporan/daftar-pegawai -> 200, the NATIONAL employee\n                                                list, and passing\n                                                satker_id=0200020 worked too\n\n`POST /pakaian-dinas/validator-action` was the same gap on the write side.\n`determine_next_status` gates the ROLE — \"may a validator_wilayah ever\napprove\" — and has never answered \"may THIS validator approve THIS satker''s\nrow\". It is now scoped, with the read placed before the write, because the\naction stamps an activity row with the actor''s identity before it returns.\n\nWhere the scope goes:\n\n- `push_laporan_filters` takes it, so all six laporan queries get it at\n  once. That function exists because the call sites had already drifted —\n  its own comment records `get_laporan_rekap_ukuran` dropping `satker_id`\n  while the export beside it kept it, so one filter produced a national\n  table on screen and a single-satker spreadsheet from the button next to\n  it. The scope binds BEFORE any client filter, which makes\n  `?satker_id=` narrowing-only rather than a way to name someone else.\n\n- The participant list''s COUNT carries it as well as the page. A scoped\n  page beside a national total still tells the caller exactly how many\n  participants are being withheld.\n\n- The activity trail has no satker column, so it is scoped through its\n  parent participation row. Out of scope it returns an empty list rather\n  than 404 — indistinguishable from \"nothing has happened yet\", so there is\n  no oracle in either direction.\n\nAlso enforced, rather than merely assumed: only pusat may author or delete\na campaign. `pakaian_dinas::scope` already argues that its list-scoping\nneeds no `created_by` escape hatch \"because campaigns can only be authored\nby validator_pusat, who is a cross-satker role and already sees all\". That\nwas documented and never checked — the handler read `claims` for a user id\nand nothing else, so an operator reached campaign creation and was stopped,\nif at all, by business validation. Delete cascades every participant''s\nrows and now needs the same authority.\n\nTwo fixtures were wrong in a way only the scope could reveal.\n`test_pakaian_dinas_validator_workflow` seeded its participation row under\nsatker `0200010` while its auth headers carried `SKR001`, so with scoping\nthe workflow could never start; the campaign tests created their campaign\nas `operator_satker`, which the new gate refuses. Both now say what they\nmean.\n\nTests: 6 integration cases against a real Postgres and 4 e2e against the\nreal stack, each with both halves — the positive half alone passes just as\nwell with no scope at all. Five unit tests pin the laporan builder''s\nplaceholder order, including that a client `satker_id` and the scope are\nboth present and ANDed. Verified by canary: with `from_claims` forced to\n`All`, all five scoping cases fail.\n\nThis finishes pakaian_dinas. Its eight remaining `_claims` handlers are the\nmaster catalogue reads (jenis / spesifikasi / subspesifikasi / ukuran) —\nnational reference data, deliberately readable by any authenticated caller.\nThe census across the rest of perlengkapan stands at 45, the largest block\nbeing kebutuhan_bmn''s 14.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"58c4c51f7be5ba787562cc8560fa283a6aa5a8f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/trees/58c4c51f7be5ba787562cc8560fa283a6aa5a8f5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/commits/2738ae07218483a1521d7bda88ace06f8c0d3ecb","verification":{"payload":"tree 58c4c51f7be5ba787562cc8560fa283a6aa5a8f5\nparent d436074b134d4168046088e6d45be95f1ef8d8b8\nauthor analisaperlengkapan <analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com> 1787930276 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787930276 +0000\n\nfix(perlengkapan): a satker saw every other satker''s campaign response (#871)\n\nA pakaian-dinas campaign is nationwide and pusat-authored. A satker''s\nRESPONSE to it — who they listed, what sizes, where it sits in the\nworkflow, who approved it — is that satker''s data. Nothing enforced the\ndifference: the participation surfaces and the reports built from them all\ntook an unused `_claims`.\n\nMeasured against deployed staging (rc29), operator_a (0200010) against\noperator_b''s satker (0200020):\n\n    GET /pakaian-dinas/pengajuan/{id}/satker  -> 200, BOTH participants\n    GET /pakaian-dinas/satker/{foreign_id}    -> 200, full row\n    GET .../satker/{foreign_id}/aktivitas     -> 200, the other satker''s\n                                                approval trail, with the\n                                                validators'' names and NIPs\n    GET /pakaian-dinas/laporan/daftar-pegawai -> 200, the NATIONAL employee\n                                                list, and passing\n                                                satker_id=0200020 worked too\n\n`POST /pakaian-dinas/validator-action` was the same gap on the write side.\n`determine_next_status` gates the ROLE — \"may a validator_wilayah ever\napprove\" — and has never answered \"may THIS validator approve THIS satker''s\nrow\". It is now scoped, with the read placed before the write, because the\naction stamps an activity row with the actor''s identity before it returns.\n\nWhere the scope goes:\n\n- `push_laporan_filters` takes it, so all six laporan queries get it at\n  once. That function exists because the call sites had already drifted —\n  its own comment records `get_laporan_rekap_ukuran` dropping `satker_id`\n  while the export beside it kept it, so one filter produced a national\n  table on screen and a single-satker spreadsheet from the button next to\n  it. The scope binds BEFORE any client filter, which makes\n  `?satker_id=` narrowing-only rather than a way to name someone else.\n\n- The participant list''s COUNT carries it as well as the page. A scoped\n  page beside a national total still tells the caller exactly how many\n  participants are being withheld.\n\n- The activity trail has no satker column, so it is scoped through its\n  parent participation row. Out of scope it returns an empty list rather\n  than 404 — indistinguishable from \"nothing has happened yet\", so there is\n  no oracle in either direction.\n\nAlso enforced, rather than merely assumed: only pusat may author or delete\na campaign. `pakaian_dinas::scope` already argues that its list-scoping\nneeds no `created_by` escape hatch \"because campaigns can only be authored\nby validator_pusat, who is a cross-satker role and already sees all\". That\nwas documented and never checked — the handler read `claims` for a user id\nand nothing else, so an operator reached campaign creation and was stopped,\nif at all, by business validation. Delete cascades every participant''s\nrows and now needs the same authority.\n\nTwo fixtures were wrong in a way only the scope could reveal.\n`test_pakaian_dinas_validator_workflow` seeded its participation row under\nsatker `0200010` while its auth headers carried `SKR001`, so with scoping\nthe workflow could never start; the campaign tests created their campaign\nas `operator_satker`, which the new gate refuses. Both now say what they\nmean.\n\nTests: 6 integration cases against a real Postgres and 4 e2e against the\nreal stack, each with both halves — the positive half alone passes just as\nwell with no scope at all. Five unit tests pin the laporan builder''s\nplaceholder order, including that a client `satker_id` and the scope are\nboth present and ANDed. Verified by canary: with `from_claims` forced to\n`All`, all five scoping cases fail.\n\nThis finishes pakaian_dinas. Its eight remaining `_claims` handlers are the\nmaster catalogue reads (jenis / spesifikasi / subspesifikasi / ukuran) —\nnational reference data, deliberately readable by any authenticated caller.\nThe census across the rest of perlengkapan stands at 45, the largest block\nbeing kebutuhan_bmn''s 14.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkaakCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxYEQAKxS76kpdutVDU/ZFxARb5U9\nvBhGQkoTTNTo2nxtDktGWge5mPyWKppYHbmiRVOs857D9pB/BvU9FEu3IBy672Zz\n2q3w9Vo422e192s8oKieS7YAeeVq5BUI2c+YHqvkh+fH0qYnbILkCqGqzzGLEKnd\n+Nsk8m/6FCxvDGYffpnrFSRDx9Aa6my+JnZtFLjbnOgmUoN/mHmZup30oxLMDSEv\nt8sGJW68VobpmZn+oi1SWM7tV5OSuyERfURE/WUr8SDF0HQWjmy1+XQiS17Ps+jb\ndf/u7U9K2lODlxzlaSUFPKlEbByX98kiZ8XgirdDf8xK3qWk9+UGbSvRnpNVcDAV\n4nf4gV5yAtVmpaZhw8ehUAo4pPOos5TE6IfheOuaEIbm4qfeONc9SFdC/MF+hV1H\n+InMBbFbBzs4Q3hGsqkZfAcEn4og8j1MZbR6ValNEsjBvEuM8CsyzIB6UDVJCUVS\npopgWSOlU29dL/IcAmpUeNVRAlJQYBgorOkTvBnBKw/n85bFl+OwrAggsAD/fGNL\nqwiltUU37EXoAiObTdYikQK1jTbs52hopTex0q6CzxaNoTIFxedC7oyLeI4p37iB\nbYeE54bq92tZPj6vzUe2G6bfpiELRiwh/6WvgP/H1I47jNfdH6oKKCMPVLLk67Q0\nPUn8Gs9tOESO3q6QNIf4\n=cJE4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-28T15:17:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/2738ae07218483a1521d7bda88ace06f8c0d3ecb","node_id":"C_kwDOP93DxNoAKDI3MzhhZTA3MjE4NDgzYTE1MjFkN2JkYTg4YWNlMDZmOGMwZDNlY2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/d436074b134d4168046088e6d45be95f1ef8d8b8","sha":"d436074b134d4168046088e6d45be95f1ef8d8b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/d436074b134d4168046088e6d45be95f1ef8d8b8"}],"sha":"2738ae07218483a1521d7bda88ace06f8c0d3ecb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/2738ae07218483a1521d7bda88ace06f8c0d3ecb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/220909633?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan","id":220909633,"login":"analisaperlengkapan","node_id":"U_kgDODSrQQQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/d436074b134d4168046088e6d45be95f1ef8d8b8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T13:47:17Z","email":"analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com","name":"analisaperlengkapan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T13:47:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(perlengkapan): any operator could read and rewrite another satker''s staff (#870)\n\nThe pakaian-dinas employee endpoints take the satker straight from the\ncaller: three reads name it in the path, and the profile write named it in\nthe body. All five took an unused `_claims` and checked neither role nor\nsatker, so the gate was \"are you logged in\".\n\nMeasured against deployed staging (rc29), not inferred. operator_a\n(0200010) against operator_b''s satker (0200020):\n\n    GET  /pakaian-dinas/pegawai-satker/0200020              -> 200\n    GET  /pakaian-dinas/pegawai-satker/0200020/with-sizes   -> 200\n    GET  /pakaian-dinas/pegawai-satker/0200020/roster       -> 200\n    POST /pakaian-dinas/pegawai-profile  (b''s employee)     -> 200, row written\n\nThe reads return named people — NIP, name, phone, gender, jabatan,\ngolongan — plus their uniform measurements. The write reached any employee\nby NIP, and the satker it stored came from the request body, so a caller\ncould both relabel an employee and overwrite one they had no claim to. The\nprobe row was removed from staging afterwards.\n\nRefusals answer 404, not 403: a 403 confirms the satker exists and has\nstaff, which is the cross-tenant existence oracle #93 closed.\n\nThe reads are scoped at the REPOSITORY signature, not at the three\nhandlers, so the compiler is what enforces coverage rather than a list\nsomeone has to remember to extend.\n\nThe write now derives the employee''s satker from\n`integrasi.mysimkari_pegawai` — the SoT for employee identity — instead of\ntrusting the body, and carries the scope predicate INSIDE the upsert''s row\nselector. A check in a preceding statement is a check the next refactor can\nleave behind, and for the bulk endpoint a check that ran once over the\nbatch would be one the caller can widen after it passed: each row is\nadmitted on its own, and the response count reports how many actually\nlanded. One consequence worth stating: a NIP absent from MySIMKARI can no\nlonger be given a profile by anyone, cross-satker roles included. That is\nthe SSoT rule the project already holds — consumers do not invent master\ndata — and it is now enforced rather than assumed.\n\nThree things this touched on the way past, each a root cause rather than a\nworkaround:\n\n- `satker_code_in_scope` had grown a verbatim copy of the same wilayah\n  query in two repositories and was about to acquire a third. The query is\n  now `SatkerScope::WILAYAH_MEMBERSHIP_SQL`, one definition, and\n  `scope_and`/`as_refs` moved beside it for the same reason.\n\n- The placeholder numbering the scope predicate depends on is untypeable:\n  the upsert binds $1..$13, so the predicate must land on $14. At $1 it\n  would compare the satker column against the NIP, match nothing, and look\n  exactly like a working deny to anyone who only tested the negative case.\n  Seven unit tests pin it, including the bind count it rests on.\n\n- The phantom-relation guard read prose as SQL. A comment inside a SQL\n  literal saying \"infer the type from the target column the way it does\"\n  parsed as `FROM the` and was reported as a missing relation. It now\n  strips SQL comments before matching — verified in both directions: prose\n  no longer matches, and a real `perlengkapan.ghost_table_canary` is still\n  caught, at the right line. Third time a guard here has read a comment as\n  code (#856, #857).\n\nTests: 9 integration cases against a real Postgres (own satker, cross\nsatker, wilayah in-region and out, cross-satker role, no satker identity,\nown write, cross-satker write refused with the record verified unchanged,\nbody-supplied satker ignored, bulk batch admitting only the caller''s row)\nand 5 e2e cases against the real stack. Verified by canary: with\n`from_claims` forced to `All`, five of the nine fail. The four positives\nstay green, which is the point — a suite of only positives passes just as\nwell with no scope at all, and that is how this survived.\n\nNot widened here: the campaign, pengajuan-satker and laporan surfaces in\nthe same module are still unscoped by-id, and the rest of the census stands\nat 33 handlers taking `Path(...)` beside an unused `_claims`.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4af17cd6e2eee9ac7f5096f4e0c9a1d409602772","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/trees/4af17cd6e2eee9ac7f5096f4e0c9a1d409602772"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/commits/d436074b134d4168046088e6d45be95f1ef8d8b8","verification":{"payload":"tree 4af17cd6e2eee9ac7f5096f4e0c9a1d409602772\nparent c03fcc70bd064e53a5eff58f94fce0e5d3952a21\nauthor analisaperlengkapan <analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com> 1787924837 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787924837 +0000\n\nfix(perlengkapan): any operator could read and rewrite another satker''s staff (#870)\n\nThe pakaian-dinas employee endpoints take the satker straight from the\ncaller: three reads name it in the path, and the profile write named it in\nthe body. All five took an unused `_claims` and checked neither role nor\nsatker, so the gate was \"are you logged in\".\n\nMeasured against deployed staging (rc29), not inferred. operator_a\n(0200010) against operator_b''s satker (0200020):\n\n    GET  /pakaian-dinas/pegawai-satker/0200020              -> 200\n    GET  /pakaian-dinas/pegawai-satker/0200020/with-sizes   -> 200\n    GET  /pakaian-dinas/pegawai-satker/0200020/roster       -> 200\n    POST /pakaian-dinas/pegawai-profile  (b''s employee)     -> 200, row written\n\nThe reads return named people — NIP, name, phone, gender, jabatan,\ngolongan — plus their uniform measurements. The write reached any employee\nby NIP, and the satker it stored came from the request body, so a caller\ncould both relabel an employee and overwrite one they had no claim to. The\nprobe row was removed from staging afterwards.\n\nRefusals answer 404, not 403: a 403 confirms the satker exists and has\nstaff, which is the cross-tenant existence oracle #93 closed.\n\nThe reads are scoped at the REPOSITORY signature, not at the three\nhandlers, so the compiler is what enforces coverage rather than a list\nsomeone has to remember to extend.\n\nThe write now derives the employee''s satker from\n`integrasi.mysimkari_pegawai` — the SoT for employee identity — instead of\ntrusting the body, and carries the scope predicate INSIDE the upsert''s row\nselector. A check in a preceding statement is a check the next refactor can\nleave behind, and for the bulk endpoint a check that ran once over the\nbatch would be one the caller can widen after it passed: each row is\nadmitted on its own, and the response count reports how many actually\nlanded. One consequence worth stating: a NIP absent from MySIMKARI can no\nlonger be given a profile by anyone, cross-satker roles included. That is\nthe SSoT rule the project already holds — consumers do not invent master\ndata — and it is now enforced rather than assumed.\n\nThree things this touched on the way past, each a root cause rather than a\nworkaround:\n\n- `satker_code_in_scope` had grown a verbatim copy of the same wilayah\n  query in two repositories and was about to acquire a third. The query is\n  now `SatkerScope::WILAYAH_MEMBERSHIP_SQL`, one definition, and\n  `scope_and`/`as_refs` moved beside it for the same reason.\n\n- The placeholder numbering the scope predicate depends on is untypeable:\n  the upsert binds $1..$13, so the predicate must land on $14. At $1 it\n  would compare the satker column against the NIP, match nothing, and look\n  exactly like a working deny to anyone who only tested the negative case.\n  Seven unit tests pin it, including the bind count it rests on.\n\n- The phantom-relation guard read prose as SQL. A comment inside a SQL\n  literal saying \"infer the type from the target column the way it does\"\n  parsed as `FROM the` and was reported as a missing relation. It now\n  strips SQL comments before matching — verified in both directions: prose\n  no longer matches, and a real `perlengkapan.ghost_table_canary` is still\n  caught, at the right line. Third time a guard here has read a comment as\n  code (#856, #857).\n\nTests: 9 integration cases against a real Postgres (own satker, cross\nsatker, wilayah in-region and out, cross-satker role, no satker identity,\nown write, cross-satker write refused with the record verified unchanged,\nbody-supplied satker ignored, bulk batch admitting only the caller''s row)\nand 5 e2e cases against the real stack. Verified by canary: with\n`from_claims` forced to `All`, five of the nine fail. The four positives\nstay green, which is the point — a suite of only positives passes just as\nwell with no scope at all, and that is how this survived.\n\nNot widened here: the campaign, pengajuan-satker and laporan surfaces in\nthe same module are still unscoped by-id, and the rest of the census stands\nat 33 handlers taking `Path(...)` beside an unused `_claims`.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkZFlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAd6YQAAnLYyB49Vt2JBMpMH+1uDuu\ntg/vKXDzODnai2qCggBlxoNygcFOiU6SYZtm4wJ8KH9U90EFHeIe78ILGPrrBjCm\nklvB+dBCHQ5sFQ/pUwvghxwssU+7lupj+NicLr0qufotZx7HnTjk9vX6nQU4hw0l\n7gRt+fLyeRqsUbDZRqf6ODoGACXrXDigyeONsY2uo3/NNBhPjn8iQJ6JrHVG9+bz\nyUrCEScp0KzQ/OmgUJJIaaXC6rsZ6D2P+ue0mKmO9ZoNkZimQfSKknBu3QqvgOV+\nSMPIlCWUj+M4wKRimdzhigkvpCylI23d0ddkqFnKc1gyhom5yaAMwbJh65zjYOWT\nf2mAwhtWGwBuv9MqybH1oG4lP0RJkNsgwUB/gik5157SYvJOwjXbIZUK6sJrOPMS\n41bIxaOtlYAlG7b5NhNqlWjKOkIGI/+t/ENMJc6GiEWfTfHDtv5K7eFd3wTXkpiL\nwSiRLexhQ3v21xcU3chJeRSgHRjjqdQAaeV6DymNLLsKu3ECcg7Oi9v/aTgsMolA\n9aKECgPJa18rLEyUoREiVdIQwmQJLwEust4gAJBDsjcdeWSGtoA2qywbFOhyNTKB\nDV8+0UbbOR58GP5U679p9zX94BZrO9N6Q6pO/ck6AbVewQvwzAnxx5FOsWxYBwmc\nDN8Zke85Q40PDNELta66\n=LOyd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-28T13:47:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/d436074b134d4168046088e6d45be95f1ef8d8b8","node_id":"C_kwDOP93DxNoAKGQ0MzYwNzRiMTM0ZDQxNjgwNDYwODhlNmQ0NWJlOTVmMWVmOGQ4Yjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/c03fcc70bd064e53a5eff58f94fce0e5d3952a21","sha":"c03fcc70bd064e53a5eff58f94fce0e5d3952a21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/c03fcc70bd064e53a5eff58f94fce0e5d3952a21"}],"sha":"d436074b134d4168046088e6d45be95f1ef8d8b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/d436074b134d4168046088e6d45be95f1ef8d8b8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/220909633?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan","id":220909633,"login":"analisaperlengkapan","node_id":"U_kgDODSrQQQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/c03fcc70bd064e53a5eff58f94fce0e5d3952a21/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T12:28:05Z","email":"analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com","name":"analisaperlengkapan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T12:28:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(perlengkapan): any operator could rewrite any satker''s usulan penghapusan (#869)\n\n* fix(perlengkapan): any operator could rewrite any satker''s usulan penghapusan\n\n`list_penghapusan_bmn` was satker-scoped. Every BY-ID endpoint in the module\nwas not. Role gating answered \"may this role ever do this\" and stopped there,\nso a caller holding the right role reached any record in the country.\n\n`update_penghapusan_bmn` did not even check the role: it took `_claims` and\nignored it, leaving the workflow *status* as the only thing between a stranger\nand the row. Proven against deployed staging (rc29), one satker to another:\n\n    operator_b (0200020) PUT  operator_a''s (0200010) DRAFT  -> 200, alasan rewritten\n    operator_b (0200020) DELETE the same usulan             -> 200, status CANCELLED\n    operator_a (0200010) GET  operator_b''s usulan           -> 200 on all five\n                                                               read surfaces\n\nThe scope now lives in the repository signature, so it is the compiler that\nenforces coverage rather than a list someone has to keep current: `get_by_id`\ntakes a `SatkerScope`, and every by-id path in the module reaches its record\nthrough it. `update` and `delete` carry the predicate in the UPDATE statement\nitself — a check that happens in an earlier statement is a check the next\nrefactor can leave behind. `forward_to_pusat`, `verifikasi_pusat` and\n`return_to_operator` stamp a validator identity BEFORE they transition, so\nthose gained an explicit scoped read ahead of the write.\n\nOut of scope answers 404, not 403: 403 confirms the id exists in someone\nelse''s satker, which is the existence oracle #93 closed for satker detail.\n\nTwo signatures crossed clippy''s argument limit once the scope joined them, so\nthe parameters that always travel together became `TransitionActor` and\n`LampiranUpload` rather than an `#[allow]`.\n\nTests: five repository unit tests pin the placeholder numbering (the failure\nmode signatures cannot catch — `update` binds $1..$7, so the predicate must\nstart at $8, and at $1 it would compare satker_code against a date), and ten\ne2e cases assert containment across every by-id surface with ids derived from\nthe API rather than hard-coded. The e2e probes are non-destructive so they\nsurvive a retry.\n\nStill open, and deliberately not widened here: the same census across the rest\nof perlengkapan — 35 handlers take `Path(...)` beside an unused `_claims`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\n* test(perlengkapan): the wilayah fixture named a satker that does not exist\n\nThe two penghapusan workflow tests sent `x-satker-id: WIL001` for the\nvalidator_wilayah. That is not a satker code — it named nothing in the\nfixture and nothing in MySIMKARI. It went unnoticed for as long as no\nby-id handler read the claim, and turned into a 404 the moment the scope\nin this branch did: an unresolvable wilayah correctly matches no rows.\n\nA validator_wilayah''s claim carries their OWN satker code, the Kejati''s,\nand the tier is resolved from it through `integrasi.v_satker_wilayah`.\nKJT01 is the Kejati the fixture already puts above SKR001, so that is\nwhat the header now carries.\n\nAlso adds the half the suite was missing. Both existing tests assert only\nthat KJT01''s validator CAN forward SKR001''s usulan — which also passes\nwhen the scope is absent entirely, which is exactly how the gap survived.\nThe new test is the half that fails without it: KJT02 supervises SKR003,\nnot SKR001, and its validator gets 404 (not 403 — 403 would confirm the\nid exists under another Kejati, the existence oracle #93 closed). It then\nasserts the record is unchanged, because `forward_to_pusat` stamps the\nvalidator identity BEFORE the transition, so a scope placed only at the\ntransition would still have branded the row. Verified by canary: with\n`from_claims` forced to `All` the new test fails 200-vs-404.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"335dc3d56d31100b9167be6d3e8efd6ba6db989d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/trees/335dc3d56d31100b9167be6d3e8efd6ba6db989d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/commits/c03fcc70bd064e53a5eff58f94fce0e5d3952a21","verification":{"payload":"tree 335dc3d56d31100b9167be6d3e8efd6ba6db989d\nparent da82dfb28de12f0b428137c84c65d7284d1811ba\nauthor analisaperlengkapan <analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com> 1787920085 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787920085 +0000\n\nfix(perlengkapan): any operator could rewrite any satker''s usulan penghapusan (#869)\n\n* fix(perlengkapan): any operator could rewrite any satker''s usulan penghapusan\n\n`list_penghapusan_bmn` was satker-scoped. Every BY-ID endpoint in the module\nwas not. Role gating answered \"may this role ever do this\" and stopped there,\nso a caller holding the right role reached any record in the country.\n\n`update_penghapusan_bmn` did not even check the role: it took `_claims` and\nignored it, leaving the workflow *status* as the only thing between a stranger\nand the row. Proven against deployed staging (rc29), one satker to another:\n\n    operator_b (0200020) PUT  operator_a''s (0200010) DRAFT  -> 200, alasan rewritten\n    operator_b (0200020) DELETE the same usulan             -> 200, status CANCELLED\n    operator_a (0200010) GET  operator_b''s usulan           -> 200 on all five\n                                                               read surfaces\n\nThe scope now lives in the repository signature, so it is the compiler that\nenforces coverage rather than a list someone has to keep current: `get_by_id`\ntakes a `SatkerScope`, and every by-id path in the module reaches its record\nthrough it. `update` and `delete` carry the predicate in the UPDATE statement\nitself — a check that happens in an earlier statement is a check the next\nrefactor can leave behind. `forward_to_pusat`, `verifikasi_pusat` and\n`return_to_operator` stamp a validator identity BEFORE they transition, so\nthose gained an explicit scoped read ahead of the write.\n\nOut of scope answers 404, not 403: 403 confirms the id exists in someone\nelse''s satker, which is the existence oracle #93 closed for satker detail.\n\nTwo signatures crossed clippy''s argument limit once the scope joined them, so\nthe parameters that always travel together became `TransitionActor` and\n`LampiranUpload` rather than an `#[allow]`.\n\nTests: five repository unit tests pin the placeholder numbering (the failure\nmode signatures cannot catch — `update` binds $1..$7, so the predicate must\nstart at $8, and at $1 it would compare satker_code against a date), and ten\ne2e cases assert containment across every by-id surface with ids derived from\nthe API rather than hard-coded. The e2e probes are non-destructive so they\nsurvive a retry.\n\nStill open, and deliberately not widened here: the same census across the rest\nof perlengkapan — 35 handlers take `Path(...)` beside an unused `_claims`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\n* test(perlengkapan): the wilayah fixture named a satker that does not exist\n\nThe two penghapusan workflow tests sent `x-satker-id: WIL001` for the\nvalidator_wilayah. That is not a satker code — it named nothing in the\nfixture and nothing in MySIMKARI. It went unnoticed for as long as no\nby-id handler read the claim, and turned into a 404 the moment the scope\nin this branch did: an unresolvable wilayah correctly matches no rows.\n\nA validator_wilayah''s claim carries their OWN satker code, the Kejati''s,\nand the tier is resolved from it through `integrasi.v_satker_wilayah`.\nKJT01 is the Kejati the fixture already puts above SKR001, so that is\nwhat the header now carries.\n\nAlso adds the half the suite was missing. Both existing tests assert only\nthat KJT01''s validator CAN forward SKR001''s usulan — which also passes\nwhen the scope is absent entirely, which is exactly how the gap survived.\nThe new test is the half that fails without it: KJT02 supervises SKR003,\nnot SKR001, and its validator gets 404 (not 403 — 403 would confirm the\nid exists under another Kejati, the existence oracle #93 closed). It then\nasserts the record is unchanged, because `forward_to_pusat` stamps the\nvalidator identity BEFORE the transition, so a scope placed only at the\ntransition would still have branded the row. Verified by canary: with\n`from_claims` forced to `All` the new test fails 200-vs-404.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkX7VCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVHoQADX2dJkgWLmiXxFVHXRjup8x\nJ1VNoYqkFDCIAecX/kK4cQZDHbRhjWTvOAJloMYz8NVcxHocxlUjDWh/IahcrKNY\n4u19GcqXHPWVf7kn5UOLpBiX6sWpfoItuIM5cU3gcwMJUvWKLc7g03tLwPwcdG+x\n1nJxqdoFAXAbkZYGNNwcozKyK44BisEwZsXtYChOjCmGvAflGGmk4WneHpzZjU/o\n9FVasfNbVMnk+Ph9Du/9wm+LSz+r6ne/DVznMcc9kTSM8Y8hHRtqvcF1LIB5PwTl\nZEPhYpiadnnfEDJumD6W4vzQXOm8DxZVy24sTi3J32WVAoO0Lg6GE5wdXJlN1rr0\nyENEtRkJoeQ+7+IBRVdr3ACcTjJMz8hcwd2qU13fe0zm/aABAPIA1g/GN3V4WkBB\nXnwbg9TYs/Kr0BbWWr7rvPH71WShY91JFDmvMCJUujuQwg4QjkRrd+/zXAhIX/U6\nWwf0ej0NeOUCzNTEayVZsEyQINtq2L/Z8EmkWRLHKuYOXvRtPX4h7yxUhBRPsiYE\nd7MT9yyU7AlUijzhC2bnMPyryit0OVkPXxroqsjwSXn9Q2IIO9iFypNhKJ3H30R4\nzC7wOacgtpbeQWtIOUwXtOXCSYosLDHAEANJD8FtROkfnFe4gOsx11PeXaOLHlVL\n7Pd5Y55iJZnJ53m8mDcb\n=kszG\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-28T12:28:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/c03fcc70bd064e53a5eff58f94fce0e5d3952a21","node_id":"C_kwDOP93DxNoAKGMwM2ZjYzcwYmQwNjRlNTNhNWVmZjU4Zjk0ZmNlMGU1ZDM5NTJhMjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/da82dfb28de12f0b428137c84c65d7284d1811ba","sha":"da82dfb28de12f0b428137c84c65d7284d1811ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/da82dfb28de12f0b428137c84c65d7284d1811ba"}],"sha":"c03fcc70bd064e53a5eff58f94fce0e5d3952a21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/c03fcc70bd064e53a5eff58f94fce0e5d3952a21"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/220909633?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan","id":220909633,"login":"analisaperlengkapan","node_id":"U_kgDODSrQQQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/da82dfb28de12f0b428137c84c65d7284d1811ba/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T10:34:15Z","email":"analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com","name":"analisaperlengkapan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T10:34:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(perlengkapan): probe \"tidak memblokir\" yang memblokir 55 detik (#868)\n\n`fetch_sync_status` sudah memperlakukan integrasi yang tak terjangkau sebagai\n\"unknown\", bukan \"risky\" — komentarnya menegaskan probe ini TIDAK boleh\nmemblokir keputusan Validator Pusat. Tapi tidak memblokir pada HASIL bukan tidak\nmemblokir pada WAKTU: kedua probe berjalan berurutan, tanpa batas waktunya\nsendiri.\n\nSaat integrasi tak terjangkau (NetworkPolicy membuka 50053 sementara service-nya\n50051 — #865), itu berarti 25 detik lalu 30 detik pada `keputusan-pusat`:\n\n    07:34:11.717  request masuk\n    07:34:36.900  mysimkari menyerah        (+25,2s)\n    07:35:06.935  siman menyerah            (+30,0s)\n    07:35:06.960  SELURUH kerja DB selesai  (+0,025s)\n\nGateway memutus klien di 30 detik, jadi tiap persetujuan mengembalikan 504\npadahal transisinya berhasil ~20 detik kemudian lewat `cancel_safe`.\n\nNetpol-nya sudah diperbaiki dan `keputusan-pusat` kini 0,10 detik. Tapi tak ada\napa pun yang mencegah ini terulang begitu integrasi lambat atau mati lagi —\nitulah yang diperbaiki di sini:\n\n- kedua probe jalan BERSAMAAN (`tokio::join!`), jadi batas waktunya menutupi\n  keduanya, bukan masing-masing;\n- satu plafon keras 3 detik untuk seluruh operasi — jauh di bawah 30 detik milik\n  gateway, jauh di atas round-trip sehat (terukur 0,02 detik in-cluster setelah\n  policy benar);\n- habis waktu menghasilkan nilai \"unknown\" yang SAMA dengan jalur error\n  per-probe, jadi ia tetap dibaca sebagai tidak-berisiko dan tak pernah mengunci\n  keputusan.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f618d2ade8089327561ee9ea7e74ddac3267eefd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/trees/f618d2ade8089327561ee9ea7e74ddac3267eefd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/commits/da82dfb28de12f0b428137c84c65d7284d1811ba","verification":{"payload":"tree f618d2ade8089327561ee9ea7e74ddac3267eefd\nparent 1285063b4a81676a09cf01fb91c1487ccda79538\nauthor analisaperlengkapan <analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com> 1787913255 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787913255 +0000\n\nfix(perlengkapan): probe \"tidak memblokir\" yang memblokir 55 detik (#868)\n\n`fetch_sync_status` sudah memperlakukan integrasi yang tak terjangkau sebagai\n\"unknown\", bukan \"risky\" — komentarnya menegaskan probe ini TIDAK boleh\nmemblokir keputusan Validator Pusat. Tapi tidak memblokir pada HASIL bukan tidak\nmemblokir pada WAKTU: kedua probe berjalan berurutan, tanpa batas waktunya\nsendiri.\n\nSaat integrasi tak terjangkau (NetworkPolicy membuka 50053 sementara service-nya\n50051 — #865), itu berarti 25 detik lalu 30 detik pada `keputusan-pusat`:\n\n    07:34:11.717  request masuk\n    07:34:36.900  mysimkari menyerah        (+25,2s)\n    07:35:06.935  siman menyerah            (+30,0s)\n    07:35:06.960  SELURUH kerja DB selesai  (+0,025s)\n\nGateway memutus klien di 30 detik, jadi tiap persetujuan mengembalikan 504\npadahal transisinya berhasil ~20 detik kemudian lewat `cancel_safe`.\n\nNetpol-nya sudah diperbaiki dan `keputusan-pusat` kini 0,10 detik. Tapi tak ada\napa pun yang mencegah ini terulang begitu integrasi lambat atau mati lagi —\nitulah yang diperbaiki di sini:\n\n- kedua probe jalan BERSAMAAN (`tokio::join!`), jadi batas waktunya menutupi\n  keduanya, bukan masing-masing;\n- satu plafon keras 3 detik untuk seluruh operasi — jauh di bawah 30 detik milik\n  gateway, jauh di atas round-trip sehat (terukur 0,02 detik in-cluster setelah\n  policy benar);\n- habis waktu menghasilkan nilai \"unknown\" yang SAMA dengan jalur error\n  per-probe, jadi ia tetap dibaca sebagai tidak-berisiko dan tak pernah mengunci\n  keputusan.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkWQnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQmcQAGHh3Eb5Dgjw9ROhqdvecCGV\nI9uEJ/5h13jN6RjXfTwcT+9ZS2TRA+uG0dOV0kSxTIrNQAKqNvJn38JXKR8WN2j5\nvZwKxmRHmHDxEO6gScUfjwxupPnDsdb6vRrbarYD2jK2lmAYZaGjw+GStOLsovFN\nRLnVn8eMCBMeIhALTtkVHwfi+wEImAkOoDecgLZlWCj2Ju9/N4OV/m2hlmp+y/xa\nnSO8GJXqSlwbfkvK4mn+Ig990Fes/NTSwzzowFDP6uP/orSMAbD9r8UN8kl5oC37\nfHmLg+eMX6AHKG9sZg14Ivrlie5DcjwUQt9OvKcvLjMZoSI5ithdvi8961u1TA++\nEgfxRPJ1olycrcUqeALeeRixrmhRBFKBrs3fQRoZH8+/QxMh0+7+UT5bQs5fy/fd\nbctqLnksWmQdDTxatnUarumWB6Iuu7awFJJiVRaaDPcu9FlypH+wWcPqLvMdTkLt\nR/Tp9zrAQyRw7x0cYrlVdHCxbNg+OhNeZtrgGl69Pq1Nt12ofPZmJ3AiCahlOacJ\nzbd9ICi3KNG/pRhzC8IRbvd87a6fCiFXGX9C7YqV+WA4Cbpt8oY9tVoxQZ+985Uc\nZbI5IvA9cQBsLWLLiKwHe3Om9xAgsBqZPREgfOwokzUK0ujBEx23LO3gTS27hu0s\nbG/3rVTgZHj5fjYbKPcD\n=D+DA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-28T10:34:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/da82dfb28de12f0b428137c84c65d7284d1811ba","node_id":"C_kwDOP93DxNoAKGRhODJkZmIyOGRlMTJmMGI0MjgxMzdjODRjNjVkNzI4NGQxODExYmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commit/1285063b4a81676a09cf01fb91c1487ccda79538","sha":"1285063b4a81676a09cf01fb91c1487ccda79538","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/1285063b4a81676a09cf01fb91c1487ccda79538"}],"sha":"da82dfb28de12f0b428137c84c65d7284d1811ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/da82dfb28de12f0b428137c84c65d7284d1811ba"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/220909633?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/analisaperlengkapan","id":220909633,"login":"analisaperlengkapan","node_id":"U_kgDODSrQQQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/analisaperlengkapan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/commits/1285063b4a81676a09cf01fb91c1487ccda79538/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T10:01:08Z","email":"analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com","name":"analisaperlengkapan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T10:01:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(e2e): asersi dropdown satker membaca sekali dan balapan dengan fetch-nya (#867)\n\nAssertion (3) memanggil `allTextContents()` lalu membandingkannya dengan\n`expect(array).toEqual(...)`. Keduanya tidak menunggu: `allTextContents()`\nadalah snapshot tanpa auto-wait, dan `expect` atas nilai biasa tidak mengulang.\n\nBaris dan dropdown datang dari DUA request berbeda. Terukur di staging:\n\n    bank-aset?page=1&per_page=25   0,53s  0,69s  0,88s\n    bank-aset/filter-options       1,81s  1,58s  1,79s\n\n`filter-options` mengagregasi hitungan atas seluruh scope, jadi konsisten 2–3×\nlebih lambat. Assertion (1) menunggu baris muncul, sehingga saat eksekusi sampai\ndi (3) daftar sudah tiba dan opsinya biasanya belum. Bacaan itu balapan dengan\nfetch-nya dan mengembalikan `[]` — yang di output kegagalan TIDAK bisa dibedakan\ndari backend yang mengembalikan kosong, dan sempat menyesatkan diagnosis ke arah\nsana. API-nya sebenarnya benar: dipanggil langsung ia mengembalikan tepat 7\nsatker yang diharapkan, dan di browser dropdown-nya terisi penuh bila diberi\nwaktu.\n\nDi CI stack-nya lokal dan cukup cepat untuk menyembunyikannya; lawan staging ia\ngagal tiap kali.\n\n`dropdownSatkerNames` juga dipecah: `expect` di dalamnya dipindah keluar supaya\ntarget `expect.poll` murni — poll yang targetnya melempar akan berhenti, bukan\nmengulang.\n\nDiverifikasi lawan staging: `validator_wilayah` yang tadinya gagal kini lulus.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9cf045895ae427232406134d29e8f0caa424136d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/trees/9cf045895ae427232406134d29e8f0caa424136d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/analisaperlengkapan/simpel2/git/commits/1285063b4a81676a09cf01fb91c1487ccda79538","verification":{"payload":"tree 9cf045895ae427232406134d29e8f0caa424136d\nparent f9f7d825ec85fe02f714fe0f126b9129533541f8\nauthor analisaperlengkapan <analisaperlengkapan@gmail.com> 1787911268 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787911268 +0000\n\ntest(e2e): asersi dropdown satker membaca sekali dan balapan dengan fetch-nya (#867)\n\nAssertion (3) memanggil `allTextContents()` lalu membandingkannya dengan\n`expect(array).toEqual(...)`. Keduanya tidak menunggu: `allTextContents()`\nadalah snapshot tanpa auto-wait, dan `expect` atas nilai biasa tidak mengulang.\n\nBaris dan dropdown datang dari DUA request berbeda. Terukur di staging:\n\n    bank-aset?page=1&per_page=25   0,53s  0,69s  0,88s\n    bank-aset/filter-options       1,81s  1,58s  1,79s\n\n`filter-options` mengagregasi hitungan atas seluruh scope, jadi konsisten 2–3×\nlebih lambat. Assertion (1) menunggu baris muncul, sehingga saat eksekusi sampai\ndi (3) daftar sudah tiba dan opsinya biasanya belum. Bacaan itu balapan dengan\nfetch-nya dan mengembalikan `[]` — yang di output kegagalan TIDAK bisa dibedakan\ndari backend yang mengembalikan kosong, dan sempat menyesatkan diagnosis ke arah\nsana. API-nya sebenarnya benar: dipanggil langsung ia mengembalikan tepat 7\nsatker yang diharapkan, dan di browser dropdown-nya terisi penuh bila diberi\nwaktu.\n\nDi CI stack-nya lokal dan cukup cepat untuk menyembunyikannya; lawan staging ia\ngagal tiap kali.\n\n`dropdownSatkerNames` juga dipecah: `expect` di dalamnya dipindah keluar supaya\ntarget `expect.poll` murni — poll yang targetnya melempar akan berhenti, bukan\nmengulang.\n\nDiverifikasi lawan staging: `validator_wilayah` yang tadinya gagal kini lulus.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUqQeBUFcU2eAw2EZwRgwn\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkVxkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASSYQAGKrMmA4iprNGR