rred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/PhoenixWild29/APFA-Prod/commit/75b60f421c9e0db11a5dcf7004772c8ef4eee602","node_id":"C_kwDOP98E2doAKDc1YjYwZjQyMWM5ZTBkYjExYTVkY2Y3MDA0NzcyYzhlZjRlZWU2MDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/PhoenixWild29/APFA-Prod/commit/b7993ef0def74966b8544721fe8b4ca3ace5db4a","sha":"b7993ef0def74966b8544721fe8b4ca3ace5db4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PhoenixWild29/APFA-Prod/commits/b7993ef0def74966b8544721fe8b4ca3ace5db4a"}],"sha":"75b60f421c9e0db11a5dcf7004772c8ef4eee602","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PhoenixWild29/APFA-Prod/commits/75b60f421c9e0db11a5dcf7004772c8ef4eee602"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/112887922?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhoenixWild29/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhoenixWild29/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhoenixWild29/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhoenixWild29/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PhoenixWild29","id":112887922,"login":"PhoenixWild29","node_id":"U_kgDOBrqIcg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhoenixWild29/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhoenixWild29/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhoenixWild29/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhoenixWild29/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhoenixWild29/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhoenixWild29","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PhoenixWild29/APFA-Prod/commits/b7993ef0def74966b8544721fe8b4ca3ace5db4a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T19:40:16Z","email":"112887922+PhoenixWild29@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Samuel J Shamber"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T19:40:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: deploy-pipeline hardening (healthcheck sentinel, structured exceptions, circuit breakers) (#315)\n\nGroups three independent, reviewed deploy-pipeline improvements into one PR.\n\n1) Health check — two-phase sentinel\n   - Remove the Dockerfile HEALTHCHECK (start_period 90s) that was silently\n     overridden by docker-compose.yml (300s).\n   - entrypoint.sh removes a stale sentinel, then writes /tmp/migrations_done\n     immediately before exec uvicorn (after Alembic).\n   - compose healthcheck switches to CMD-SHELL, gating `curl -sf` on the\n     sentinel so failed checks during migrations don''t burn retries.\n   - Harden monitoring config bind-mounts read-only (:ro): prometheus.yml,\n     alerts.yml, grafana-dashboards (data volumes stay rw).\n   - Add docker-compose.override.yml.example (live --reload dev) and gitignore\n     the real docker-compose.override.yml.\n\n2) Structured exceptions — new app/exceptions.py\n   - Replace 5 sentinel error strings (retrieve_context + market tools) with a\n     typed hierarchy: RAGIndexUnavailableError, RAGRetrievalError,\n     ToolExecutionError (under RAGError/ExternalServiceError/APFAError).\n   - LLM-safe tool wrappers convert exceptions back to strings; retriever_agent\n     degrades to confidence 0.0; the retriever test endpoint maps errors to\n     503/500 and fixes a latent Pydantic-v2 500 (string treated as List[str]).\n\n3) Circuit breakers — wire get_breaker()/CircuitBreakerOpen into 8 sites\n   - OpenAI (analyzer + orchestrator, shared breaker), MinIO (both uploads),\n     Resend, Stripe (x4), YouTube (x3). All surface in /health.\n\nReview fixes folded in: analyzer returns non-empty messages (avoids\n_run_advice_graph result[\"messages\"][-1] IndexError); batch upload appends its\nresult dict and corrects counters before `continue`; retriever test re-raises\nHTTPException before the generic handler; entrypoint sentinel ordering pinned.\n\nTests: tests/test_exceptions.py (hierarchy, raises, wrappers, retriever_agent\ndegradation, endpoint 503/500).","tree":{"sha":"0a231ef8aee5b0581160dc1a75c3da86dbd2f0bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PhoenixWild29/APFA-Prod/git/trees/0a231ef8aee5b0581160dc1a75c3da86dbd2f0bf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PhoenixWild29/APFA-Prod/git/commits/b7993ef0def74966b8544721fe8b4ca3ace5db4a","verification":{"payload":"tree 0a231ef8aee5b0581160dc1a75c3da86dbd2f0bf\nparent 4d1a664a4c6fbd358a89ab406fbd2c1d5c950287\nauthor Samuel J Shamber <112887922+PhoenixWild29@users.noreply.github.com> 1786822816 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786822816 -0400\n\nfeat: deploy-pipeline hardening (healthcheck sentinel, structured exceptions, circuit breakers) (#315)\n\nGroups three independent, reviewed deploy-pipeline improvements into one PR.\n\n1) Health check — two-phase sentinel\n   - Remove the Dockerfile HEALTHCHECK (start_period 90s) that was silently\n     overridden by docker-compose.yml (300s).\n   - entrypoint.sh removes a stale sentinel, then writes /tmp/migrations_done\n     immediately before exec uvicorn (after Alembic).\n   - compose healthcheck switches to CMD-SHELL, gating `curl -sf` on the\n     sentinel so failed checks during migrations don''t burn retries.\n   - Harden monitoring config bind-mounts read-only (:ro): prometheus.yml,\n     alerts.yml, grafana-dashboards (data volumes stay rw).\n   - Add docker-compose.override.yml.example (live --reload dev) and gitignore\n     the real docker-compose.override.yml.\n\n2) Structured exceptions — new app/exceptions.py\n   - Replace 5 sentinel error strings (retrieve_context + market tools) with a\n     typed hierarchy: RAGIndexUnavailableError, RAGRetrievalError,\n     ToolExecutionError (under RAGError/ExternalServiceError/APFAError).\n   - LLM-safe tool wrappers convert exceptions back to strings; retriever_agent\n     degrades to confidence 0.0; the retriever test endpoint maps errors to\n     503/500 and fixes a latent Pydantic-v2 500 (string treated as List[str]).\n\n3) Circuit breakers — wire get_breaker()/CircuitBreakerOpen into 8 sites\n   - OpenAI (analyzer + orchestrator, shared breaker), MinIO (both uploads),\n     Resend, Stripe (x4), YouTube (x3). All surface in /health.\n\nReview fixes folded in: analyzer returns non-empty messages (avoids\n_run_advice_graph result[\"messages\"][-1] IndexError); batch upload appends its\nresult dict and corrects counters before `continue`; retriever test re-raises\nHTTPException before the generic handler; entrypoint sentinel ordering pinned.\n\nTests: tests/test_exceptions.py (hierarchy, raises, wrappers, retriever_agent\ndegradation, endpoint 503/500).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqgMCgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjywQADdx0y3LLNKpTKy1RsKfOtN7\ny48sTILpTMpRVzZ95/ABn8LAlaxjCcaQ5QWQ9L5VKsTK5V85Pq08+TviimZjOAq/\nJ8iRA4Mqw4I0SO0ijysaLZbnO/hPPPlAi6dHzTqz0W+uzjiUj8AjX0BXWGOm2YW5\nEvf3dZ/3rpp5CswCR7qiVJ2341Nbwh/+9cUg3scBfylBXVZvP4rGHiGVlZZWCkyk\n6KMsdHS/Q8W/TiyW47QjCDg7GerMRuoClZUl/85m8IjHYbZPPGHA/kyQnu1PVO0h\nAYjUBYrYQSsV/XFQ/PVJ0sez6SDCuPyzASVPeHvUwOXBMHi6bUxg2QnbhI8UA7P+\nQON7I/AUKqTKu1k/k9RoHNxccgdo5Aoegua/hhzVSyCX7NWjzRctZw/k6oHWxkrG\nszdpz0Wqpn/e5YKyLhIqVqa/91jnH6z8wGVX2FVbJ9i6w5HXlJzDD8TkVTL3XN6m\n+6n/L/2SYyT4fqkLLaA9c5BKv3QXf1PRHn+a/EQmK9afHwN8C1OZ57HOrc5CNsCf\na/FKVThG1wFPWOCOWf4Dc63FwbvSA5g/7cNZBPEzAPtqyI0NEleNmEl7s3YaJNwV\nOea7oOyaLL1RHjibzokfANueeg2z5LDamGo9GDger7KqtllrRAIPzAT5j0W+FNgv\nlkckaxp2My8uvqBxPmzO\n=joHr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-15T19:40:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/follo