esearcher appends live citations to sources list\n- _run_advice_graph returns dict (advice, sources, confidence)\n- OptimizedAdviceResponse gains Optional sources field (cache-safe)\n- generate_advice passes sources to response and conversation persistence\n- Security: os.path.basename strips paths from titles, scores clamped 0-1\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"81fd98caa9e065c27295d283e377b94cfe2ca1d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PhoenixWild29/APFA-Prod/git/trees/81fd98caa9e065c27295d283e377b94cfe2ca1d9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PhoenixWild29/APFA-Prod/git/commits/75c67ab7d9d612380ba6cd2c1751fdd89990e7dd","verification":{"payload":"tree 81fd98caa9e065c27295d283e377b94cfe2ca1d9\nparent 1765de15bb37f1e7dd038abed005309095578637\nauthor Samuel J Shamber <112887922+PhoenixWild29@users.noreply.github.com> 1781176574 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781176574 -0400\n\nfeat: wire RAG + Perplexity source attribution end-to-end (#308)\n\nSurface structured source metadata from FAISS retrieval and Perplexity\ncitations through the advisor pipeline to the API response and\nconversation persistence. The frontend SourceCards component, Source\ntype, and parseAdviceResponse already handle sources — this closes the\nbackend gap.\n\nChanges:\n- retrieve_context returns (str, float, list[dict]) with source metadata\n- AgentState gains sources field; retriever_agent populates it\n- perplexity_researcher appends live citations to sources list\n- _run_advice_graph returns dict (advice, sources, confidence)\n- OptimizedAdviceResponse gains Optional sources field (cache-safe)\n- generate_advice passes sources to response and conversation persistence\n- Security: os.path.basename strips paths from titles, scores clamped 0-1\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKpj+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGE0QAAP9r/86rf9izt0ArPiQotoD\nO5YC6