comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-27T14:24:11Z","email":"112887922+PhoenixWild29@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Samuel J Shamber"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-27T14:24:11Z","email":"112887922+PhoenixWild29@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Samuel J Shamber"},"message":"feat: reduce RAG chunk sizes from 400 to 128 tokens for retrieval precision\n\nOversized chunks (400 tokens / ~300 words) diluted LLM context with\nirrelevant text during financial Q&A retrieval. Reduces to 128 tokens\n(~75-100 words) with 20% overlap — the sweet spot for focused RAG\nretrieval. All chunk parameters are now configurable via Settings\n(env vars) instead of hardcoded in function signatures.\n\nChanges:\n- config.py: 5 new settings (chunk_target_tokens, chunk_overlap_pct,\n  chunk_transcript_window_sec/overlap_sec, chunk_spreadsheet_max_rows)\n- chunking.py: Updated all 4 strategy defaults (prose 128/0.20,\n  transcript 60s/10s, spreadsheet 20 rows), chunk_text() router\n  accepts configurable params\n- All 4 callers wired to settings: google_drive.py, youtube.py,\n  perplexity_connector.py, tasks.py (process_document)\n- POST /admin/rechunk endpoint: allowlist-based purge of connector\n  chunks (google_drive, youtube, perplexity_research) — preserves\n  seed data, manual uploads, and FAISS metadata. Sets Redis lock\n  to pause auto-rebuild during rechunk sequence.\n- force_full param added to Google Drive sync task and API endpoint\n  for forced re-ingestion after chunk purge\n- FAISS auto-rebuild respects faiss:rechunk_in_progress lock,\n  explicit rebuild clears it\n- Unit tests for all 4 chunking strategies at new defaults\n\nCoWork review: B1 (allowlist predicate), B2 (FAISS rebuild lock),\nB3 (force_full for GDrive), S1 (configurable for eval A/B testing),\nS2 (manual trigger) — all addressed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7da2ac36cc4a686fe52b1ada3259b33c8042288f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PhoenixWild29/APFA-Prod/git/trees/7da2ac36cc4a686fe52b1ada3259b33c8042288f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PhoenixWild29/APFA-Prod/git/commits/adf7e62f61d9fb1fe489a7b0c3760664aa2529ad","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/112887922?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhoenixWild29/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhoenixWild29/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhoenixWild29/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhoenixWild29/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PhoenixWild29","id":112887922,"login":"PhoenixWild29","node_id":"U_kgDOBrqIcg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhoenixWild29/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhoenixWild29/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhoenixWild29/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhoenixWild29/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhoenixWild29/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhoenixWild29","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/PhoenixWild29/APFA-Prod/commit/adf7e62f61d9fb1fe489a7b0c3760664aa2529ad","node_id":"C_kwDOP98E2doAKGFkZjdlNjJmNjFkOWZiMWZlNDg5YTdiMGMzNzYwNjY0YWEyNTI5YWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/PhoenixWild29/APFA-Prod/commit/1d3e87f96e0ade41ef36b815c9539815ace6a3dc","sha":"1d3e87f96e0ade41ef36b815c9539815ace6a3dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PhoenixWild29/APFA-Prod/commits/1d3e87f96e0ade41ef36b815c9539815ace6a3dc"}],"sha":"adf7e62f61d9fb1fe489a7b0c3760664aa2529ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PhoenixWild29/APFA-Prod/commits/adf7e62f61d9fb1fe489a7b0c3760664aa2529ad"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/112887922?v=4","eve