"type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opensuperapp/opensuperapp/commit/a952034dd706b9243ce43f79010cdca9a07554d5","node_id":"C_kwDOP_DE69oAKGE5NTIwMzRkZDcwNmI5MjQzY2U0M2Y3OTAxMGNkY2E5YTA3NTU0ZDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opensuperapp/opensuperapp/commit/3224f11fb023d80320122d4ddb317f5ba9021295","sha":"3224f11fb023d80320122d4ddb317f5ba9021295","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opensuperapp/opensuperapp/commits/3224f11fb023d80320122d4ddb317f5ba9021295"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/opensuperapp/opensuperapp/commit/281f744c70c52966bcc95546c798f3e5c7f4f236","sha":"281f744c70c52966bcc95546c798f3e5c7f4f236","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opensuperapp/opensuperapp/commits/281f744c70c52966bcc95546c798f3e5c7f4f236"}],"sha":"a952034dd706b9243ce43f79010cdca9a07554d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opensuperapp/opensuperapp/commits/a952034dd706b9243ce43f79010cdca9a07554d5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46480892?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/v15a1/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/v15a1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/v15a1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/v15a1/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/v15a1","id":46480892,"login":"v15a1","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NDgwODky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/v15a1/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/v15a1/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/v15a1/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/v15a1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/v15a1/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/v15a1","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opensuperapp/opensuperapp/commits/281f744c70c52966bcc95546c798f3e5c7f4f236/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T07:28:39Z","email":"visalrajapakse@gmail.com","name":"v15a1"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T08:39:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Add business card data model, vCard encoder and token claims\n\nIntroduces the data layer behind the digital business card, with no UI\nand no wiring into a screen yet.\n\n- `utils/vcard.ts` builds an RFC 2426 vCard. Escaping runs backslash,\n  semicolon, comma, then newlines, in that order, so later escapes do not\n  re-escape earlier ones. Absent optional fields are omitted rather than\n  emitted empty, which is what keeps a mobile number off a card that has\n  none.\n- `utils/businessCard.ts` merges the directory `/user-info` response with\n  the access token claims, directory first and the claim filling gaps,\n  since `jobtitle`, `phone_number` and `profile` are only in the token.\n- `utils/tokenClaims.ts` and `hooks/useTokenClaims.ts` decode and merge\n  claims field by field across the access and ID tokens, because Asgardeo\n  places a given claim in whichever token the OIDC app config names and\n  that differs per app.\n\nThe vCard encoder is specified by `utils/__tests__/vcard_cases.json`, a\nfixture shared with the wallet pass service''s Go encoder so the QR on a\npass and the QR in the app scan to the same contact. Expected values are\nhand-derived from the RFC, never regenerated from an implementation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c84a67d19291beb1493c391c6b5e82cd0277c8c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opensuperapp/opensuperapp/git/trees/c84a67d19291beb1493c391c6b5e82cd0277c8c4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opensuperapp/opensuperapp/git/commits/281f744c70c52966bcc95546c798f3e5c7f4f236","verification":{"payload":"tree c84a67d19291beb1493c391c6b5e82cd0277c8c4\nparent 3224f11fb023d80320122d4ddb317f5ba9021295\nauthor v15a1 <visalrajapakse@gmail.com> 1787642919 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787647171 +0530\n\nAdd business card data model, vCard encoder and token claims\n\nIntroduces the data layer behind the digital business card, with no UI\nand no wiring into a screen yet.\n\n- `utils/vcard.ts` builds an RFC 2426 vCard. Escaping runs backslash,\n  semicolon, comma, then newlines, in that order, so later escapes do not\n  re-escape earlier ones. Absent optional fields are omitted rather than\n  emitted empty, which is what keeps a mobile number off a card that has\n  none.\n- `utils/businessCard.ts` merges the directory `/user-info` response with\n  the access token claims, directory first and the claim filling gaps,\n  since `jobtitle`, `phone_number` and `profile` are only in the token.\n- `utils/tokenClaims.ts` and `hooks/useTokenClaims.ts` decode and merge\n  claims field by field across the access and ID tokens, because Asgardeo\n  places a given claim in whichever token the OIDC app config names and\n  that differs per app.\n\nThe vCard encoder is specified by `utils/__tests__/vcard_cases.json`, a\nfixture shared with the wallet pass service''s Go encoder so the QR on a\npass and the QR in the app scan to the same contact. Expected values are\nhand-derived from the RFC, never regenerated from an implementation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjVTDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZSoQAB0wQ4C8RluU4C1JXCh/VDra\nmf1B3kOkIVO6/gQnAESrkVaS+dlgC7Rpm2hmPz+sjp2k6HhKL5CKjpLFcJADhFw+\nEFdl4VZ+fJPxOLY3ZSdP7YngxYXb5TDjRrZUvkdDC2b6leTiAP3GAqrGEoP1Obli\npOHZHz50TLAm7jotWbiWNDeJa0TQzTl1e3ck1fc1Vof2VRmCxeccOaemSv2/usT2\nm77hQZWqU4iYm6xx1OQy7JTGSkyFSm40/5+YkmwGN6Dho5XJhkOnRvxXC6lPWpg4\n+RbfjTVykGx5dxN5Aa8tE04DnCp8BE4Og6lcWABViQWA1RLjgsobBJf6hzpXhgjY\nl9j4QTZ2z2Xnv4GILKkAS1SupSK8zXaRFaxvQ4Lu847GVUH9F1Rd+CePE75//zZM\n7WRNVOREvp77G5vKK+Ln7TXndYyBsvWs1LKYT31P/7QT5XWRO5+3O8/bem9ihr38\nJ9urWC/o/Fxw0YNzcBsxfEifkdhG